(93084,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Amarr COSMOS / Combat',500012,16727,5,'Eliminate all the ennemies',''),
(93085,0,5,24285,1,0,'COSMOS Amarr COSMOS / Trade',500003,0,0,'Acquire 1x Corpum Commander Medallion (0.1 m³)',''),
(93086,0,1,24287,1,0,'COSMOS Amarr COSMOS / Courier',500003,0,0,'Transport 1x Zach''s Note (0.1 m³)',''),
(93087,0,3,17211,30,5,'COSMOS Amarr COSMOS / Encounter',500003,16727,5,'Transport 30x Sansha Diamond Tag (3{{m3','We have a policy here within the Amarr Empire that our more prominent members fly a suitable ship according to their status, both to give them an edge during combat and to uphold our image, especially within our borders. We have recently decided to extend this benefit to mercenaries or freelancers employed by us that have shown admirable bravery and skill in the field, or earned the right through countless hours of dedicated service to our corporations. As you undoubtedly already know I have been assigned the task of allocating these ships to their deserved owners. After looking at your record, we decided that you, <Character>, are worthy of such an honor. There is just one catch, since you aren''t an official member we need something in exchange for this gift. Cough up 30 x Sansha Diamond Tag and the Apocalypse Navy Issue Blueprint is yours. Dismissed.'),
(93088,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Amarr COSMOS / Encounter',500012,16727,5,'Retrieve Keron''s Head (10 m3)','What an outrage! The Emperor''s House requires the finest delicacies from around the region to be delivered to its local office for the royal lineage to feast upon. As their humble servents we are tasked with the timely delivery of Nidupadian Yorak Eggs from this system. Those blasted Blood Raiders have attacked our main processing plant in this system, we believe that there are still some Blood Raider pirates in the vacinity of the plant lead by a skilled mercenary called ''Keron Vandafelt'' who is looking for left over Eggs and killing incomming vessels unaware of the recent attack. These pirates must be eliminated once and for all. I am sending you the co-ordinates to the attack site now. I want Keron''s head on my desk before the end of the day!'),
(93089,0,1,23863,100,0,'COSMOS Amarr COSMOS / Courier',500003,0,0,'Transport 100x Nidupadian Yorak Eggs (100 m3)','Although you managed to prevent more Eggs from falling into the hands of the Blood Raiders, we currently do not have enough supplies to cope with the royal household''s demands. Therefore i need you to collect me some more. I have already located a sufficient supply from a neighbouring constellation. Be quick we do not have much time before the Emperor''s Household runs out of their most valued delight.'),
(93090,0,3,12531,30,5,'COSMOS Amarr COSMOS / Security',500007,16727,5,'Bring 30 x Angel Crystal Tag (3.0 m³))','We have a policy here within the Ammatar Mandate that our more prominent members use certain implants to boost their mental ability, since it''s important that our people in key positions perform at a level above what''s considered normal for a human being. It''s a competitive world we live in, and sometimes one has to take risks to achieve one''s goals, even if it means meddling with the brain. You may not be a full-fledged member of Ammatar Fleet, but you''ve created such a name for yourself that we feel obliged to treat you as one of our own. And considering your record, we feel that our policy pertains to you as well. So I''ve been authorized to give you this implant in exchange for one simple task. Bring me a few insignias and the reward is yours.'),
(93091,0,3,12536,30,5,'COSMOS Amarr COSMOS / Security',500008,0,0,'Transport 30x Blood Crystal Tag (3 m³) to 0.9 Tori Aman''s Punisher in Agil.','We have a policy here within the Khanid Kingdom that our more prominent members use certain implants to boost their mental ability, since it''s important that our people in key positions perform at a level above what''s considered normal for a human being. It''s a competitive world we live in, and sometimes one has to take risks to achieve one''s goals, even if it means meddling with the brain. You may not be a full-fledged member of Royal Khanid Navy, but you''ve created such a name for yourself that we feel obliged to treat you as one of our own. And considering your record, we feel that our policy pertains to you as well. So I''ve been authorized to give you this implant in exchange for one simple task. Bring me a few insignias and the reward is yours.'),
(93092,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Amarr COSMOS / Courier',500003,0,0,'Deliver 5 x Training Certification Results (5.0 m3)','Ahem. I''m really sorry if I insulted you, <Pilot>, but there''s nothing I can do about this. I was given the order to test EVERYONE before we send them out into the fray, and if I would ignore that order I risk being demoted. I hope you understand. Minas is very strict about us following his orders. Now you''ll find the details of your test assignment in the briefing which I''m about to load into your NeoCom. Complete the assignment. which I''m sure you''ll do in no time. and I''ll send you off to the general. And don''t forget to read the advice I''ve uploaded into your journal. Good luck.'),
(93093,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Amarr COSMOS / Courier',500003,0,0,'Deliver 5 x Training Certification Results (5.0 m3)','Ahem. I''m really sorry if I insulted you, <Pilot>, but there''s nothing I can do about this. I was given the order to test EVERYONE before we send them out into the fray, and if I would ignore that order I risk being demoted. I hope you understand. Minas is very strict about us following his orders. Now you''ll find the details of your test assignment in the briefing which I''m about to load into your NeoCom. Complete the assignment. which I''m sure you''ll do in no time. and I''ll send you off to the general. And don''t forget to read the advice I''ve uploaded into your journal. Good luck.'),
(93094,0,1,22847,20,0,'COSMOS Amarr COSMOS / Courier',500007,0,0,'Pick-up and deliver 20x Minmatar Civilians (100 m³)','With political relations between the Ammatar and the Minmatar Republic quickly deteriorating, things look dire for our citizens across the border. There are thousands of Nefantar inhabitants stuck in the Tartatven constellation, some who are working there on official business, others who simply settled there years ago. The Republic government refuses to let the majority of them leave their sovereign space and, in fact, has many under constant surveillance. We fear that their lives may be at risk should the Ammatar declare war on the Republic and invade Audesder. There''s already a huge buildup of military forces here in Kenobanala, and many fear that war is inevitable. So it''s my task to ensure the safe return of as many Nefantar to Ammatar space as possible. What I need you to do is deliver a group of Nefantar refugees from Aeddin II - Imperial Armaments Warehouse to Fort Kumar. I will then relocate them to one of our settlements in Joas. May God light your path.'),
(93095,0,1,22847,20,0,'COSMOS Amarr COSMOS / Courier',500007,0,0,'Pick-up and deliver 20x Minmatar Civilians (100 m³)','You have done well <pilot>. But our task is not finished. There are still thousands of Nefantars that need to be moved. If you have more time on your hands. I''d like you to make a few more runs to Aedald for me.'),
(93096,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Amarr COSMOS / Courier',500007,0,0,'Deliver 5 x Training Certification Results (5.0 m3)','Ahem. I''m really sorry if I insulted you, <Pilot>, but there''s nothing I can do about this. I was given the order to test EVERYONE before we send them out into the fray, and if I would ignore that order I risk being demoted. I hope you understand. Minas is very strict about us following his orders. Now you''ll find the details of your test assignment in the briefing which I''m about to load into your NeoCom. Complete the assignment. which I''m sure you''ll do in no time. and I''ll send you off to the general. And don''t forget to read the advice I''ve uploaded into your journal. Good luck.'),
(93097,0,1,22705,1,0,'COSMOS Amarr COSMOS / Courier',500003,0,0,'Acquire 1x Minas''s Voucher (1 m³)','Bring me a voucher from one of the recruiters nearby and you''re in.'),
(93098,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Amarr COSMOS / Encounter',500004,11076,5,'Destroy the Gallente spy drones and then report back to General Minas','Your first assignment is to intercept a group of spy drones that the Gallente have deployed in Kenobanala. They are guarded by a few Federation Navy cruisers and an interceptor. They probably haven''t figured out that we have them on our radar, so they won''t be expecting you. With the element of surprise on your side, this should be an easy job.'),
(93099,0,3,22707,1,5,'COSMOS Amarr COSMOS / Encounter',500002,17138,5,'Find 1 x Oggiin Kalda''s DNA (0.1 m³)','Our intelligence agency has informed us of an Ammatar traitor in our midst. Apparently he''s been collaborating with the Minmatar Republic, supplying them with information and even hiring mercenaries to sabotage our operation here. I want you to locate him and take him out. Our last reports indicate that he is most likely hiding near one of the moons within Kenobanala. You will need a probe launcher to pinpoint his location. Once the job is done, return to me with something from his ship and I''ll give you your reward. Dismissed.'),
(93100,0,1,22708,1,0,'COSMOS Amarr COSMOS / Courier',500003,0,0,'Transport 1 x Amarrian Spy (1.0 m³) to Aedald VIII - Moon 5 - Republic Military School ({{ColorSecurityRating','It''s time to send you into the front lines, <Pilot>. Yes that means flying into Audesder. It will be dangerous, there''s no doubt about that. But I''m sure you''re prepared for those kind of risks, considering you signed up for this job in the first place. Your first task in Audesder is in fact to fly through Audesder, to Aedald. Our intelligence agency wants to place a spy inside their base, to gather intel on their defensive positions, plans and such. It''s too risky sending him straight into the Alliance Barracks, so we''re going to start with dropping him off at one of their stations in Aedald, where he''ll hitch a ride on one of their ships heading to the barracks in Audesder. That''s all you need to know for now, <Pilot>. Drop him off at Aedald VIII - Moon 5 - Republic Military School, then hurry back here. Try not to be seen by the enemy, or you might compromise our agent''s mission. Good luck.'),
(93101,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Amarr COSMOS / Encounter',500004,11076,5,'Destroy the Gallente surveillance tower in Audesder then report back to General Minas.','This time I''d like you to do something a little more daring. The Gallente have set up a high-tech surveillance tower inside Audesder, which has allowed them to find every single one of our spy drones in the system, greatly hindering our intelligence gathering of their forces. It will take them a while to rebuild the tower after you demolish it, giving us time to gather some intel and possibly launch a sneak attack. I''ll give you the coordinates of the surveillance tower. All you have to do is fly over there and take it out. Good luck.'),
(93102,0,1,22708,1,0,'COSMOS Amarr COSMOS / Courier',500003,0,0,'Bring 1 x Amarrian Spy (1.0 m³) to Minas Iksan''s Control Tower in Kenobanala.','It''s time to retrieve the secret agent you delivered into Minmatar space earlier. He''s currently located inside their main base in Audesder, called ‘Alliance Barracks''. It''s filled with Gallente and Minmatar ships, and perhaps mercenaries like you as well. It will be extremely dangerous, <Pilot>. But if we don''t get this done quickly, not only will the intelligence operation we put weeks of effort in be for nothing, our agent will also most assuredly be executed. He will most likely be located inside one of the Minmatar bunkers. Get him out of there in one piece. Good luck.'),
(93103,0,3,22701,1,5,'COSMOS Amarr COSMOS / Encounter',500002,17138,5,'Find 1 x Minmatar Bluechip (0.1 m³)','This next mission will most likely be the hardest you''ve done so far. As you probably know by now, the Minmatar forces have set up a blockade at the main jump gate into Audesder, which they call the ''Minmatar Alliance Defense Brigade''. It''s located not far from the stargate itself, and they are equipped with a short-range surveillance tower enabling them to detect any movement of our forces through the gate at all times. Mercenaries like you can generally get past them unhindered, but any official Amarrian strike force sent through there would have to face them or be destroyed. To get to the point, I want to weaken the Minmatar position near the gate. The best way to do that is to take out their command post, it''s destruction will hopefully send them into a disarray, giving us a hefty advantage when we launch our sneak attack. Bring me the Command Post''s Bluechip as proof of your deed. Good luck.'),
(93104,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Amarr COSMOS / Encounter',500002,17138,5,'Destroy the Major Assembly Array and then report back to General Minas.','I hope you are, <Pilot>, I hope you are … As I mentioned before, this last mission is critical to our campaign. It will definitely test your mettle in battle, and I am certain that you will need backup to complete the assignment. Unfortunately I won''t be sending any of my own guys with you, that would most likely compromise the mission anyway, so I do hope you have some merc friends along for the ride. Your task is to commandeer a full scale assault on the Minmatar Dreadnought Manufacturing Facility in Audesder. It''s a massive installation, funded by ORE, the Gallente Federation, the Minmatar Republic and various other allies of theirs. It allows them to quickly build their dreadnought ships and deploy them immediately, with devastating effect on the battle field. If we take it out, it will seriously cripple their war effort, for some at least until they manage to build another one. This should give us the edge we need to attain victory. You have your orders, <Pilot>, now make us proud. May God be with you.'),
(93105,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Amarr COSMOS / Courier',500001,0,0,'Deliver 5 x Training Certification Results (5.0 m3)','Ahem. I''m really sorry if I insulted you, <Pilot>, but there''s nothing I can do about this. I was given the order to test EVERYONE before we send them out into the fray, and if I would ignore that order I risk being demoted. I hope you understand. Minas is very strict about us following his orders. Now you''ll find the details of your test assignment in the briefing which I''m about to load into your NeoCom. Complete the assignment. which I''m sure you''ll do in no time. and I''ll send you off to the general. And don''t forget to read the advice I''ve uploaded into your journal. Good luck.'),
(93106,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Amarr COSMOS / Courier',500008,0,0,'Deliver 5 x Training Certification Results (5.0 m3)','Ahem. I''m really sorry if I insulted you, <Pilot>, but there''s nothing I can do about this. I was given the order to test EVERYONE before we send them out into the fray, and if I would ignore that order I risk being demoted. I hope you understand. Minas is very strict about us following his orders. Now you''ll find the details of your test assignment in the briefing which I''m about to load into your NeoCom. Complete the assignment. which I''m sure you''ll do in no time. and I''ll send you off to the general. And don''t forget to read the advice I''ve uploaded into your journal. Good luck.'),
(93107,0,5,25277,20,0,'COSMOS Amarr COSMOS / Trade',0,0,0,'Trade 20x Lime Cytoserocin (200{{m3','I came here to investigate Constellation 9HXQ-G, which has been reported to contain massive gas clouds full of material used in booster manufacturing. There have been a lot of rumors about it within HZO Refinery, and I thought I''d take a look for myself. Unfortunately, the number of pirates here has me quite worried, so I dare not go looking for the clouds myself. Hence, I might have a job for you... However, I suggest you refrain from accepting my task unless you have access to a gas cloud harvester module. Without that, you will just be wasting my time. ---- A Brief Guide to Booster Manufacturing<br> Boosters are made by processing chemicals extracted from special gas clouds that can be found in certain deadspace areas in many regions. Some constellations, such as E-8CSQ, 09-4XW, 9HXQ-G, OK-FEM, Pegasus, Assilot, I-3ODK, and 760-9C, however, are rumored to have massive clouds of a scale not seen anywhere else. Finding these clouds requires the ability to conduct long-range scanning, for example via scan probes. Finding them is not always an easy task, though; it sometimes requires quite a bit of exploration. The downside of searching for these clouds is the fact that they are generally located in dangerous pirate-infested space. Few if any of these clouds exist in civilized space, having been depleted long ago by the mega-corporations. Hence, searching for them can be quite risky and is not recommended for any but the most experienced combat pilots. To extract the chemicals from the gas clouds, you need a gas cloud harvester module. You also need to find the correct type of gas cloud. Not all clouds have chemicals that the gas cloud harvester can extract, and therefore you might have to go through some trial and error at first before you get the hang of gas cloud harvesting. Today, most boosters are very much illegal in civilized space, due to the horrible side-effects experienced by users during the Great Booster Craze many decades ago. Manufacturing them must therefore be done in lawless space, outside the spheres of power of the major civilized factions. Similarly, anyone caught smuggling illegal boosters into civilized space can face very steep penalties. Manufacturing boosters can broken into a few phases. Phase 1 involves extracting the material from the gas cloud. Phase 2 requires a refinery structure with the appropriate service module to process the chemicals and create reactions. Phase 3 also requires a structure or station with the equipment for booster manufacturing to process the reaction and create the booster. This simple 3-step process will result in the creation of a fairly common booster. With additional work, the right blueprint, and a combination of several low-quality boosters, one can create higher-quality versions.'),
(93108,0,3,22793,20,5,'COSMOS Amarr COSMOS / Encounter',500003,16727,5,'Venture to the coordinates listed inside your journal and retrieve the stranded harvesters from the damaged prorator. Transport 20 x Amarr Corpse (20.0 m³) to {{ColorSecurityRating','I need someone to investigate a distress signal from an industrial registered to a group of harvesters in MY-W1V. I''d like you to fly them back here to safety, and we''ll fetch the industrial later. Sure, <Pilot>. Something up your alley just hit my desk this morning, in fact. I need someone to investigate a distress signal in MY-W1V. It was sent from an industrial registered to a group of harvesters that recently came to Fatimar Outpost from Amarr space. It''s probably just an engine failure or something, but I don''t have spare mechanics to deal with that problem just now. So I''d like you to fly them back here to safety, and we''ll fetch the industrial later.'),
(93109,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Amarr COSMOS / Encounter{{Verify',500003,16727,5,'','Deliver the bad news to the slain workers'' colleagues. They reside in a small outpost in a nearby system; I''ll upload the coordinates directly into your NeoCom. As usual, all you have to do is fly close to the outpost structure and the message should automatically be uploaded into their communications database.'),
(93110,0,5,25277,20,0,'COSMOS Amarr COSMOS / Trade',500003,0,0,'Trade 20x Lime Cytoserocin (200{{m3','I came here to investigate Constellation 9HXQ-G, which has been reported to contain massive gas clouds full of material used in booster manufacturing. There have been a lot of rumors about it within HZO Refinery, and I thought I''d take a look for myself. Unfortunately, the number of pirates here has me quite worried, so I dare not go looking for the clouds myself. Hence, I might have a job for you... However, I suggest you refrain from accepting my task unless you have access to a gas cloud harvester module. Without that, you will just be wasting my time. ---- A Brief Guide to Booster Manufacturing<br> Boosters are made by processing chemicals extracted from special gas clouds that can be found in certain deadspace areas in many regions. Some constellations, such as E-8CSQ, 09-4XW, 9HXQ-G, OK-FEM, Pegasus, Assilot, I-3ODK, and 760-9C, however, are rumored to have massive clouds of a scale not seen anywhere else. Finding these clouds requires the ability to conduct long-range scanning, for example via scan probes. Finding them is not always an easy task, though; it sometimes requires quite a bit of exploration. The downside of searching for these clouds is the fact that they are generally located in dangerous pirate-infested space. Few if any of these clouds exist in civilized space, having been depleted long ago by the mega-corporations. Hence, searching for them can be quite risky and is not recommended for any but the most experienced combat pilots. To extract the chemicals from the gas clouds, you need a gas cloud harvester module. You also need to find the correct type of gas cloud. Not all clouds have chemicals that the gas cloud harvester can extract, and therefore you might have to go through some trial and error at first before you get the hang of gas cloud harvesting. Today, most boosters are very much illegal in civilized space, due to the horrible side-effects experienced by users during the Great Booster Craze many decades ago. Manufacturing them must therefore be done in lawless space, outside the spheres of power of the major civilized factions. Similarly, anyone caught smuggling illegal boosters into civilized space can face very steep penalties. Manufacturing boosters can broken into a few phases. Phase 1 involves extracting the material from the gas cloud. Phase 2 requires a refinery structure with the appropriate service module to process the chemicals and create reactions. Phase 3 also requires a structure or station with the equipment for booster manufacturing to process the reaction and create the booster. This simple 3-step process will result in the creation of a fairly common booster. With additional work, the right blueprint, and a combination of several low-quality boosters, one can create higher-quality versions.'),
(93111,0,5,25277,20,0,'COSMOS Amarr COSMOS / Trade',500003,0,0,'Trade 20x Lime Cytoserocin (200{{m3','I came here to investigate Constellation 9HXQ-G, which has been reported to contain massive gas clouds full of material used in booster manufacturing. There have been a lot of rumors about it within HZO Refinery, and I thought I''d take a look for myself. Unfortunately, the number of pirates here has me quite worried, so I dare not go looking for the clouds myself. Hence, I might have a job for you... However, I suggest you refrain from accepting my task unless you have access to a gas cloud harvester module. Without that, you will just be wasting my time. ---- A Brief Guide to Booster Manufacturing<br> Boosters are made by processing chemicals extracted from special gas clouds that can be found in certain deadspace areas in many regions. Some constellations, such as E-8CSQ, 09-4XW, 9HXQ-G, OK-FEM, Pegasus, Assilot, I-3ODK, and 760-9C, however, are rumored to have massive clouds of a scale not seen anywhere else. Finding these clouds requires the ability to conduct long-range scanning, for example via scan probes. Finding them is not always an easy task, though; it sometimes requires quite a bit of exploration. The downside of searching for these clouds is the fact that they are generally located in dangerous pirate-infested space. Few if any of these clouds exist in civilized space, having been depleted long ago by the mega-corporations. Hence, searching for them can be quite risky and is not recommended for any but the most experienced combat pilots. To extract the chemicals from the gas clouds, you need a gas cloud harvester module. You also need to find the correct type of gas cloud. Not all clouds have chemicals that the gas cloud harvester can extract, and therefore you might have to go through some trial and error at first before you get the hang of gas cloud harvesting. Today, most boosters are very much illegal in civilized space, due to the horrible side-effects experienced by users during the Great Booster Craze many decades ago. Manufacturing them must therefore be done in lawless space, outside the spheres of power of the major civilized factions. Similarly, anyone caught smuggling illegal boosters into civilized space can face very steep penalties. Manufacturing boosters can broken into a few phases. Phase 1 involves extracting the material from the gas cloud. Phase 2 requires a refinery structure with the appropriate service module to process the chemicals and create reactions. Phase 3 also requires a structure or station with the equipment for booster manufacturing to process the reaction and create the booster. This simple 3-step process will result in the creation of a fairly common booster. With additional work, the right blueprint, and a combination of several low-quality boosters, one can create higher-quality versions.'),
(93112,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Amarr COSMOS / Security',500019,26249,5,'Destroy all of the Sansha ships guarding their outpost, then report back to General Zulandor.','As you may or may not know, we are on a secret mission on behalf of the Imperial Navy, to capture an infamous Sansha infidel who resides on HY-RWO III. We haven''t found him yet, but we''ve had a most unfortunate encounter with a fleet of Sansha warships guarding one of their supply outposts nearby. The locals must have alerted them to our presence. I would rather not risk my men in a direct confrontation, I''ve already lost too many ships on our trip here and I need all the manpower I currently have to keep the search going, incase we encounter more of those blasted zombies. I''ll supply you with a bookmark to the entrance of their supply depot. It''s located within a deadspace pocket, so you''ll have to make due without your micro-warpdrive. I also suggest you bring friends along for the ride, their outpost is heavily guarded with battleships and sentry guns. Good luck.'),
(93113,0,3,22801,10,5,'COSMOS Amarr COSMOS / Security',500019,26249,5,'Acquire 10 x Amarr Light Marines (20.0 m³)','I''ll start from the beginning. I joined Frolo''s crew many years ago, when I was a young lad, and served under him right up to his death. Those were some good times, and we made a fortune from harvesting gas clouds in this area and neighboring constellations. Dorim, Frolo''s second son, also served under his father and we became the best of friends. Now life here was simple, until Frolo died. He was a great man, a remarkable leader. The pioneers out here all looked up to him and followed the rules while he was around. But soon after his death that was about to change. A few months after Frolo passed away, his firstborn, Jamur Fatimar, arrived in Fatimar Outpost. He had lived all his life with his mother in Amarr space, far away from the grueling life we have here in no-man''s-land. Basically he was fed with a silver spoon his entire life, and that rubbed off on him. As soon as he arrived he claimed ownership of the Outpost. We decided to play along with his little game, as neither I nor Dorim had any real ambition to take on the leadership role. But people quickly started to despise him. He was much harsher than Frolo ever was, and was very detached from the local miners and harvesters here who Frolo used to work along-side. He was a strict, traditional Amarrian ruler who had zero tolerance for any difference of opinion from his own. He implemented a hefty tax which was largely used to pay for his extravagant lifestyle. Needless to say, things got hairy around here. Some of pioneers split away from Fatimar Outpost and founded their own colonies elsewhere, and there were rumors of a rebellion. When I saw everything that we had built virtually crumbling beneath us, I was forced to intervene. I claimed leadership over Fatimar Outpost. A power struggle ensued, which I eventually won. As you might expect, Jamur was not very fond of losing his title and decided to split away from us, forming his own colony elsewhere in MY-W1V. But I''ve always had the impression that he was out for revenge, and therefore I''ve had his little colony under surveillance for quite some time. And that''s what alerted me to an extremely worrying turn of events. Jamur had been in contact with someone from outside MY-W1V, who my sources tell me has promised to help him in ''his war with Fatimar Outpost''. I can''t imagine what a bitter, power hungry man like Jamur would do to reclaim his title. I want you to find out for me. I will upload the coordinates of the meeting point into your NeoCom, all you have to do is warp there and disrupt the meeting. Bring this ''agent'' to me for questioning.'),
(93114,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Amarr COSMOS / Security',500019,26249,5,'Lure Jamur Fatimar out of the battletower he is hiding in and kill him.','Yes, they coughed it up immediately. Apparently they aren''t very loyal to their former master. The leader of the group has been in close contact with Jamur and claims he''s gone mad. His hatred of me has clouded his judgment, and he''s done the unthinkable. The secret agent in your previous mission was in fact an agent of the Sansha''s Nation! Talk about striking a deal with the devil ... he''s gone way too far this time. The good news is that we can trace Jamur''s exact whereabouts. The bug I had implanted into his ship is still functional, and I can see his location on our scanner. I want you to find him immediately and take him out. Every minute that passes is crucial, he must not be allowed to reveal our location to the Sansha''s Nation. If that happens then all may be lost.'),
(93115,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Amarr COSMOS / Security',500002,17138,5,'Destroy the Minmatar miners, then report back to your agent. Location -0.1 MY-W1V (Low Sec Warning!)','I''m not just angry, I''m bloody furious! I was just minding my own business in an asteroid field in MY-W1V, when an extra group of miners show up. I ignore them and continue mining my roid. Then one of them jams me and threatens to blow my ship up if I don''t leave. Talk about being rude! And to top it off, they''re from a rival Minmatar mining colony in 9HXQ-G. What I need you to do first is warp to my asteroid field and take out the louts who stole it from me. When that''s done, we''ll take care of the pesky Minmatar mining colony.'),
(93116,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Amarr COSMOS / Security',500002,17138,5,'Destroy the Minmatar Mining Station, then report back to your agent. Location -0.3 AX-DOT (Low Sec Warning!)','Ok, now it''s time to finish the job we started. The expedition you faced in your last mission hails from a colony in AX-DOT, and they''ll probably not be happy when they find out what happened to their colleagues. I want you to completely obliterate their outpost and any ships nearby, that way I can safely venture back to the asteroid field without worrying about reprisal attacks. This will also rid Fatimar Outpost of a long standing competitor, so we''ll effectively be killing two flies in one blow. Good luck.'),
(93117,0,5,25277,20,0,'COSMOS Amarr COSMOS / Trade',500003,0,0,'Trade 20x Lime Cytoserocin (200{{m3','I came here to investigate Constellation 9HXQ-G, which has been reported to contain massive gas clouds full of material used in booster manufacturing. There have been a lot of rumors about it within HZO Refinery, and I thought I''d take a look for myself. Unfortunately, the number of pirates here has me quite worried, so I dare not go looking for the clouds myself. Hence, I might have a job for you... However, I suggest you refrain from accepting my task unless you have access to a gas cloud harvester module. Without that, you will just be wasting my time. ---- A Brief Guide to Booster Manufacturing<br> Boosters are made by processing chemicals extracted from special gas clouds that can be found in certain deadspace areas in many regions. Some constellations, such as E-8CSQ, 09-4XW, 9HXQ-G, OK-FEM, Pegasus, Assilot, I-3ODK, and 760-9C, however, are rumored to have massive clouds of a scale not seen anywhere else. Finding these clouds requires the ability to conduct long-range scanning, for example via scan probes. Finding them is not always an easy task, though; it sometimes requires quite a bit of exploration. The downside of searching for these clouds is the fact that they are generally located in dangerous pirate-infested space. Few if any of these clouds exist in civilized space, having been depleted long ago by the mega-corporations. Hence, searching for them can be quite risky and is not recommended for any but the most experienced combat pilots. To extract the chemicals from the gas clouds, you need a gas cloud harvester module. You also need to find the correct type of gas cloud. Not all clouds have chemicals that the gas cloud harvester can extract, and therefore you might have to go through some trial and error at first before you get the hang of gas cloud harvesting. Today, most boosters are very much illegal in civilized space, due to the horrible side-effects experienced by users during the Great Booster Craze many decades ago. Manufacturing them must therefore be done in lawless space, outside the spheres of power of the major civilized factions. Similarly, anyone caught smuggling illegal boosters into civilized space can face very steep penalties. Manufacturing boosters can broken into a few phases. Phase 1 involves extracting the material from the gas cloud. Phase 2 requires a refinery structure with the appropriate service module to process the chemicals and create reactions. Phase 3 also requires a structure or station with the equipment for booster manufacturing to process the reaction and create the booster. This simple 3-step process will result in the creation of a fairly common booster. With additional work, the right blueprint, and a combination of several low-quality boosters, one can create higher-quality versions.'),
(93118,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Amarr COSMOS / ?',500003,0,0,'','Yes I do. I''m the leader of a small gang of harvesters, and I''d like to hire you to clear a rogue drone infestation near a gas field we''ve been working on. They have been continually harassing us, and it''s come to a point where my gangmates have refused to venture back there. Armed escort would cost a fortune over a long period, so we believe the most cost effective approach is simply eradicating the threat all-together. Your first mission is to clear the area of rogue drones. Once that is done then report back to me immediately.'),
(93119,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Amarr COSMOS / ?',500003,0,0,'','Now it''s time to strike at the root of the problem, the Drone Hive. The drones are manufactured there, so as along as it''s around they will just keep coming. Destroy it and report to me for your reward.'),
(93120,0,5,25278,20,0,'COSMOS Angel COSMOS / Trade',500011,0,0,'Trade 20x Vermillion Cytoserocin (200 m3)',''),
(93121,0,3,26140,10,5,'COSMOS Angel COSMOS / Encounter',500011,17138,5,'Destroy Targets, loot 10 x Rogue Harvester (50{{m3','The concept of ''miner''s justice'' is new to some freelancers here. Have you heard of it? No? It''s rather simple, really. Space can be dangerous, and we at the Angel Cartel are charged with keeping the peace, ensuring that people don''t step out of line. We don''t have the luxury of courts and lawyers, nor the option to hold long and protracted trials, so justice tends to be meted out in swift, decisive doses. It''s quite a convenient arrangement for the most part, and the mining harvesters only need to defray the slight cost involved. Sadly, though, not everyone sees it this way. There are some who feel themselves to be beyond the reach of justice, and who apparently believe they won''t have to face the consequences of their rebellious actions. I''ve received word of a group of harvesters who have been misreporting their earnings and paying only a fraction of what they should, thus swindling the Cartel out of our rightly-earned tribute. Needless to say, this kind of behavior is absolutely unacceptable. You are to head out, destroy their equipment and ships along with anything else you find, but return the harvesting personnel to us intact. While normally I wouldn''t hesitate in demanding their bodies be splattered all over deep space, we need them alive to extract information about any other rogue operation.'),
(93122,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Angel COSMOS / Encounter',500011,17138,5,'Destroy targets in M-PGT0 ({{ColorSecurityRating','We''ve finished with the harvesters you brought in, and it turns out they weren''t just skimming the profits. There is a gas cloud there, a very valuable gas cloud, which they had discovered and were hoping to keep all for themselves. This isn''t some minor act of subterfuge, it''s outright betrayal! I cannot express how angry I am at this. Here we are, working day and night to ensure the safety of these people, and for very little pay, I might add, and this is how they treat us. Rest assured, we will make a memorable example of these traitors. Their bodies will be flayed open and their skin will flap in the wind like the bloodied flags of a failed uprising. As for the gas cloud, since you were the one who brought these miscreants to justice, you''re the only one I trust to inspect the cloud and verify whether it''s as valuable as they claimed. Head out there, give it a look, and tell me what you saw. I suppose it''s possible that the Minmatars will get a little cranky at the fact that you were responsible for the mutilation and death of their kind, but I''m sure they won''t do anything drastic about it. Still, I''d appreciate if you also made sure that the area was clear of enemies.'),
(93123,0,5,25278,20,0,'COSMOS Angel COSMOS / Trade',500011,0,0,'Trade 20x Vermillion Cytoserocin (200 m3)',''),
(93124,0,5,25278,20,0,'COSMOS Angel COSMOS / Trade',500011,0,0,'Trade 20x Vermillion Cytoserocin (200 m3)',''),
(93125,0,3,11742,1,5,'COSMOS Angel COSMOS / Encounter',500011,17138,5,'Destroy these targets. And acquire and deliver 1x The Damsel (0.1{{m3','This one is personal. I haven''t usually bothered too much about Sansha''s Nation; they''re here, and we''re going to kick them out eventually, but until now they haven''t been worth the effort. That''s all changed. They have taken my sister. Understand, this is one of very few people in the world who means anything to me. We grew up together, and since I was older by a few years, I was the protector. She isn''t too clever, dear Nokana, but she always meant well, and all the times I had to pull her out of trouble were paid for a thousand times over by the times she stood by me when no one else would. When I got this job as an Angel Cartel agent, she demanded that she be employed here as well so that she could keep an eye on me. It''s risky business sometimes, being an agent for the pirates, and Nokana wouldn''t let me do it alone. But now it''s all gone wrong. Nokana apparently heard of a group of Sansha''s who had it in for me, and went to try and negotiate with them. She''s wonderful, my sister, but she''s no diplomat, and they ended up kidnapping her. If my bosses find out about her meddling they''ll fire both of us, so I need you to go in, get her, and return her to me before anyone else finds out. I hear they''re keeping her in a slave pen, the barbarians!'),
(93126,0,1,11742,1,0,'COSMOS Angel COSMOS / Courier',500011,0,0,'Deliver 1x The Damsel (0.1{{m3','Now that Nokana is safe, I''ve decided it''s too much of a risk to let her stay here. Wanting to protect me is good and fine, and exactly what I''d expect from her, but she''s going to end up getting both of us into serious trouble, and if anything happened to her I would never forgive myself. Not to mention that I''d have to tell our parents, and they''d have my hide. I would like you to take her back to my parents'' place in Cartel space. I know this is a little outside the realm of your usual work, to be escorting someone home like a chaperon, but I''d really appreciate it. You did a good job in bringing Nokana back, and I''m sure you''re as eager as I am to ensure that she doesn''t cost us any more time and effort. I''ll arrange matters here, talk to her superiors and give them some reasonable explanation. A friend of mine will meet Nokana at the landing point, so once you''ve docked safe and sound, let me know and we''ll take care of the rest. Just don''t let her convince you to turn around or do anything silly. Head straight home with her. And for heaven''s sake, don''t tell her anything about this conversation. I''ll take care of that as well.'),
(93127,0,5,25278,20,0,'COSMOS Angel COSMOS / Trade',500011,0,0,'Trade 20x Vermillion Cytoserocin (200 m3)',''),
(93128,0,3,25989,6,5,'COSMOS Angel COSMOS / Security',500022,16732,5,'Acquire 6 x Minecore Harvester (12.0 m³)','We had a team of people doing mining work for us in one of our harvester outposts. It''s a thankless and hazardous job, eons away from the safe mining you ship pilots get to engage in. The harvesting equipment they have to use is incredibly dangerous in untrained hands and requires both physical strength and endurance, particularly for the length of time these people have to work. I daren''t even think of the accidents that might have occurred had the Minecore harvesters not taken it on themselves to ease their working days a bit with some innocent entertainment. It breaks up the monotony somewhat, so that one''s focus on the mining laser won''t accidentally slip, leaving some poor soul plastered all over the nearby asteroids. The Minecore harvesters aren''t allowed to have any signals in their suits apart from the ones required to run their equipment. All they have is closed communication channels. So a few began telling jokes, and some of them shared stories from past work, and eventually it turned out that one or two of them, embarrassed though they were at first, could even carry a tune. There is now a core troupe of harvesters who have dedicated themselves to keeping up their coworkers'' spirits, maintaining a steady stream of radio talk all through the day. These are men whose only thoughts were how long it was until the end of their shift and how much they were going to drink when they got back to their quarters, and now for the first time they all have something to look forward to. Except that their workplace is now under siege by rogue drones, and the company apparently refuses to waste manpower rescuing ''expendable resources''. If these people die, the tradition dies with them, and the entire workforce slides back into old, ugly habits. I cannot let that happen, no matter what the company thinks. I want you to go in there and get them.'),
(93129,0,3,25988,5,5,'COSMOS Angel COSMOS / Security',500002,17138,5,'Acquire 5x Mining Equipment (6.0 m³)','Here is a mission suited for someone of your caliber. Thank you for your task. I know not everyone cares about company morale, but with these poor people, distraction and boredom can kill. I''m sure the whole mess will give them plenty to talk about when they feel up to returning to work. Unfortunately, we have a new problem. Not everyone feels so philanthropical toward their fellow man, even under circumstances where you''d think that people would stick together and help one another out. Now that you''ve cleared the last of the Minecore harvesters out of the area, the scavengers arrive. I have reason to believe that these rogue harvesters, unaffiliated with Minecore, have moved in and are proceeding to rob us of our equipment. These people undoubtedly intend to set up a business of their own, and plan to use our property as a starting point. The next step will certainly be attempts to headhunt our own employees, with extravagant offers of better working conditions, higher pay, more benefits and time off. Total and utter lies, all of it. Rogue operators pay even less, and if you desert the company to go work for them, you might as well have placed yourself in indentured servitude. I am not letting that happen to my people, especially now that they''ve built so much camaraderie and trust. I want you to return to the outpost, find these cowardly harvesters and destroy them, and retrieve our mining equipment. Declining a mission from a particular agent more than once every 4 hours may result in a loss of standing with that agent, except in the case of special missions that clearly state otherwise in their description.'),
(93130,0,5,15664,1,0,'COSMOS Angel COSMOS / ?',500011,0,0,'Bring 1x Republic Fleet Navy Commander Insignia (0.1{{m3','We have a policy here within the Angel Cartel that our more prominent members fly a suitable ship according to their status, both to give them an edge during combat and to uphold our image, especially within our borders. We have recently decided to extend this benefit to mercenaries or freelancers employed by us that have shown admirable bravery and skill in the field, or earned the right through countless hours of dedicated service to our corporations. As you undoubtedly already know I have been assigned the task of allocating these ships to their deserved owners. After looking at your record, we decided that you, <Pilot>, are worthy of such an honor. There is just one catch, since you aren''t an official member we need something in exchange for this gift. Cough up 1 x Republic Fleet Navy Commander Insignia and the Machariel Blueprint is yours. Dismissed'),
(93131,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Angel COSMOS / Encounter',500011,17138,5,'Destroy these targets. Acquire and deliver 3 Sansha Infiltrator Tag (0.3{{m3','You are talking to the last survivor of a vicious, dishonorable assault. I used to soar through this area with the rest of my gang, taking care of business, talking to people who needed a good talking to, maybe knocking them around a bit, keeping things tight and running. I loved my job, and I was good at it. But then we ran into a bunch of Sansha''s, and things went very wrong. They snuck up on us while we were minding our own business, and they murdered every single one of my gangmates. I still have nightmares about those last few seconds, when each one of my communication channels to them was filled with screams, then static. Then nothing at all. The Sansha''s left me alive only so that I could crawl back to home and tell the tale, a message that they were coming to push us out of the territory. We''re going to send them a message in return. We don''t dare risk total war, though, so we need a freelancer. You are going to head out, find a bunch of Sansha''s puppets, and kill them. Bring me back their tags so that I can hang them over my bed like a set of wind chimes; that ought to stop then nightmares for good.'),
(93132,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Angel COSMOS / Encounter',500011,17138,5,'Destroy these targets in DUU1-K ({{ColorSecurityRating','After you left, I got to thinking. Killing some random gang of Sansha''s is good, but it''s not enough. All we did was send the message that someone had wanted to kill their grunts. We need more. As luck would have it, the person reputed to be Sansha''s provincial leader in this area, a man named Abufyr Joek, is situated not far from us. If we take him out, along with all his staff and guards, we will be sending a clear message to those brainless drones. They won''t dare declare war on us, since they''ll have nothing to officially tie the attack to our forces, but they''ll know exactly who was responsible. Abufyr probably gave permission for his troops to roam around and viciously murder anyone they met, and even if he didn''t he''s still the nominal figurehead for them, so his death will be a statement. Kill everyone you see at that place, then bring me back Abufyr''s head, and we''ll show Sansha''s Nation what happens when you get the stupid, stupid idea to attack the Angel Cartel. Don''t worry about special storage, either, just put it in your cargo hold like everything else. We want it to be good and ripe before we vacuum-seal it to send off to the Sansha.'),
(93133,0,5,15663,1,0,'COSMOS Angel COSMOS / ?',500011,0,0,'Acquire and deliver 1 x Republic Fleet Raid Leader Insignia (0.1{{m3','We have a policy here within the Angel Cartel that our more prominent members fly a suitable ship according to their status, both to give them an edge during combat and to uphold our image, especially within our borders. We have recently decided to extend this benefit to mercenaries or freelancers employed by us that have shown admirable bravery and skill in the field, or earned the right through countless hours of dedicated service to our corporations. As you undoubtedly already know I have been assigned the task of allocating these ships to their deserved owners. After looking at your record, we decided that you, <Pilot>, are worthy of such an honor. There is just one catch, since you aren''t an official member we need something in exchange for this gift. Cough up 1 x Republic Fleet Raid Leader Insignia and the Cynabal Blueprint is yours. Dismissed'),
(93134,0,5,15662,1,0,'COSMOS Angel COSMOS / ?',500011,0,0,'Acquire an deliver 1x Republic Fleet Squad Leader Insignia (0.1{{m3','We have a policy here within the Angel Cartel that our more prominent members fly a suitable ship according to their status, both to give them an edge during combat and to uphold our image, especially within our borders. We have recently decided to extend this benefit to mercenaries or freelancers employed by us that have shown admirable bravery and skill in the field, or earned the right through countless hours of dedicated service to our corporations. As you undoubtedly already know I have been assigned the task of allocating these ships to their deserved owners. After looking at your record, we decided that you, <Pilot>, are worthy of such an honor. There is just one catch, since you aren''t an official member we need something in exchange for this gift. Cough up 1 x Republic Fleet Squad Leader Insignia and the Dramiel Blueprint is yours. Dismissed'),
(93135,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Angel COSMOS / Encounter',500011,17138,5,'Destroy these targets in TSG-N0 ({{ColorSecurityRating','As you may know, Minecore has been launching expeditions into BLC-X0 in order to find more gas cloud sites. We''ve been pretty successful so far, if I do say so myself. But success breeds the need for more success, and also breeds a certain type of man who expects that success. My superior, Akrada Ubje, is that type of man. Akrada is one of the few people in Minecore who can deal with the pirates on their own terms. The Angel Cartel have us in a stranglehold, but Akrada is so defiant of everything and everyone that the Angels respect him, and even if it''s the grudging respect a predator may show its prey, it''s one of the things that has kept them from completely devouring our operations here. Problem is, Akrada expects everyone else to be defiant, showing constant bravery and strength so that the pirates won''t think us weak. This means he occasionally demands too much, and the rest of us have to ensure he doesn''t push us into something dangerous. We''ve recently received word of quite a promising gas cloud. However, we have also heard that Sansha''s Nation plans to establish a base there, intending to beat us to the punch. They have put up a scanning sentry there which will call for backup the instant an enemy force approaches. I want you to destroy this sentry, and do it quickly. No matter what Akrada says, we cannot deal with this on our own.'),
(93136,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Angel COSMOS / Encounter',500011,17138,5,'Destroy these targets in TSG-N0 ({{ColorSecurityRating','Unfortunately, the Sansha''s Nation isn''t so easily deterred. They received backup right after you left, and have now set up a full base in the area. The place is crawling with Sansha''s pirates and we desperately need your services again. I can''t let this get to Akrada, since he''ll go berserk and demand we all fly in there, guns blazing. Anyone who refuses will find themselves out of a job at the very least, which in this part of space is tantamount to death by starvation. So we need this done on the quiet, like. No major forces, no big deal made, and no bragging afterwards. You simply head back out there, kill everything you see, then silently head back to me for debriefing. I should warn you that if you find yourself in trouble, no one will be able to help you, and I will not admit to knowing anything about your mishaps. All I wanted was to do my nice desk job in this company, pay my dues to Minecore and the Angel Cartel, and head back home at the end of the harvesting season. Flying out on suicide missions wasn''t part of the job description, and neither was having to hire freelance pilots to sneak around behind my boss''s back.'),
(93137,0,5,25278,20,0,'COSMOS Angel COSMOS / Trade',500011,0,0,'Trade 20x Vermillion Cytoserocin (200 m3)',''),
(93138,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Blood Raider COSMOS / Encounter',500012,16727,5,'Eliminate the renegade Blood Raider ships.','"I have a very dire situation on my hands at the moment. I have been the caretaker of a few dozen slaves for 5 years now, and recently the unthinkable happened. They managed to convert a few of our pod clones to their side, and together they have made an audacious get-away from the slave pens. Fortunately, we still have them on our radar, but we fear they might try to use one of the smuggler gates in CX8-6K to escape. Obviously, it will set a very bad precedent should they manage to successfully get away. We can''t have that. There''s enough rebelliousness and infighting as it is within our ranks. Although it pains me to say this, I require that you destroy all of the vessels carrying these rebels. They will be flying our ships, but will not hesitate to fire upon you - so feel free to extend the same courtesy. I will give you the precise coordinates of their whereabouts, of course."'),
(93139,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Blood Raider COSMOS / Encounter',500012,16727,5,'Acquire 1x Head in a Jar (1 m³).','"Unfortunately, we discovered a few stragglers who avoided the fate of those rebels you took care of in that last assignment. Worse, we think they''re about to make an attempt to reach an old abandoned stargate in CX8-6K. Their getting away would be a huge embarrassment, so I want you to get to that stargate first in order to foil their plans. There''s something that will work in your favor though: This particular stargate is a very old model, and it needs to be powered up for a while before it will work. Therefore you''ll have a few minutes to destroy the escapees before the stargate is completely powered up. Don''t bother to attack the stargate itself ? if you destroy it they''ll just warp away, and then who knows when we''ll have another chance to catch them. Oh, and bring me the head of their leader. I will present that to our people as a reminder of what happens to those who double-cross the Blood Raiders. This is an important mission, which will have significant impact on your faction standings."'),
(93140,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Blood Raider COSMOS / Encounter',500012,16727,5,'Retrieve Dalitat Dakpor''s Clone (5 m³)','I need someone to help me retrieve one of my clones. He''s stuck near the Pagera Manton, his ship pretty much destroyed by Kalorr''s gang when it accidentally ventured too close to the Pagera. We must act quickly, before Kalorr decides to make a meal out of the guy. I will give you a bookmark to the Pagera. But whatever you do, don''t venture too close to the holy site. Kalorr will not look too kindly upon that, and I have a feeling he''s not in the best of moods ... not ever.'),
(93141,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Blood Raider COSMOS / Encounter',500003,16727,5,'Take care of High Priest Heftah Nekmar, who resides within a massive amarr fortress.','I believe it''s time to turn our eyes towards the defilers, led by the vile High Priest Heftah Nekmar. He''s been a problem for years, and now he has the audacity to venture into our territory to attack our beliefs! He must be punished! An example must be set! And you shall be the deliverer of our wrath.'),
(93142,0,5,25276,20,0,'COSMOS Blood Raider COSMOS / Trade',500012,0,0,'Trade 20x Malachite Cytoserocin (200{{m3',''),
(93143,0,5,25276,20,0,'COSMOS Blood Raider COSMOS / Trade',500012,0,0,'Trade 20x Malachite Cytoserocin (200{{m3',''),
(93144,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Blood Raider COSMOS / Encounter',0,0,0,'Warp to the prison area. Retrieve the prisoners from the prison facility, then report back to Neyan Khahsel in Blood Reach.','I have just the job for someone like you. My underlings have rounded up hundreds of those pesky gas harvesters who keep flooding into OK-FEM. I want them all moved here to Blood Reach, where they''ll be used for various purposes *sly grin*. I''ll upload a bookmark to where my men are holding them, just retrieve them from the prison and bring them to me.'),
(93145,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Blood Raider COSMOS / Encounter',0,0,0,'Find and destroy Nevar Took.','Nevar''s gang needs to be taken care of. It''s comprised of mercenaries and militia under the command of the mercenary general Nevar Took, and they''ve been hounding us ever since we raided one of the harvester colonies under their protection. I want as many of them dead as possible, especially the leader. They probably won''t recover from a blow like that. I want you to venture to one of their hideouts which we''ve discovered. Hopefully you''ll find Nevar there, if not then simply dispatch as many of them as possible.'),
(93146,0,3,3804,20,5,'COSMOS Blood Raider COSMOS / Encounter',500022,16732,5,'Acquire 20x VIPs (60.0 m³)','Those blasted migrants are causing trouble again. Because of the abundance of gas clouds in OK-FEM, our space is just crawling with them. As a matter of fact, a large group of Khanid harvesters built an outpost right next to my hideout in M0O-JG! I spent years building that place, and now they want to keep me out of my own home. I can''t even go back without being shot at. It''s just not right I tell you. What I need you to do is find their outpost and blow it to bits. That should nudge them away, but it''s not going to be easy. They locked and booby-trapped the acceleration gate leading into the deadspace pocket containing their base, so we have to find the key somehow. I know where they normally work, which is near a collection of massive gas clouds which they tend to harvest. I want you to ambush them there, and bring back captives for interrogation. Objective: Find your way to the Khanid outpost inside the gas fields, and destroy the ship carrying their highest ranking personnel. Bring back the VIPs to your agent for interrogation.'),
(93147,0,3,24441,30,5,'COSMOS Blood Raider COSMOS / Encounter',500008,0,0,'Acquire 30 x Civilians (150.0 m³)','The interrogation is going well. They coughed up the access codes to the acceleration gate immediately. They look like frightened animals in fact, so entertaining. We''ll have such fun together... But now to more important matters. I will upload the access codes into your ship''s mainframe, that should allow you to use the acceleration gate without problems. Once you have the bookmark, I expect you to warp out there and obliterate that base. And bring any stragglers to me, I so enjoy those sacrificial rituals. This is an important mission, which will have significant impact on your faction standings. Objective: Destroy the Khanid Innovation Depot and then report back to Pondah Shanjih at Blood Reach.'),
(93148,0,5,25276,20,0,'COSMOS Blood Raider COSMOS / Trade',500012,0,0,'Trade 20x Malachite Cytoserocin (200{{m3',''),
(93149,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Blood Raider COSMOS / Security',500003,16727,5,'Destroy the Amarr scouting party located near the asteroid field. Location: -0.8 YAW-7M. (Low Sec Warning!)','I''ve been looking for someone of your talents. It has come to our attention that an armada of Amarr crusaders has arrived in OK-FEM. According to our sources, their primary objective is to destroy the Pagera Manton, which they view as being a sacrilegious icon of the Blood Raider faith. They believe the Blood Raider organization is defiling the graveyard of their ancestors, and their aim is to ''give them rest''. These sorts of incursions are nothing new, but this time they mean business. I''ve never seen such a huge armada threaten our beloved holy site, and to top it off it''s being led by one of the Amarrian High Priests, Heftah Nekmar, which is of some concern to us. He has recently led a campaign of propaganda against the Blood Raider religion from inside the Amarrian territories, and the destruction of the Pagera Manton would certainly be viewed as a mighty victory by his people. Your job is to intercept a squadron of ships that have split off from the main armada. It''s probably a scouting party, and they''ve ventured awfully close to the Pagera''s resting place. You will be supplied with a bookmark, of course.'),
(93150,0,5,25276,20,0,'COSMOS Blood Raider COSMOS / Trade',500012,0,0,'Trade 20x Malachite Cytoserocin (200{{m3',''),
(93151,0,1,21602,1,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Distribution',500003,0,0,'Provide 1 x Jakon''s Head (0.1 m<sup>3</sup>)','Unbelievable. I never expected to get out of this hell-hole in one piece. I''ve been stuck here for the last few days, tortured day and night by Guristas scoundrels trying to find information I don''t have! It''s been a total nightmare so far ... However freeing me isn''t as easy as it sounds. And I won''t tell you how, until you prove to me that you''re telling the truth. For all I know, you could be a Guristas agent in disguise, looking for security breaches. To prove your worth, bring me Jakon''s head. Jakon Tooka is the Blood Raider criminal I was sent here to capture over a year ago. Banished from the Blood Raider territories and with me on his tail, he had no choice but to flee. After many months of searching for him, I finally discovered his scent here in Okkelen. I tracked him down to Otitoh, but that''s as far as I got. A Guristas fleet ambushed us, killing everyone save myself. Since then they have kept me here in this run-down prison facility, attempting to scrounge out any valuable information that I have. Once I have proof that Jakon is slain, I can return home with pride. I would rather spend my last hours in this stinking cell than fly back to the Emperor with my tail behind my legs. I will await your return anxiously, <Pilot>.'),
(93152,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Distribution',500003,0,0,'Provide Myrkai''s Data Chip (0.1 m<sup>3</sup>)','The reason I haven''t asked you to release me from this habitation module yet is simple, if I leave the prison structure I die. The Guristas commander, Myrkai, had a micro-sized explosive device implanted into my brain. It activates as soon as I leave the area, or if someone tampers with it. They didn''t say how powerful the explosion would be, but probably enough to destroy any ship I am in along with myself. Upon checking the data logs here in the prison after you opened my cell, I discovered a device which acts as a remote control for the bomb inside my skull, apparently it''s the only thing that can deactivate it. But I can''t access this device, it requires a data chip that only Myrkai has access to. I''m convinced Myrkai has it stored in the officer''s quarters near the prison, where he resides. If you could just find it for me, I''d be eternally grateful. You''ll find the officer''s quarters nearby, but I warn you, it''s equipped with a very high tech EM forcefield. It might take you a while to destroy it, and as soon as the guards at the lookout posts notice you firing on the structure they will attack.'),
(93153,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Distribution',500003,0,0,'Provide one Guristas Shuttle (500.0 m<sup>3</sup>)','Now that I''ve disabled the explosive device preventing me from leaving this place, it''s time to make my getaway. I managed to forge some documents, using the prison''s central computer, that should allow me to escape the Guristas installation unharmed, but they require that I fly a Guristas Shuttle. The documents say I am being moved to another installation in Okkelen, this should allow me to leave unharmed. Although I''m no expert on Caldari ships, I''ve had some basic training that should be adequate to fly those shuttles. I know you''re probably eager to bring me along in your own ship, <Pilot>, but I''d rather not risk your life needlessly, nor my own. This plan of mine is pretty much fool proof, as long as you can get the shuttle here in time. I don''t know how you managed to get in here before, but I''m sure you can do it again. You''ll find a Guristas shuttle in their supply depot within this complex, to get past the acceleration gate you''ll need a Guristas Crystal Tag. Once you''ve brought it here I''ll reward you generously.'),
(93154,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Courier',500001,0,0,'Transport 10 x Large Sealed Cargo Container (1,000 m3) from agent to a station in Ihakana','Good of you to stop by, <Pilot>! And you couldn''t have chosen a better time to show up ― I''ve got some things that need to be taken care of, and you seem like the perfect pilot for the job. It has been my goal for the past two decades to terraform this beautiful planet, Otomainen V, which we locals call Oshuron. Its temperature is extremely hostile to human life at present, but I believe its position in the solar system and its abundant supply of frozen H20 and CO2 makes it perfect for terraforming. I''ve even come to the conclusion that scientists residing in this once prosperous community here, in Rush Town, had plans to start the terraforming themselves, but never got around to it before the exodus. To start the process, I need to acquire a form of extremely simple microorganism that has the ability to survive the terrible conditions on the icy planet. I''ve located a number of hot springs far beneath the surface that are ideal for harvesting microorganisms, and I believe they will eventually cause a chain reaction on the planet that will lead to a thickening of the atmosphere and thence to global warming. Now, I´m sure you´re thinking, "Where do I fit into your marvelous scheme?" Well, all I need you to do is bring this stack of sealed containers, filled with old goods I scavenged from the ruins in the area, to an acquaintance of mine at Helkelen''s Blackbird in Otomainen. Once that task is complete, I will receive a passcard to a stash of viral agents that have been genetically modified to withstand extreme temperatures, which is exactly what I need to start the terraformation process. But enough of that. Finish your first task and then I will tell you what to do next. Just don''t lose the passcard!! Oh, and if you‘re on time, I might even give you some ISK for your troubles.'),
(93155,0,3,20510,400,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',0,0,0,'Acquire 400x Potent Viral Agent (200 m3)','Alright, now that we have the passcard, it''s time to get the goods. The viral agents that I need are located in a small secluded area near our moon, guarded by Mordu''s ships. The Legionnaires were hired by Tsuna Qayse, an obnoxiously wealthy Caldari State citizen who happens to be a major shareholder in the Nugoeihuvi Corporation. She hired the mercenaries to protect her assets, which include the viral agents you are to retrieve for me. My source within the Mordu''s Legion ― the same person who provided us with the passcard ― tells me Qayse intends to sell the viral agents on the black market. Unfortunately I don''t have the kind of money she''s asking for, but that''s where you come in. I want you to fly to her compound in Otomainen and retrieve the stash. You might encounter some resistance from Mordu''s guards within the complex, but just try avoiding any direct confrontation. The viral agents are located in a secure location within a high-tech science laboratory in the first area of the complex. The passcard will get you through the acceleration gate. When you find the science labs, destroy them and retrieve the viral agents. They won''t be harmed in the explosion, as they are protected by a safety evacuation system, according to my source. Find the ejected container after the labs have been obliterated, and grab them. Bring them back to me immediately, and just ignore the Legionnaires who may attack you as you attempt to destroy the science labs. Sounds simple, doesn''t it!? You''ll be well rewarded for your efforts.'),
(93156,0,5,672,1,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'Acquire 1x Caldari Shuttle (500 m3)','Wonderful! However, now that I have the viral agents, I need a way to transport them down to the planet''s surface. I''d like a small ship, one that´s easy to fly and can maneuver handily in the harsh atmosphere of the planet. A shuttle will do nicely. I only know how to fly the Caldari one, so you''ll have to bring me that specific type. Don''t tarry, my life''s work depends on this!'),
(93157,0,5,20541,4,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'Acquire 4x Drill Parts (400 m3)','Alright, now that I have the shuttle, there''s just one more thing I need before I can get started. To infest the hot springs with these microorganisms, I will need to get to them through an enormous ice sheet. The only way to do that is to have an extremely powerful drill. And I know just the place to acquire one. Well, actually, four. Jorek Lephny is an old mining tycoon who has been operating in the asteroid belts and moon orbiting Otomainen V for quite some time. The old coot has a mining outpost equipped with a hoard of high-tech drilling equipment, among other things. These drills should do the trick for me, but I need at least four of them in case of breakage or malfunction, which is quite likely due to the scope of the task at hand. The only problem is this: Lephny is extremely paranoid, and we had a falling out of sorts a few years back when I, er, borrowed some of his minerals to construct my lab equipment. He has also had to deal with many pirate attacks through the years and, as a consequence, recently hired a seasoned mercenary veteran from the Mordu''s Legion to protect his assets. This mercenary operates a battleship, and he might pose some problems for you if Lephny refuses to hand over the drilling parts willingly. You will find Lephny''s mining outpost in a small asteroid belt near here. There is an acceleration gate close by, inside Rush Town, which will send you to it. Once there, use any means necessary to get those drilling parts! They are located inside the mining outpost itself. Good luck.'),
(93158,0,5,20548,1,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'Acquire 1x Ratei''s Insignia (0.1 m3)','I am now on the verge of starting my project, but there is one last hindrance to be eliminated. There is a suspicious-looking craft hovering by a lone rock formation near here. I''ve tried hailing it, but I get no response. The ship is registered to Ratei Jezzor, whom I have never seen before in these parts. I''m convinced he is an agent working for Caldari Customs, here to spy on us. I''d like you to take care of him for me, ―name‖. This task will be the last one I give you, I am sure, before I''m on my way into the great annals of history. Just make certain he doesn''t bother me when I make my descent to the planet. My life''s work depends upon it! When you finish this final job, you will have done me a great service that I can probably never repay in full. But I hope you''ll like my gift ― it''s an ultra-rare mineral that I scavenged from one of the ruins here in Rush Town. I have no use for it, but you might. I hope you know what I meant when I said, ―Take care of him‖…'),
(93159,0,1,21619,1,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Distribution',500011,0,0,'Deliver 1x Wiretap Plant (0.1{{m3','I''ve been hired by my Corp mate Krakan Rost for a certain job he''s planning. Go talk to him for details, if you haven''t already. Anyway, I need some help from you. I have here a wiretap device that I need to get into the local State and Region Bank station. The only problem is that I have a history with that particular branch of the bank and can''t enter it myself. I''ll pay you well for such a small job. Just take the plant I''ve hidden the wiretap in and place it anywhere in the bank. I will take it from there and tap into the surveillance mainframe.'),
(93160,0,1,21612,1,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Distribution',500011,0,0,'Deliver 1x Dynamite Crate (80{{m3','Thanks again for a job well done with the wiretap. It looks as if there''s someone attempting to set up a surveillance fence around the bank. That fence would make my job very difficult. Whoever is doing this is too clever by far, he''s using state of the art scanners called Barbed Wire Scanners that are very hard to tamper with. I managed to break into the cargo manifest at the State War Academy station in Ishisomo and discovered that a bunch of these scanners are sitting there waiting to be shipped out here. I have an accomplice on the station, but he doesn''t have the means to deal with them. I want to provide him with those means. Rost gave me a crate of dynamite he''s not using and I want you to smuggle it into the State War Academy station. My accomplice there will then use it to sabotage the scanners, making it all look like an accident of course. We have to move quickly before the scanners are shipped out, so I''m enticing you with a nice bonus reward if you get there within 20 minutes.'),
(93161,0,1,21620,1,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Distribution',500011,0,0,'Deliver 1x Assistant''s Keychain (0.1{{m3','Thanks again for a job well done with the wiretap. It looks as if there''s someone attempting to set up a surveillance fence around the bank. That fence would make my job very difficult. Whoever is doing this is too clever by far, he''s using state of the art scanners called Barbed Wire Scanners that are very hard to tamper with. I managed to break into the cargo manifest at the State War Academy station in Ishisomo and discovered that a bunch of these scanners are sitting there waiting to be shipped out here. I have an accomplice on the station, but he doesn''t have the means to deal with them. I want to provide him with those means. Rost gave me a crate of dynamite he''s not using and I want you to smuggle it into the State War Academy station. My accomplice there will then use it to sabotage the scanners, making it all look like an accident of course. We have to move quickly before the scanners are shipped out, so I''m enticing you with a nice bonus reward if you get there within 20 minutes.'),
(93162,0,3,21739,1,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500001,16796,5,'Provide 1x Shady Acres Deed (0.1 m3)','Are you settling here in the Shady Acres as well? No? Lucky for you. My regiment retired last year after decades with the Navy. Our retirement gift was a piece of land in the Shady Acres. I can see the wisdom in it from the State''s point of view; who are better suited to settle a bandit-infested territory than a group of Navy veterans? But that doesn''t mean I have to like it. I was hoping that after a lifelong service they would cut me a little slack in my final days. But if life in the Navy has taught me anything it is never to give up. I''m the first of my regiment to arrive here, the others will arrive in the next few weeks. I''m aiming to make this place a little friendlier for their arrival than it was for me. A few days after I arrived this guy came along claiming he was a representative for the Shady Acres development firm. He even had credentials to back up his claim and everything. In my naivety I lent him the deed to my land here. He took it and I haven''t seen him since. I''ve heard rumors that he''s hanging out in the old mining facility over in Friggi system. Along with a lot of other bandits, I understand. All I can tell you is that he was a member of the black mask gang, so concentrate your search on them. I''m stuck here guarding my possessions, this territory is much too dangerous for me to leave them alone for even an hour. I would be much obliged if you could get my deed back. So much so that I would be willing to give you some navy issue ammo for your trouble.'),
(93163,0,3,21464,1,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500010,16796,5,'Provide 1x Rifles (2 m3) to agent.','The bandits here in Ihakana aren''t too happy with all these Caldari settlers coming here. Who can blame them? This constellation has been their little playground for years and now suddenly the State is arriving in force, effectively putting the bandits in a straight jacket. But they''re planning something big, I can feel it in my bones. Call it an old warhorse''s instinct, if you will. I''ve pulled some strings with some friends in the Navy. One of them gave me the coordinates for a location favored by the local bandits for smuggling. And from another I got reliable news that a large shipment of armaments is due to be smuggled into the system. Even an old army idiot like me can put two and two together. The arms dealers are using the place as a rendezvous and if we could take them out in a lightning strike it will safe us all a lot of grief down the road. Now, be careful. These bandits are not taking any chances, so don''t expect them to be sitting in some indies waiting to be taken out. From past experience with these guys they''re probably using battleships as smuggling vessels. I''m giving you some top-notch torpedoes as a reward for this mission, that should be incentive enough for you to round up a posse and take these guys down.'),
(93164,0,3,21743,1,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500010,16796,5,'Destroy all guards and provide 1x Nakyo Fukoren (1.0 m3)','It seems these cursed bandits are more clever than I gave them credit for. They''ve become aware of my attempts to weaken them and are paying back in kind. Not since I was serving against the Anarchists way back when have I encountered such ruthlessness. My fiancé, Nakyo Fukoren, was making her way out here on my bequest. We''ve been looking forward to finally being able to settle down and start a family together. But she was ambushed on the way and kidnapped. She''s being held in a secret prison facility operated by the local bandits. I called in all the favors owed to me to get this information, but I don''t care. Nakyo is everything to me. I''m even willing to offer you all my life savings as a reward if you can get her back to me. And if you get her back to me within the hour I''ll even throw in a very rare BPC. The jail she''s being kept in is a high-security one, with stasis cells to make any break out attempts impossible. But those stasis cells are going to help us to set her free after all. They can withstand massive explosions, even the destruction of the jail itself. And that''s exactly what I want you to do. Once you''ve blown up the prison, the stasis field around the cells will quickly run out of its internal power batteries. Then you''ll be able to pick Nakyo up, but you''ll have to act quickly because she will be exposed in space once the stasis field goes down. Please hurry, <Pilot>, I could never forgive myself if something happened to her.'),
(93165,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500001,16796,5,'Provide 1 Pansya‘s Head (0.1 m3','Beautiful! I''m totally devastated, <Pilot>. Those filthy bandits ravished my beautiful Nakyo while she was in their hands. Now she is but a broken shell, always breaking down in sobs and flinching every time I try to touch her. It''s unbearable. I''m not usually a vengeful man, but these beasts went too far. I want you to be my avenging angel. Excuse me for sounding so melodramatic, it''s my grief talking. I know the name of the man that gave the orders for the kidnapping and mistreatment of my fiancé, one Sanku Pansya. He and his gang hang out in the contested mining facility over in Friggi system, I''m sure you know where to find it. I want that son of a gun dead. Bring me his head as proof that his evil doings have been avenged. You will receive a great reward for doing this, a blueprint copy I intended to pass down to my first born son. I fear he may never be conceived now.'),
(93166,0,3,21726,2,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500001,16796,5,'Acquire these goods: 2x Guristas Light Weapon Console (0,2{{m3','The Chief Executive Panel may have charged only a couple of the mega-corporations with the task of settling Okkelen, but that doesn''t mean the others have to sit idle by on the sidelines and watch Lai Dai and NOH hog all the glory. And all the riches, more importantly. Ishukone wants to keep a watchful eye on the goings on here. I''m one of several covert and not-so covert operators roaming the constellation gathering intelligence. Personally, I''m particularly interested in the spy station operated by the Guristas pirates over in Airmia. Why spend a lot of time and resources to do something that others are already doing? If you are proficient hacker and have all the right equipment, you could do much worse than snoop around there and collect some choice tidbits to sell to information peddlers such as myself.'),
(93167,0,5,12544,30,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'Provide 30 x Guristas Gold Tag (3{{m3','We have a policy here within the Caldari State that our more prominent members fly a suitable ship according to their status, both to give them an edge during combat and to uphold our image, especially within our borders. We have recently decided to extend this benefit to mercenaries or freelancers employed by us that have shown admirable bravery and skill in the field, or earned the right through countless hours of dedicated service to our corporations. As you undoubtedly already know I have been assigned the task of allocating these ships to their deserved owners. After looking at your record, we decided that you, <Pilot>, are worthy of such an honor. There is just one catch, since you aren''t an official member we need something in exchange for this gift. Cough up 30 x Guristas Gold Tag and the Caracal Navy Issue Blueprint is yours. I‘ll be expecting those tags soon. With your track record, I‘m sure I won‘t be disappointed.'),
(93168,0,5,3647,1,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'Transport 1x Holoreels (0.5 m3)','So you''re the cigar smokin'' traveler people have been talkin'' about in these parts, eh <Pilot>‖? I''ve got just the job for you, a lil risk involved but nothin'' someone with your abilities can''t handle. You see, there was a terrible, terrible crime committed here in Otitoh recently, in the Lai Dai station. A dastardly sexual predator by the name of Ryoke Aura raped a young woman, my wife to be exact, in her quarters while I was away on duty. The no-good sheriff in these parts hasn''t been able to track him down yet, and I think he''s even given up on the search. I can''t let this pass, my wife deserves better! I want to inform the media about this, maybe if they plaster the bastard''s face all across the region someone will notice him and contact the proper authorities. Bring this holoreel to Poinen IV - Moon 8 - Sukuuvestaa Corporation Factory, my friend in the media center there will make sure it''s shown on State television at least once in the next week. It depicts the suspect leaving my wife''s bedroom in a hurry, with his cloths all ruffled up like he had just put them on.'),
(93169,0,3,21064,1,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500001,16796,5,'Provide 1x Zvarin Karsha (1 m3)','It''s now time to take the law into our own hands, <Pilot>. Since the Sheriff is completely incompetent, we have no choice. I''ve done a little background research on Ryoke, and I''ve discovered that he has a close relative living near here, in Ihakana. If anyone knows Ryoke''s whereabouts, it would be this guy. He''s called Zvarin Karsha, and is a small time peddler dealing in foodstuffs and other goods. I heard he and his escort are currently located near the State and Region Bank in Ihakana. Go there and find him, then bring him alive to me. You will be well rewarded for your efforts.'),
(93170,0,3,21066,1,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500001,16796,5,'Provide 1x Ryoke Laika (1 m3)','I''ve managed to force Zvarin to cough up the location of his nephew, Ryoke. He admitted that Ryoke was actually a Guristas Pirate! I should have known it would turn out this way ... not only is this guy a rapist but he''s also a member of the most feared criminal organization in the Forge! Zvarin also gave me the location of his nephew. It took some ''convincing'' on my part, but eventually he gave in. Ryoke is apparently on duty in the Guristas Stronghold in Otomainen. They use the area as their main base of operations in this constellation. Bring me his head, on a plate if possible. Nyhaha!'),
(93171,0,5,21074,4,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'Provide 4 x Talocan Sketch Books (4 m3) to agent.','I''m working toward my doctorate in Archaeology from the Science and Trade Institute. I''m already done with my thesis, but before my advisory committee allows me to submit it, they''re demanding I get some more field experience. So they''ve sent me out here to collect some artifacts from the fabled dig sites here in Okkelen. I''ve been out here for some time trying to get into these areas, but to no avail. I''m simply outclassed. The main dig site is over in Otitoh, but the excavation there is heavily infested with rogue drones, so it''s very hard getting anything from there. I''ve heard rumors that something of interest might be found here in Otomainen, but I haven''t found anything substantial yet. But I have one good lead. I understand that the artifacts the infamous Kazka bandits have pillaged or looted throughout the constellation are stored in their headquarters over in Sakkikainen. If you''re willing to help, assuming you have some basic knowledge of archaeological practices, I think that Sakkikainen is the best bet for finding something of interest that is not too dangerous to collect. My committee is mainly interested in old manuscripts, so if you could find something of that nature, I would be willing to pay you good money for it.'),
(93172,0,5,21097,1,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'Acquire 1 x [[Goru''s Shuttle]] (500 m3)','You''re not part of the Kazka Bandits, are you <Pilot>? I''m warning you, I''m armed and dangerous ... I suggest you turn around and go your merry way before I send you back to Jakon in a bodybag. Well in that case stay as long as you want. But don''t bother going after Jakon, I don''t want anything to do with killing him, it would get me into even deeper trouble. All I want is to clear my name. You see I used to be a respectable Caldari State citizen, with an unfortunate habit of finding myself in the nearest casino whenever I am on vacation. It so happens that a few weeks ago, when I was spending the night in the Diamond Ace Den, I got caught up in a bet with someone I shouldn''t have. I was drunk at the time and not thinking straight, but excuses aside I lost the bet and didn''t have the cash available to pay for it. So you see I''m kind of in a ... erm ... tight spot at the moment. I''ve been hiding here ever since the incident in the Den. Nobody ever comes to these old ruins, so I''m pretty sure I''ll survive. But I''m terribly bored, this feels like a prison to me. So you must help me clear my name, it''s the only way I''ll be able to leave this place with my head intact. The man who won the bet against me is Jakon, an infamous Amarrian scumbag of the Blood Raider cult. He lives in Otitoh along with his Kazka Bandit friends. I wouldn''t approach him if I were you, rumor has it that he can kill a man simply by looking at him. I don''t know if it''s true or not, but just stay clear of him will you. Anyway, my first problem is that I lost my shuttle when I made my hasty escape from the Diamond Ace Den after I lost the bet. I had parked it outside but it was surrounded by Kazka goons, so I had to find another means of escape. The shuttle has some valuables on board, just some family photos and personal information, nothing a pirate would care for. Not to mention I received it as a birthday present from my father, and I definitely wouldn''t want him to find out about my current situation. Your first task is to retrieve this shuttle for me. Bring it here and I''ll reward you well. You''ll find it near one of the moons orbiting Otitoh VII, which is pretty close to the Diamond Ace Den. I tried going back after it myself just after I escaped, but I fled when I saw all the Kazka ships guarding it. I forget which moon it was, you''ll have to find it yourself, can''t be too hard though. Also, expect a number of cruisers as well as warp scramblers guarding it. You''ll probably need friends to help you out clearing the guards, as well as an industrial to transport the shuttle to me. Jakon probably expects me to show up sooner or later looking for my shuttle, so he''ll keep it there until he finds me.'),
(93173,0,1,26778,1,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Courier',500001,0,0,'Transport 1 x Crates of Holoreels (50 m3) from a station in Ihakana to the agent','To ease my suffering, I require my entertainment systems. I left them on Ihakana VI - State and Region Bank Depository before I set off to the Diamond Ace Den, and I''m sure Jakon has some friends of his snooping about the area incase I try to get back to my apartment there. You''ll have to be extra careful not to be spotted, I wouldn''t want them following you back here, that would be the end of me for sure.'),
(93174,0,5,15410,1,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'Provide 1 x Neophite (0.1 m3)','There''s just one final task I need you to complete. And that is to help me acquire the one item that will help me clear my name. I''m looking for a piece of neophite mineral, which is an extremely valuable mineral found in very remote areas of the galaxy. I am certain that Jakon will forget my bet in exchange for this priceless item. I''ve heard that you can find it somewhere in Okkelen, but I can''t be too sure. If you stumble upon it in your travels, then let me know. Don''t bother accepting this mission if you don''t have it or know how to acquire it, because I have no idea where to find this item.'),
(93175,0,5,15410,1,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'Provide 1x Neophite','I''m in kind of a tight spot at the moment, but I can''t reveal anything to you until I''m certain of your intentions. To prove yourself to me, bring me a piece of the extremely valuable mineral, neophite. You''ll get it back when I''m done with you, but I really need to have something that will keep you from double-crossing me before I can give you any of the details of my situation. I hear Akira Helkelen has a little neophite in stock; you might want to pay him a visit at the Rush Town Ruins if you don''t have any neophite yourself.'),
(93176,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500001,16796,5,'Provide 1 Sheriff Togany','Now that I have your attention, I''ll tell you my story. I am a prominent salesman sent to Otitoh on a special assignment from Expert Distribution. Well… I was. I was born and raised in New Caldari, and I wasn''t prepared for the harsh life of this run-down system. My first few months here were quite difficult, and I often thought about abandoning my work here and running back to my family. In my depressed and lonely state, I needed a companion: someone to ease the tension of everyday life here. My wife refused to leave our home in New Caldari, so I had no one. So, I was completely helpless when I stumbled upon a beautiful young woman who seemed to be caught up in the same situation that I was. There was no one around who gave a damn. I found her in a bar in the Lai Dai station in Otitoh. She actually started the conversation— considering how I was brought up, I''m not used to a woman taking the initiative in such matters. Anyway, next thing I knew, I was waking up the next morning in her bedroom with a terrible hangover. Before I had time to fully clothe myself, I discovered my mistake: the door to the apartment opened and a short, gnarled old man came in. As soon as I saw him, I knew I was in trouble. That man was Eteri Tazaki, an officer of the Lai Dai Protection Services. He was furious, but— fortunately for me—unarmed. He chased me out of the apartment, calling for the guards. I managed to escape into a nearby alley, and, with my heart about to explode, I ran as fast as I could to the hangar bay. I''ve been running ever since. The fact is, every law enforcement officer in this system seems to be corrupt, and by the virtue of his position alone, Tazaki has managed to convince the authorities that I raped his wife. I''m now a wanted man, hunted by those I once trusted with my life. I''m still trying to come to terms with what has happened, but it''s hard. I just hope my family doesn''t hear about this until I have time to explain everything in person. What I need from you, ―name‖, is help to escape this constellation. I can''t risk trying to make the jump out of here without adequate preparation; if I''m caught, I could end up in prison for the rest of my life. That''s something I want to avoid at all costs, especially in these parts. Your first task will be a difficult one. The sheriff of Otitoh, Togany, has been snooping around the area looking for me. I think he must have been tipped off by one of the locals, because he''s currently scouring the asteroid belts near here, where I usually run at the first sight of law enforcement officers. You must take him out— destroy his ship or whatever; just prevent him from finding me. I fear that if he''s not taken care of soon, I will be caught. If he catches me, he''ll call in back-up, and there''ll be no stopping them. He''s currently located near one of the moons of Otitoh VII. Bring me proof of his demise and you will be rewarded.'),
(93177,0,5,11370,1,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'Provide 1x Prototype Cloaking Device I (100 m3) to agent.','Now that you''ve neutralized the sheriff, it''s time to prepare my getaway ship. I will need a cloaking device to keep myself from being detected, just in case CONCORD or Customs have been notified about me. Being cloaked doesn''t make my plan foolproof, but it will increase my chance of escape significantly. You should be able to find a Prototype Cloaking Device on the market; I''d buy it myself if I wasn''t trying to lie low. If you don''t think you''ll be able to get ahold of one, don''t screw me around-- just don''t bother taking this job.'),
(93178,0,3,21091,1,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500001,16796,5,'Provide 1 x Bai''s Corpse (1 m3) to agent.','I''m almost ready to set off for the outer regions, where I can hide until my lawyer clears my name, but there''s one final obstacle. I was scanning the stargate to Ihakana from a great distance to avoid detection, when I noticed a few Caldari bandits led by Bai Tarziiki camping nearby. I remember seeing Bai''s face in a news bulletin a while back; he''s reputed to be a member of the Kazka Bandits, a notorious gang of outlaw mercenaries in these parts. They are also rumored to have close ties with the corrupt security forces in Otitoh, which Eteri is a part of. I''m not sure what Bai is up to, but I have a sinking feeling that he was sent by Eteri to block my exit. He probably knows that Ihakana is the first place I would go to. Outlaws like Bai are experts at sniffing out people in hiding, so there''s no doubt that he has an anti-cloaking device and multiple scanners on his ship. I can''t afford to take this kind of chance: if they catch me I''ll be tortured and killed. Your last task is simple. Take out Bai, and bring me proof that he won''t bother me anymore. His corpse will do.'),
(93179,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'','Well, it seems this will be your last assignment for me. My commanding officers have noticed your abilities and want to give you some tougher assignments. This is the first step to greatness, my friend. Don''t screw it up. These reports contain your employment and assignment history. Take them to Friggi VIII - Moon 20 - Nugoeihuvi Corporation Publisher for them to examine. If everything checks out alright, you can report back to me and I will tell you where to go next.'),
(93180,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'','Those weapons you delivered are being put to good use as we speak, Hirmis Pine. You did an excellent job; I''m beginning to see your qualities as a pilot. I can start giving you some worthwhile assignments now. We at Nugoeihuvi cannot allow any security liabilities; spies try to infiltrate our ranks every day, and because of that we have to be extremely careful of where we place our trust. If you wish to prove yourself to us further, then go to this location and destroy these targets. They pose a substantial security threat to our nearby operations, and that is something we cannot allow. Complete this and we can be sure you are not on their side.'),
(93181,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'','So, you''re interested in working for the Nugoeihuvi corporation, yes? This whole constellation is filled with riches, and I must admit, we could use some help in our quest to claim it all. Many large corporations have their eyes set on this place, but they won''t get there before we do. I have a few tasks for you. If you can complete them without messing anything up, perhaps we can begin to trust you. Firstly, I want you to take these weapons and deliver them to Ishisomo IV - Nugoeihuvi Corporation Development Studio. Our agents there are want to be well prepared should there be an uprising. The locals have been giving them some troubles lately and its time to show them who''s boss. Do you think you''re up for it?'),
(93182,0,5,20713,1,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'Deliver 1x Utrainen''s Employment Voucher (1 m3) to agent','Who are you? I sent a request to my colleague, Kochi Utrainen, to find some suitable mercenaries for hire to help us out on a few missions. If you are interested, I suggest you seek him out first. I won''t deal with anyone who hasn''t been approved by Kochi. Now leave me alone, please.'),
(93183,0,5,20715,1,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'Deliver 1 x Jorek Lephny (1 m3) to agent','Before you begin I''d like to explain a few things to you, ―name‖. I am Hitami Magye, of the Mercantile Club, which is a prominent corporation within the Caldari State. I came here with a little over 130 other settlers on a project put together by our Chief Operative, Anken Aronainen. Most of the others are miners or engineers, which are here to complete our building project in the area. We are building a small structure which is to serve as the Mercantile Club''s headquarters in Otomainen. It is to serve as the meeting place between various State officials of this solar system. More you need not know. The project has just started, but we''ve run into a few problems already. First of all, it was our intention to use the surrounding asteroid belts as a means to acquire minerals for maintaining our structures, as well as components for building extensions to them once we have imported the necessary equipment and facilities. The problem is this run-down craphole, which was supposed to be abandoned, apparently has some rather stingy inhabitants. One of them is a crazy old miner called ''Jorek Lephny'', who refuses any sort of deal with us to share the vast wealth of asteroids near here, which he claims as his own. His license ran out ages ago, so we decided to ignore him and mine the area anyway. That''s when we encountered his equally insane friend, Markus. Markus is ... or was ... part of Mordu''s Legion, and was hired by Lephny who has made quite a fortune since he started strip mining the area. Markus is on a contract for Lephny to protect his assets from random pirate assaults, which I take it he has to deal with on occasion. However, I didn''t expect him to attack law abiding citizens of the State ... but I was wrong. He destroyed our Badger and all our mining equipment on board, but allowed the miners to escape on the ejected capsule. This is of course a treasonous act, and should be dealt with appropriately. I requested military aid from my superiors, but for some reason they would rather I use hired freelance mercenaries to do the job. Something about the legal implications ... anyway here is where you come in. Use one of the stargates in Rush Town to get to the asteroid belt where Lephny is currently stationed at. Find Lephny, and bring him to me. I will make sure he is brought to a mental institution where he belongs. I don''t expect you to go up against Markus, he''s way too powerful. Once Lephny has been take care of, I''m sure Markus will leave.'),
(93184,0,1,20715,1,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Courier',500001,0,0,'Transport 1 x Jorek Lephny (1 m3) from agent to Otsela VI - Moon 13 - Ishukone Corporation Factory','While we wait for our interrogators to finish extracting the information we need from Zarkona, I''d like you to deliver some very important reports to my superiors on <station>. The last courier I sent to complete this task was ambushed and killed on the way there. These documents are very important; they contain reports of our activities here for the last few days, and I wouldn''t want them to fall into the wrong hands. So make sure you avoid any conflict if possible, and stay clear of pirate infested areas. Good luck.'),
(93185,0,5,482,5,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'Provide 5 x Miner II (25 m3)','Since our Badger was destroyed by Markus a while back, with most of our mining equipment on board, we need to find some new supplies. I have ordered a shipment already, but Prompt Delivery is taking it''s sweet time to deliver it here. In the meantime, I''d like you to acquire some Miner II''s for me, 5 to be exact. If you get them here in time, I''ll let you have one of our Co-Processors in exchange, plus a bonus payment should you be extra fast.'),
(93186,0,5,20479,40,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'Provide 40 x Outlaw Spur (4 m3)','We''ve been scouting the area''s near here and have come across an abundance of outlaws. These pirates are a bit strange for city slickers like me, they wear very old fashioned garments and carry spurs (on their boots) instead of insignias as an identification marker. And they seem even more bold than their compatriots deeper within Caldari space, attacking us without warning. A few of our ships have been destroyed, and it''s probably only a matter of time before they strike at our position here in Rush Town. The toughest of the lot that we''ve encountered so far seem to be the pirates carrying the ''outlaw'' spurs. They fly cruiser class ships, and are quire deadly. I can''t afford to hire you on a permanent basis, -name, so I''ll have to make due with clearing the area for us. You can find most of the outlaws hauled up near Otomainen II''s moon. I don''t care where you find them, just eliminate as many as you can. Bring back 40 of the outlaw spurs and I''ll reward you with an ancient treasure map we discovered in one of the ruins here. I haven''t been able to make heads or tails of the map, but someone with your experience might be able to make use of it. Good luck.'),
(93187,0,3,22494,1,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500022,16732,5,'Deliver 1 x Utrainen''s Reports (0.1 m3) to agent','The trial consists of 2 tests. The first test is rather simple. Mercantile Club has set up some practice grounds in Otomainen where our combat pilots train every day. Inside one of these practice grounds you''ll find a group of drones, similar to the rogue drones that keep harassing Caldari convoys in the outer constellations. If you manage to destroy all of these drones, you''ll find some reports that you must bring back to me. These reports contain nothing of importance, they are just part of the test. Once I have the reports, you will have passed the test. Just a word of warning though, I''ve already sent a few pilots on this test and none of them have returned. You might find the wreckage of their ships at the practice grounds, that is unless they fled before the drones managed to destroy them heh heh.'),
(93188,0,5,20478,5,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'Deliver 5 x Marauder Spur (0.5 m3) to agent','The final test that I need you to complete is a bit more complicated. One of the major pirate organizations in Okkelen are the Kazka Bandits. They are a constant thorn in our side, and the inadequate security forces here don''t seem to have the capacity to exterminate them. To get straight to the point, I would like you to destroy 5 of their lower-grade cruisers. Bring me the spurs from their pilot''s boots, that will be proof enough of your deed. Unlike your previous mission, I don''t know exactly where you''ll find them. I heard that one of their hideouts is located near one of Otomainen XI''s moons, but that''s all I know. Return to me once you have all 5 marauder spurs. I know this might seem like a pain in the rear-end, but I can''t give you that voucher unless I know that you''ve got the skills to track down the prey, sometimes that''s required in case we don''t have a bookmark to the exact location of your targets. If you can get this done then I''m sure you have what it takes to do any of our missions.'),
(93189,0,3,20477,20,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Security',500011,17138,5,'Acquire 20x Bandit Spur (2 m³).','What have we here? You look like a pilot not overburdened with morals or ethics. I like that. In fact, I might have a bit of work for someone like you. I''m planning something big, nothing you need to know about right now. Let''s say it''s just something to help me in my retirement. But before I let you in on my little plan, I must make sure you really are made of stern stuff. There''s a band of pirates hanging out in the Sakkikainen system that have been causing me all kinds of grief. They go by the name Kazka. Seems some of them have similar ideas as I and I don''t want some idiot to ruin my plan by jumping the gun. If you would go in there and bring a bit of devastation to them, it would take their minds off things they shouldn''t be thinking about. Do this and then we can start talking real business.'),
(93190,0,3,21612,1,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Security',500011,17138,5,'Transport 1x Dynamite Crate (80 m³) from 0.6 Liekuri VII - Moon 22 - Expert Distribution Warehouse to 0.5 Vahunomi.','"You''ve proven yourself to be a tough fighter, kid. I like your style. Now onto business. Maybe you have guessed it already, but the target is the local bank vault. Simply put, I''m gonna pick that place clean. And I want you to help me. Do well and you''ll get a healthy cut of the profit. That bank vault is ripe for the taking, but it''s actively bolstering its defenses as we speak, so we need to act fast. There''s a crate of dynamite I''ve procured sitting on a station not far from here. I want you to pick it up, I plan on using it to blast my way into the security vault in the bank. It''s a mundane task, I know. But I''m sure that if you keep your thoughts on all that gold that awaits us, you''ll be back in a jiffy." |collapsed=yes'),
(93191,0,3,21613,1,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Security',500011,17138,5,'Transport 1x Safe-Deposit Box Owner List (0.1 m³)from 0.6 Liekuri VII - Moon 1 - Caldari Funds Unlimited Depository to 0.5 Vahunomi','The planning for entering and leaving the bank is already well under way, but we''re still left with finding the best targets once we''re inside. I''ve been working on that while you''ve been away. I was getting rather frustrated in not finding anyone within the State and Region Bank that I could bribe. Then I got the bright idea of checking out some corporations associated with the bank. And wouldn''t you know. I found this cash-strapped guy with the Caldari Funds Unlimited. It''s an ideal match; he has all the information I need and I have all the money he craves. I''ve already made all the arrangements with him, but the information he''s giving us is too sensitive to send over the communication lines. I need someone to go and pick up that list and as you''re still wearing your courier boots you''re the best pilot for the job. To sweeten the deal a little I''ll give you some Paradise Cruise Missiles as a reward. You can occupy yourself on the way by thinking of all those you''ll want to blow up with them.'),
(93192,0,3,21614,1,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Security',500011,17138,5,'Transport 1x Plan to Crack Impregnable Safe (0.1 m³) from 0.7 Olo III - Moon 1 - Sukuuvestaa Corporation Warehouse to 0.5 Vahunomi','We have a bit of a situation here. While you were gone I received credible information that the bank we''re about to hit is planning to install a new safe in their vault. I''m afraid the TNT you got for me earlier isn''t enough to crack that baby open. We could hit the bank early, but the preparations are still not done, so I won''t risk it. And if we wait while I get better explosives it could be too late. So I took a big risk and put the word out in the underworld that I was looking for a solution. An hour ago I was contacted by this SuVee gal in a nearby constellation. A buddy of hers found a way to crack this new safe and she''s willing to sell us the secret. Time is of the essence, so I''ll go out on a limb and double your pay if you manage to bring it back to me within 15 minutes.'),
(93193,0,3,21615,1,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Security',500011,17138,5,'Acquire 1x Pakkori''s Hat (0.1 m³)','We''re in the final stages of our planning. I''m in the process of tying up loose ends at the moment. I''ve been digging up more stuff about our friend with the Caldari Funds Unlimited. The man, Uchi Pakkori, is a total sleazeball by the looks of it. I can''t trust him, he''s liable to try and sell what he knows to the police. I was going to take care of this myself, so I set up a meeting with him. But like the rat he is he smelled the ambush and fled. Now we have to take him out fast, before he comes out of his hiding hole and starts babbling. I''ve tracked down Pakkori''s hiding place. He''s locked himself up in and old warehouse over in Airmia system. He''s hired some thugs to protect him, so they have to be dealt with as well. Pakkori always wears an exceptionally ugly hat. With its wide brim I think he sees himself as some sort of a cowboy riding the steppes of Caldari Prime. I don''t know. But that hat is as good as DNA, because no one else is crazy enough to wear something as ugly as that. Go and blow up his hiding hole and bring me his hat. I don''t care if it has some burn marks on it, I''ll probably use it to wipe my arse anyway. You''ll be handsomly rewarded for this, but be careful. With the amount of money I paid Pakkori he could have hired a whole battalion to protect him. Not that I expect it from the cheap bastard, but you never know. This is an important mission, which will have significant impact on your faction standings."'),
(93194,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'','You see this? I''m flying a capsule! Those damn Nugoeihuvi don''t know who they''re dealing with here. If they think they can blow up my ship and get away with it, they are horribly mistaken. I''m going to build myself a new Merlin. If you could somehow find 2674 units of Isogen and bring it to me, you would have my gratitude.'),
(93195,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'','You see this? I''m flying a capsule! Those damn Nugoeihuvi don''t know who they''re dealing with here. If they think they can blow up my ship and get away with it, they are horribly mistaken. I''m going to build myself a new Merlin. If you could somehow find 2674 units of Isogen and bring it to me, you would have my gratitude.'),
(93196,0,1,22080,300,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Courier',500001,0,0,'Pick up and deliver 300x TX-890 Polytextile Fabric (300.0 m3)','For you, my friend, there''s always something. Since you''re a trusted operative of the State, I''m going to let you in on my current operation in the hope you can render me some assistance. I am, along with a few other agents, on an undercover mission to infiltrate some of the bandit gangs in this area, in an effort to get the Navy a better foothold in these blasted badlands. We need some supplies from the outlying areas, but we need to maintain complete secrecy. In fact, it''s best if we don''t show our faces anywhere, and thus we need inauspicious people such as yourself to gather some materials for us. First off, we''re creating a disguise to try and infiltrate the Roving Dodgers, a gang that''s been terrorizing some of the outposts in this constellation. We''re going to need some specialized polymer fabrics in order to create disguises that pass inspection, yet provide protection in the event that we''re discovered. I need you to head out to the Nugoeihuvi Development Studio in Sakkikainen and pick me up some TX-890 polymers. Nugoeihuvi manufactures them specially for that idiotic extreme reality show, and our insider has allowed us access to some of it. Head over there and bring me back some of it, and I''ll probably have another job for you.'),
(93197,0,1,2731,7,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Courier',500001,0,0,'Pick up and deliver 7x Crates of Silicon (350 m3)','I have just the thing you want. First off - thanks again for the polymers. They will come in very handy. Our technicians have most things they need to complete the disguise now, but one crucial thing is still missing. In order to create certain facial characteristics required for the impersonation of one of the people we''ll be, ahem, "replacing," we''re going to need some silicon from one of the Lai Dai factories in the constellation. Head out to Sakkikainen, get us that silicon, and we''ll be one step closer to our goal.'),
(93198,0,3,22083,1,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500001,16796,5,'Acquire 1 x Jerpam Hollek''s Head (0.1 m³)','We''ve just discovered that one of the operatives on our team was a double agent from the very gang we''re trying to infiltrate! Just before he decamped, we managed to plant a homing beacon on his ship. We can give you a bookmark to the location of the beacon. When you activate the bookmark, the beacon shoots out from his ship to prevent you colliding with him straight out of warp. He''s probably at a rendezvous point right now, waiting for someone to give the information to. Move quickly, or all our work here will be for nothing! I want his head. I will reward you handsomely if you complete this job in time for our mission to be salvaged.'),
(93199,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'','So glad of you to show up, Hirmis Pine. I''ve been on the lookout for a freelancer for some time now. We''re completely overloaded with work here, and there''s no end in sight. I am the project manager for the latest research project here in the Lai Dai research center, and we''ve employed dozens of miners to get us the minerals we need to complete our project but they haven''t been able to keep up with the load. I ordered some Veldspar ore this week, but haven''t managed to find any pilot yet who''s available for the run. It''s not far, you can pick up the shipment at Otitoh IV - Moon 1 - Lai Dai Corporation Factory. Bring it here to the research outpost, and I''ll reward you well. After you''re done I''ve got a couple more jobs for you.'),
(93200,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'','In your last assignment for me you brought back a load of veldspar ore which I had ordered for our project here in the Lai Dai research outpost. But unfortunately we also need some omber to finish our schedule for this week, and I have been unable to find any for reasonable prices in the vicinity. But we''ve become quite desperate now, so I''m willing to pay a very high price for what I need. Once you acquire the omber, return here and I''ll drop it off at our reprocessing facility.'),
(93201,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'','For your final task I need you to do a quick combat mission for me, Hirmis Pine. You might need some help for this task, depending on your battle experience. But first I''ll explain why we need this done. The reason the miners we employed to strip-mine the local asteroid fields haven''t been able to complete the job on time is not just because they''re a bunch of lazy sods. Because this system has been relatively unsettled for the past years, a number of rogue drone infestations have cropped up in outlying areas. From their hives in Okkelen they launch their attacks against any human presence they can find. It''s one of the reason''s my wife didn''t want me to take this job … maybe I should have listened to her after all. … The miners have been driven off on more than one occasion by these drone pests as well as Guristas and Kazka pirate gangs. This has sometimes led to casualties, which is very bad for morale and our productivity here. There is one particular asteroid belt near here which I have long wanted to strip-mine. It''s only infested with a few rogue drones, nothing a veteran combat pilot wouldn''t be able to handle. I want these drones eliminated completely, allowing my men to move in safely. Do this quickly so that we can get the job done before more of those things appear. Good luck.'),
(93202,0,3,20476,30,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500001,16796,5,'Acquire 30x Drifter Spur','The bank manager at the local State and Region vault has heard some worrying rumors that some thugs are planning a run on his bank. He is in no position to investigate the matter himself, so he sent for the cavalry. The Caldari Navy, that is. I was sent here by the Navy to check out the validity of these rumors. I haven''t dug up anything of interest yet, but just to be on the safe side I''d like to put some heat on the bandits roaming in the area. I''ve asked my buddy Jali Tanaka to help me out too, but he''s busy setting up a surveillance system, so I don''t want to take too much of his time. The Kazka bandits over in Sakkikainen seem like likely candidates for this sort of an operation. I don''t know for sure, but it doesn''t hurt to stirt things a little. You seem like a hardy pilot more than capable of roughing them up a bit. How about you get in there all guns blazing and bring me back, say, 30 drifter spurs? That should shake them up, hopefully enough for one of them to spill his beans into the wrong ear. Finally, be very careful. The Kazka bandits are rough. Make sure you only target their grunts, the others are too tough to be worth the hassle.'),
(93203,0,3,21469,500,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500001,16796,5,'Bring 500x Bag of Counterfeit Credits to the agent.','It seems you managed to stir up a hornet''s nest over in Sakkikainen. The bandits there are in turmoil and intelligence has been picking up all kinds of interesting information lately. Alas, none of it has to do with the supposed bank robbery. But one transmission we intercepted was particularly interesting. It seems one of the gangs associated with the Kazka bandits has managed to forge some counterfeit credits. I don''t have to tell you the effects it would have on the fragile economy in the constellation if these credits get into circulation. The gang in questioned is called Dry River. We need to stop these guys before they go on a shopping spree. I need you to head back into Sakkikainen, find these counterfeiters and take them out. Pick up as much of the counterfeit credits as you can and get them back here to me. I will send them on to the Navy''s crime labs for further analysis. So gather up some friends and take care of business. Oh, and in case you were wondering, you''ll be paid in real ISK for completing this mission.'),
(93204,0,5,21469,500,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'Transport the 500x Bag of Counterfeit Credits','Ok, while you were out there collecting the counterfeit money, I was contacted by my superiors. It seems the Navy is taking this whole counterfeit operation very seriously. The Navy has sent out a team of investigators; they''ve set up shop in the State War Academy station in the Ishisomo system. They want me to send all counterfeit credits I get directly to them, no delay. The investigation team there is trying to determine the source of the forgery. Anyway, while I can understand their concern, this whole thing is disrupting my own work in keeping the bank vault safe. So I want this dealt with promptly and with as little hassle as possible. I want you to take the bags of counterfeit credits you just procured and bring them to the investigation team immediately.'),
(93205,0,3,21517,5,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500010,16796,5,'Bring 5x Parts of Printing Machine to the agent.','This counterfeit business is really getting on my nerves. Yet again I''ve been contacted by headquarters; they want me to bring this matter to an end. That means I can''t do my job securing the bank vault properly, but they''re not cutting me any slack. If the bank is actually robbed, all the blame will fall on me. Oh, well. At least I can make sure this counterfeit business has a happy ending. The investigation team in Ishisomo got a breakthrough in their analysis. They''ve tracked the source of the forged credits to the Airmia system. The Dry River gang owns a warehouse there that was once part of a Lai Dai mining facility that''s been overrun by bandits. The printing machines used in creating the counterfeit credits are located there. I want you to take some stout fellows over to Airmia and blow that warehouse to bits. The warehouse is undoubtely guarded by some Dry River thugs, you''ll have to deal with them first. Bring me back what parts of the printing machines you can find in the ruins of the warehouse once you''ve blown it up. I will send those to my superiors. Hopefully that will get them off my back and let me get on with my real assignment here. You''re getting a nice reward for this one, so make sure you do it properly.'),
(93206,0,5,21043,1,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'Provide 1x Ancient Treasure Map from Hitami Magye to agent','Now look at what the cat dragged in... another exhausted traveler looking for something cheerful to break the monotony of his existence. If that''s really the case then you came to the right place! We got a casino here that''s open all hours every day of the week, except on the major Otitoh holidays. If you''re looking for a place to rest and have a pleasant evening, then spend the night in our pleasure hub nearby. If you want entertainment, you came to the right place dude! Echelon E. provides all your entertainment needs with prices unrivaled in the entire galaxy ''''cough'''' excluding some Gallente venues ''''cough''''. If you''re looking for fame and fortune however, I might be of some help. I''ve been searching for a long lost treasure rumored to be hidden somewhere inside Otitoh, by the captain of a Gallente freighter who was ambushed here during the first Caldari-Gallente war. I''ve come across a number of clues, but have never managed to find that blasted treasure map which is supposed to lead me straight to it. Find me the map, and we can become rich together. What do you say?'),
(93207,0,5,21047,1,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'Transport 1x Oshima''s System Scanner (800 m3)','After taking a quick look at the map you brought back, I''m positive that I need a system scanner to find the exact location that the map specifies. It''s very vague, but does specify a relatively small area in space where I should be able to locate a cosmic signature. I''ll tell you what, retrieve my old system scanner at Ishisomo IX - Moon 9 - Chief Executive Panel Bureau and I''ll give you a bookmark to the treasure. I won''t accept any of those new fancy-pancy scanners, I wouldn''t know how they work anyway. In other words, if you don''t get me my scanner then the deal''s off, understand?'),
(93208,0,3,21048,1,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',0,0,0,'Provide 1x Kepheur''s Keycard (0.1 m3)','Now that I have the system scanner, there is just one more item that''s missing. Upon closer examination I noticed a small paragraph scribbled on the back of the map, where the map-maker claims a keycard is needed to enter the site where he hid the treasure. I had actually discovered this long ago, before I first came to Otitoh, when I spoke to a relative of the deceased Gallente pilot who originally hid the treasure. I tracked this keycard down to a famous Guristas buccaneer, Tao Pai Motow, who often roams the asteroid fields inside the Kazka Headquarter deadspace pocket in Sakkikainen. Needless to say, I barely escaped with my life when I confronted Tao and offered a generous deal for the keycard. Apparently he''s fully aware of what the keycard is for, and has been searching for the treasure himself for many years. I''m afraid we do not have any choice except to hunt this pirate down and nab the keycard from him by force. There isn''t a Ark roid''s chance in Curse of getting it from that brute without a fight. Once you''ve found him and acquired the keycard, we can continue our search.'),
(93209,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500022,16732,5,'','Now the time has arrived to claim the long lost treasure of Kepheur Buquet! You have his keycard, and I''ll give you the coordinates of the deadspace pocket where he hid his treasure. I''m a bit worried that you might run into some trouble getting to it, as the area where I located the cosmic signature is heavily infested with rogue drones. It''s officially a ''no-fly'' zone according to the Caldari authorities here, and they refuse to offer any kind of assistance in clearing those pesky drones. Many pilots have lost their lives there, so be careful. Once you have found the treasure, loot it and return immediately to me.'),
(93210,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500002,17138,5,'Bring 100 Powdered Cubensis to the agent.','I''ve been working on this here concoction, see. It frees the mind from its everyday shackles, lets the spirit roam free among the hinterlands and is one hell of a laxative to boot! Only thing is, I need this one particular ingredient. Just a little spice to perfect the whole deal, see. Now, I know of this feller who''s got a bit of what I need. If you could see fit to - how to put it - relieve him of his fear of death, then you could bring me that special ingredient and I could give you a cut of my profits. Feller''s called Wolf Skarkert, and he hangs around in that contested mining facility, peddling his wares to the lonely souls actually trying to eke out a living in them god-forsaken badlands. Get me his powdered cubensis, and we''ll see if we can''t make ya that tiny bit richer. How about it?'),
(93211,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500002,17138,5,'''''Clear some mission pocket from rats.''''','Well, friend, we''re in it now. I just caught a whiff that there''s one of them darned bounty hunters in system, looking for my hide. And I have a hunch you''re next. See, this here''s one of them Caldari fellers, and he''s working for the corporation that synthesized the cubensis you stole. Cubensis is always a hot product on account of how much the Man hates it, so they hafta take extreme measures if''n it slips out. He''s hanging out at the Gravediggers Saloon, a filthy smuggler dive located in this system and filled with lowlives. I''ll give ya the coordinates if ya can take him out for me. I''ll also give ya something more. And remember, this feller could come for YOU next. And he''s a tough one, I hear, so you''d better pack yer big guns. For good measure, I''m gonna ask ya to destroy the saloon well, so there won''t be no evidence for those other scumbags to trace ya back here. Well, whatcha waiting for? Get to it!'),
(93212,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500002,0,0,'Bring 2500 Liberation Elixir (500 m3) to a given destination.','Alright, partner, thanks to your good work I''ve been able to make my wonderful concoction, The Liberation Elixir. Greatest thing since Quafe Ultra, I tell ya. Now all I need is someone to help me get it to my distributor so it can start working for the greater good o'' mankind. That''s right, friend, I''m eyeing you for the job. If you can be a dear and get it to <station> within a couple of hours, I can be makin'' money in no time! And, of course, I''ll reward you handsomely for your work. How''s that sound to ya?'),
(93213,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'','You have to help me! I screwed up big time. My superiors trusted me with secret locations to ancient relics hidden by the civilizations that lived here centuries ago. If they find out about this I''m finished within Lai Dai, they will probably even make sure that I never find work again! This document was stolen from me by one of our adversaries, I''m sure. Go to the contested Lai Dai Refinery and see if you can find it there. If you find it, bring it back to me.'),
(93214,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'','I think I''m going mad! Those reports you gave me were nothing like the stolen ones! We have to make sure my superiors do not find out about the missing reports. Go to <station> and give them these status reports, any doubts they have should be cleared once they see these.}}<noinclude> [[Category:COSMOS missions]] {{NPCTableCSS'),
(93215,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'','"name", go back to the Lai Dai refinery and destroy every single ship that might be there. Bring back to me every report you find, if we look hard enough we''re bound to find the right one eventually. You have to hurry though, my superiors are getting suspicious of why I haven''t made any progress on the excavation operations that were assigned to me. Letting your plans fall into enemy hands is bad for business.'),
(93216,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500010,16796,5,'Retrieve the scanner data from the Radio Telescope and then return to Raidon Setala.','We''ve set up a few telescopes in the surrounding asteroid belts around Sakkikainen VI to establish a powerful surveillance network, which we will use to determine the magnitude of rogue elements in the area. This is necessary for us to be able to calculate the cost of maintaining an adequate police force in Sakkikainen VI. A few days ago we lost contact with 3 of our telescopes. I hope that it was caused by a malfunction in the communication device inside the telescope, but I have to be prepared for the worst. And the fact that the last team I sent out there to investigate haven''t returned yet ... well, it pretty much confirms my fears. I want you to fly over to one of the surveillance telescopes and retrieve the scanner data chip from it''s main computer. If lady luck is with us, the telescope will still be intact. If the data is retrieved, I will be able to access the logs and discover what caused the loss of communication.'),
(93217,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500010,16796,5,'Bring the agent a Scanner Data II','I''ve received word from two other teams I sent out to investigate the loss of communication with the surveillance telescopes. They reported that the other two telescopes have been completely looted, leaving nothing behind save the exterior hull of the structures. This obviously means they could not retrieve the scanner data as I had requested. I believe that the scanner data, along with the expensive computer systems we had installed in the surveillance telescopes, is in the possession of the Guristas Pirates or other bandit elements within Okkelen. I want you to personally organize a search for the missing scanner data chips. Scourge the asteroid belts in Okkelen, the pirates responsible for stealing the data may be located anywhere within the constellation. If you miraculously find the computer chips, then return to me and I will reward you generously.'),
(93218,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500001,16796,5,'Bring the agent a Scanner Data III.','Now that we have two of the surveillance scanner data chips, there''s just one more to go. I expect you''ll be able to find it in much the same way as the second data chip. Search the asteroid belts in Okkelen for pirate elements, eventually you might stumble upon the computer chip. If you do, I''ll pay a great deal of ISK for it.'),
(93219,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500001,16796,5,'','After reviewing the data from the surveillance telescope logs, I''ve confirmed that the Guristas did in fact stand behind the sabotage. The leader of one of the attacks, Quao Kale, is a well known Guristas agent. I want him captured and brought to justice. With luck, he will lead us to someone higher in the Guristas chain of command who can be held accountable for organizing the entire operation. The Guristas who attacked our installations were far too coordinated for this to have been just a spate of random burglary. You''ll find Quao in the Kazka Bandit Headquarters within Sakkikainen. He''s one of the Guristas envoys there, who are rumored to be controlling the Kazka behind the scene. You''ll probably have to fight your way through a legion of bandits to get to him, so be prepared. And don''t forget to bring him here alive, he''s worth nothing to us dead! Good luck.'),
(93220,0,1,21672,1,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Courier',500001,0,0,'Transport 1x Quao Kale (1m3) to destination station.','I want you to bring Quao Kale, who you captured in your last mission, to our station in Silen. There he will be tried and punished accordingly. Once that is over with, he will be interrogated and perhaps even brain scanned, depending on the legal implications. You''ve done well for us so far, and certainly have earned your reward. My mission here is nearing completion, soon I''ll personally deliver my report to Hien Karnuras. I only hope I don''t have any more encounters with the Guristas, I just can''t wait to get back to my comfortable office on New Caldari Prime. Declining a mission from a particular agent more than once every 4 hours may result in a loss of standing with that agent, except in the case of special missions that clearly state otherwise in their description.'),
(93221,0,3,21734,240,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500001,16796,5,'Provide 240 x Cattle (240 m3) to agent.','It so happens that the School of Applied Knowledge ordered a very large shipment of cattle to their station here in Sakkikainen. I was given the job after losing a bet with one of my co-workers ― as you might expect, Okkelen is one of the least popular constellations within the State for delivery people like me. It''s simply swarming with pirates and other scum. Needless to say, once I arrived through the stargate, I was immediately beset by pirates camping the other side of the gate. I hit my microwarpdrive and almost made it, but they managed to warp scramble me at the last moment. And of course my darned escort team fled like a bunch of pansies at the first sight of combat! So I had no choice but to eject my cargo. It was either that or death, and I''ll be damned before I commit suicide in the name of those corporate pigs! Anyway, you now know my dilemma, and my question is simple: Will you help me get my cattle back!? I''m in no position to do it myself, obviously, and I''d rather not return home empty-handed. You certainly look like someone who has some combat experience... so if you''re up to it, then I''ll give you directions to the bandit outpost where I believe they are keeping my cattle.'),
(93222,0,1,21734,2600,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Courier',500001,0,0,'Transport 2,600x Cattle (2,600 m3) to agent.','Unfortunately, the cattle you retrieved from the pirates in your last mission are insufficient. In fact, I don''t think the School of Applied Knowledge will even bother accepting such a low quantity of them; I need 2600 more units to complete the shipment. I''d like you to help me make ends meet: I''ve contacted my colleagues at Kiainti IX - Moon 8 - Prompt Delivery Storage, and they have the cattle I need. If you could pick up those cattle and deliver them to Sakkikainen VI - Moon 8 - School of Applied Knowledge, I would be extremely grateful.'),
(93223,0,3,21736,1,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500001,16796,5,'Deliver 1x Loki''s DNA (0.1 m3) to agent.','Damn that Loki Machedo. He headed up the bandit gang that stole my cattle and delayed me by many days. I''ll probably get demoted for this! I will have my revenge. I heard he wasn''t at the bandit site where you found some of the cattle, so he must still be at large. I know a guy, Midoki Urigamu, who is surprisingly knowledgeable about the Guristas pirates. He told me that Loki works as a prison guard in the Guristas Outrider Post in Otomainen. So you might find him in the Prison Facility, as long as he''s on duty and not raiding defenseless convoys... I''ll give you everything I have in exchange for proof that he''s dead.'),
(93224,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'Bring 3 Wiyrkomi Rifles (15 m3) to the agent.','Are you looking for work? Wiyrkomi is expanding into this area and help would be greatly appreciated. This whole constellation seems to be infested with the scum of the universe. Rogue drones, pirates and ruthless scavengers are everywhere and everybody wants a piece of the action. Yesterday we discovered that a big part of our weapon stash had gone missing. We have every reason to believe that the Guristas hanging out at the contested Lai Dai Refinery in the Airmia system are behind this theft and would like you, along with others, to go and try to retrieve some of the weapons. If you can complete this task, perhaps I will give you something more rewarding next time.'),
(93225,0,5,439,3,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'Pick up 3x 1MN Afterburner I (15 m³)','Those weapons you retrieved were essential to our effort, thanks to you our troops will be well armed and ready for battle. If they think they can shove us out of this constellatiom they''re wrong. We''re getting a piece of this cake whether they like it or not. The battle is far from being won, your services are required for another task. I need you to go to Ishisomo VII - Moon 14 - Propel Dynamics Factory and pick up some afterburners. They are a gift from our friends at Propel Dynamics and I want them delivered here in perfect condition. Now, do not screw this up, or it will have dire consequences.'),
(93226,0,5,21463,3,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'Pick up 3x Excavation Equipment (3 m³)','I have another task for you, <Pilot>. One of our excavators has stumbled upon what seems to be the remains of an ancient monument. The extinct civilizations worshipped many different gods and are believed to have buried hundreds of artifacts around their monuments. If this excavation is successful, it could make us all very rich men. Our problem is that we are sending more people out there right now and have run out of supplies. I need you to go pick up some excavation equipment and deliver it to me, if this goes well perhaps both of us can pay tribute to the only god that matters, the god of more money.'),
(93227,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500001,16796,5,'Bring one Ancient Weapon to the agent.','I''m sorry to inform you that our excavation didn''t go as planned. Just as our lead scientist on location, Reilen Oshomi, announced that is team had come across some kind of ancient weapon, the whole operation was raided by Guristas pirates and only Reilen and a few others managed to escape. The Guristas captured the item and we believe they took it to the Lai Dai Refinery in Airmia. Perhaps if you went there you might be able to retrieve it for us. There is a lot fighting going on there between many factions, so be careful. Also, I''m afraid this is going to be the last mission I can give to you. After this incident my commanders issued a no-fly policy of all Wiyrkomi vessels and it seems their interests in the area have severly dwindled. Please complete this mission for me, and perhaps one day we will have the pleasure of working together again.'),
(93228,0,3,21616,5,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500010,16796,5,'Retrieve 5x Nugoeihuvi Dogtag (0,5 m3)','Hey there, I realize you might be busy with something else, but I could really use some help over here. My superiors have assigned a lot of tasks to me and I''m not sure if I can handle them all by myself. There are some Nugoeihuvi excavators stepping on our turf at the contested Lai Dai Refinery in Airmia. If you could go there and "take care" of them, it would be well appreciated. Bring back some Nugoeihuvi dogtags as proof of your actions.'),
(93229,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'','I have another task for you, my friend. Small outbreaks have been popping up around Vahunomi X - Moon 4 - State and Region Bank Vault and the local police authorities are having troubles defusing the situation. Please deliver these rifles, they will prove a valuable aid and my superiors would definitely notice if you played a part in this.'),
(93230,0,3,21783,1,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500001,16796,5,'Kill Rats and Bring Item 1 x Unassembled Hybrid Weapons (5.0 m³)','As you may know, my organization is looking to find inroads into this constellation and we believe the Friggi system is a key location. Thing is, we''ve got some of those no-good Caldari troublemakers in this system, and they just won''t stop hounding us. What could they ever have against peaceful businessmen like us, I wonder? Well, no matter. I need you to bring me some information. In order to have a real impact here, we''re going to need to have some dirt on our competitors and play it the ol'' sly way. Brute force doesn''t always work, and we don''t really want to get the State''s bristles up enough for them to send a Navy detachment down here. That would just ruin the whole peaceful vibe we''ve got going down here, don''t you agree? I''ve uploaded some coordinates to your Neocom, there. Upon arrival at these coordinates, you''ll find a tiny asteroid belt whose signature is masked due to a deadspace pocket. The Nugoeihuvi chaps -- you''re familiar with them, right? -- have been using this belt to conduct some illicit business with parties unknown. Now, when you arrive they''re likely to attack you on sight, so you just use your superior firepower and show them what for. Bring me any evidence you can find of their dealings. I''ll make sure you''re rewarded properly.'),
(93231,0,1,26781,1,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Courier',500010,0,0,'Transport 1x Crates of Transmitters (60.0 m³) to 0.5 Otitoh','Okay, first off, the box you brought back with the unassembled weapon parts was a valuable find, so thanks for that. In addition to the weapons, it contained some evidence that Nugoeihuvi have certain plans for this system that conflict with ours - and they''re not going about them through the proper, stiff-assed Caldari channels, which puts us in a fine position, leverage-wise. But on to some other matters at hand. My organization has an outpost in the Otitoh system, one that is in dire need of supplies at the moment. In particular, they require some transmitters to keep the outpost''s reconnaisance operations running. We''ve been expecting a large Caldari Navy incursion for a while now, and capsuleer forces have been hitting the complex pretty hard these past few weeks, so we need to keep a pretty steady stream of supplies coming in. If you can get these transmitters to the Caldari Executive Panel station in Otitoh within 20 minutes and drop them in your hangar there for pickup, I''ll make it worth your while.'),
(93232,0,1,21800,1,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Courier',500010,0,0,'Transport 1 x EMP Charge Components (1.0 m³) to 0.5 Friggi','We have a situation that''s come up. There''s a Caldari Navy operative in this system by the name of Agent Maro Yama. We''ve discovered that he''s the one who''s supposed to be orchestrating the big attack on our Otitoh outpost in the coming weeks. Gurista High Command has instructed me to sabotage his operation, and to this end you can help. Agent Yama is based at a place called the Clear Water Spring in this system, but anything as crass as an all-out attack will only send the Navy crashing down on our heads in full force, something which would be very detrimental indeed to our expansion efforts in this constellation. Agent Yama does, however, have extensive ties to the Lai Dai Corporation Factory station at Friggi VII - Moon 12, and we know him to have ships and equipment at that station ready for deployment at a moment''s notice. The mission, as it pertains to you, is relatively straightforward. This package here has been made to look like a standard shipment of holofeed receptors, egones and projectors but contains hidden parts that, when assembled correctly, will be capable of doing severe electromagnetic damage to Caldari Navy assets in the station. Bring this there, and don''t get caught, and you will have done the Guristas a great service. Do this well, and we might discuss what else you can do for us - and how we can reward you.'),
(93233,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500001,16796,5,'Destroy the Navy''s Command and Control center in Otitoh System.','It''s time to act fast, <Pilot>. We''ve just received reports that the Caldari Navy has established a forward outpost in the Otitoh system, in preparation for a strike at our complex in the area. According to our information they have a sizable force there already, and are preparing to move in more people. We''re happy to tell you, however, that the EMP charge you placed at the Lai Dai station had its desired effect, severely damaging a substantial number of support vessels and equipment the Navy had meant for use in Otitoh. Now is therefore the time to strike, while they are weakened and working to compensate for the loss of backup assets. We need you to go in there and take out the Navy''s Command and Control center in the area. Any losses you can inflict on them while doing so will be most appreciated, but the primary target is the CCcenter. If that is taken down, the Navy will have to retreat from the area, and our plans for this constellation will be that much closer to fruition. Once the building is destroyed, report back to me and I will see to it that you are rewarded handsomely for your efforts. The Guristas will not forget this one, <Pilot>. Good luck.'),
(93234,0,3,21634,1,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500011,17138,5,'Acquire 1x Secret Garage Coordinates (0.1 m³)','I''m setting up an escape route for my friend Krakan Rost, for some job he''s planning. I already got two fast ships, a Crow and a Raptor, lined up as the getaway vessels. I''m plotting the escape course as we speak. I want to use the Crow as the first getaway ship, then switch over to the Raptor to confuse the police and any potential pursuers.'),
(93235,0,5,21637,1,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500011,0,0,'Transport these goods: 1 x Data Chip Decoder (0.1 m³).','Congratulations again on a job well done. Sad thing is, these bandits are obviously more paranoid than most: The data chip you gave me is encoded with some heavy-duty codelock. The Data Analyzer I''ll need for this is not something available on the common market. I did some digging around, and turns out there''s a black marketeer operating out of the Chief Executive Panel station in Otitoh. Strange place for such an operation, but I gather he''s working under the protection of some high-level official there. Only goes to show what a strange place Okkelen is these days. Anyway, Rost wants me here, so I need someone to get that decoder for me. And as you did so well the last time, I think you''re the one.'),
(93236,0,3,2624,1,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500011,17138,5,'Bring Item Objective 1x Crates of Mechanical Parts (100 m³)','I''ve finally managed to crack this damn data chip open, thanks to the decoder you got me. The garage is in the middle of nowhere, as I expected. No wonder the police have no idea of its whereabouts. It''s just too perfect a place to switch ships. Definitely worth all this hassle. I''m ready to ship the Raptor out to this garage, but first it has to be cleared out. I think you''re the right person for that task. It shouldn''t be too hard, though ― there are probably just a few mechanics over there ― but just to be on the safe side you might consider bringing some pals along. As soon as you accept this mission, I''ll upload the location of the garage into your ship computer. I have a nice reward lined up for you for doing this for me.'),
(93237,0,5,21661,1,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500011,0,0,'Transport Cargo 1 x Spiked Quafe (0.1 m³).','Okay, I''m all set with my preparations, so now all I have to do is wait for Rost to finish ... well, whatever it is he''s doing. My guess is it has something to do with the bank vault here in Vahunomi, but I have no idea really. Go talk to him about that, if you haven''t already. There''s only one more thing I need, and then everything is perfect. It''s my custom to down a bottle of spiked Quafe just before the action heats up. The only problem is, I don''t have any with me, and as far as I know there''s none to be found in this godforsaken constellation. Thankfully, I''ve located a supermarket station in the next constellation that carries it. Can you bring me a bottle? Such a simple task, I know, but I will pay you well for it.'),
(93238,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500001,16796,5,'Transport these goods: 4x Symmetry Decryptor (0.4 m3)','There are a lot of sharks swimming the dark waters of Okkelen these days. But that isn''t all bad for small fish like you and me because these sharks are mainly interested in what the other sharks are doing. And wouldn''t you know, they''re even willing to pay good money to someone that can provide them with that information. Enter little ol'' me. I''ve been making steady business ferreting out interesting stuff from various sources and selling them to the highest bidder. There are a lot of places that such information can be gathered. The contested complex in Friggi is one such place, but not for those faint of heart, for it is heavily defended. But right here in Airmia is a place ideally suited for a bit of old school industrial espionage. The Guristas are operating a small spy station in the contested Lai Dai Refinery. If you possess some decent hacking skills you''re bound to find something of value there. I might even be interested in buying some of the stuff you dig up.'),
(93239,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Courier',500001,0,0,'Acquire 1x System Scanner (5 m3)','Hello <Pilot>, I''m Tamoko Raytio and with me here in the Bustard is my entire family. We left our home on Airkio VII - Moon 3 - Lai Dai Corporation Factory, intent on settling somewhere in the wild frontier, and ended up here in Otomainen. We originally set off with two ships, one Badger carrying our supplies, and then the Bustard carrying us. The Badger was piloted by a close friend of mine, Tari Ykonan, may he rest in peace, who was killed in a cowardly pirate attack near the Rush Town Ruins in this system. The attack damaged our ship and left us stranded here in this desolate place. Now we need to replenish our supplies to survive the rest of the trip. We are still intent on settling here, it''s too late to turn back now. We have enough food supplies in the Bustard''s cargo hold to last us at least a few months, so that''s not a problem. The first item I need is a system scanner. You''ll find one that I purchased on Ihakana VIII - Moon 6 - Nugoeihuvi Corporation Development Studio, bring it here a.s.a.p.'),
(93240,0,3,21126,30,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500001,16796,5,'Provide 30x Raytio Family Supplies (300 m3) to agent.','You might be wondering how we''ll store all the containers, due to their total size they won''t all fit into our cargo hold. Which is why we''ll keep them stored in one of the asteroids here, and slowly transport them to our new settlement.'),
(93241,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500019,26249,5,'Clear the area of Sansha ships, including their Envoy.','Now that we have salvaged all the supplies we need for the time being, it''s time to find the promised land. You see, we didn''t come to Otomainen by pure chance, there is a reason for us choosing this system as our new home. A few years ago, we heard of a great Monolith, one of the famous Black Monoliths which are a very rare sight indeed in our galaxy. My wife actually stumbled upon it in a news report on the KLC network. When we decided to leave on our adventure, we were convinced that this monolith would be the key to our fortune. Not only is it a beautiful sight, it also holds an enormous commercial value. Imagine how much people, especially the Amarrian religious fanatics who view the Monoliths as some kind of symbol of their faith, would pay for viewing the object. We''ll change this run-down system into a major hub of tourist activity! But there''s one catch to our plan. The Black Monolith is located inside a deadspace pocket, which happens to be inhabited by the Sansha envoy to the Guristas forces in Okkelen. He has a sizable entourage with him as well. Eliminate this hindrance and we will be eternally grateful, <Pilot>.'),
(93242,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'','The mega-corporations are trying to hog all the action here in Okkelen, but if you''re careful to stay under their radar it''s easy to get your hands on something good from time to time. I''m monitoring the excavation site here, looking for opportunities that might arise. In the meantime, I hear the Kazka Bandits over in Sakkikainen have hoarded a sizeable amount of artifacts in their headquarters. I''m well connected to shift these artifacts, so if you know anything about archaeology I''m interested in striking a bit of a buisness deal. I''ll pay you good money for any Talocan Mechanical Gears you manage to scavenge from the Kazka Bandits.'),
(93243,0,3,21465,1,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500001,16796,5,'Provide 1x Ancient Weapon (2 m3)','Welcome, <Pilot>. It is good to see capable pilots joining our ranks, these are troubled times and we certainly need all the help we can get. Your previous employer told me good things about you, perhaps if you do as well for me as you did for him, I will refer you to an even higher level agent. Now, for your first assignment. We have had reports of Guristas pirates destroying a Wiyrkomi excavation operation. Apparently the Wiyrkomi scientists had come across some sort of ancient weapon. The Guristas found out and raided the place, killing almost all the scientists and capturing the weapon. I want you to investigate this matter. Go to the Lai Dai Refinery in Airmia. Members of all factions are fighting over the refinery and if you move quickly, perhaps you could sneak in and steal the weapon.'),
(93244,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500001,16796,5,'Provide 3 Miner (9 m3)','Guristas are a constant pain in the backside. This time they have taken five of our miners captive and are demanding a ransom for their return. Our policy has never been to negotiate with terrorists, so I want you to go in there full force and deal with them. They are hanging out at the contested Lai Dai Refinery in Airmia. Bring the miners back to me unharmed, it would not look good with the State if we became responsible for those people''s deaths.'),
(93245,0,5,21467,1,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'Transport 1x Spy (3 m3)','Lately, Propel Dynamics have been trying to infiltrate our ranks. They know we have the upper hand in this region and apparently they seem to be wanting to sabotage our operations. We have discovered the identity of this spy, yesterday we arrested him and he is currently in my custody. I want you to take him to <Station>, there he will be tried and justice brought to the matter.'),
(93246,0,5,21520,5,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'Provide 5x Guristas Outlaw Dogtag (0.5 m3)','That spy is being tried for his crimes as we speak, thanks to you he will go away for a long time. I, however, have another task for you. Around these parts, outlaws are a constant threat. Every day they raid caravans, steal their loot and murder innocents. Here in Ishisomo, we believe the source of these attacks is the Lai Dai Refinery in Airmia. I want you to go there, destroy every structure you see and leave none alive. Show them the might of Nugoeihuvi, show them justice. Bring me back five Guristas Outlaw Dogtags as proof of your actions.'),
(93247,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'Transport 2 Propel Dynamics Reports (3.0 m3)','You''re moving even further up the corporate ladder, my friend. My superiors have taken a great interest in your talent and have decided that after this task, you will be reassigned to a new agent in Airmia. Apparently the troubles there are much greater than the ones here and they wish only for the most competent of pilots to head out there. Your last assignment for me will be to deliver these reports to <Station>, they are reports of all Propel Dynamics activity in the past two weeks. If there is another spy among us, this is how we will find him. Be safe, my friend. Perhaps we will see each other in the future.'),
(93248,0,5,21082,2,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Trade',500001,0,0,'Retrieve 2x Talocan System interface unit (0.2 m3)','Something tells me that we''re on the verge on discovering something really marvelous here in Okkelen that might change the way we look at the world forever. There are artifacts here that are thousands of years old and if we can discover who left them behind and what kind of society they lived in, it might put our own meager existence into a more enlightened perspective. Yes, interesting times indeed, and I for one want to do what I can to advance humankind to the next rug in the evolution ladder. I''m collecting interesting relics and am on the lookout for independent pilots that have some rudimentary knowledge of archaeology to help me out in this great endeavor. Are you interested?'),
(93249,0,3,20477,60,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500001,16796,5,'Provide 60x Bandit Spur (6 m3) to agent.','I''m so glad to see you ―name‖. I had almost given up hope on finding a skilled mercenary to do some dangerous work for Lai Dai Corporation. I''ve looked everywhere in this run-down system but you''re the first ray of hope that I''ve encountered so far. We have a serious problem on our hands at the State And Region Bank in Ihakana. A gang of hooligans has been terrorizing passersby in the area, allegedly causing damage to our property and pestering our customers. We haven''t been able to pin anything major on them yet, but our patience has worn out. I will pay you a large sum of ISK if you take care of these pests yourself, before they do any serious harm. The deadspace pocket is hidden from passive sensors. You will need to use probes to scan down the Kazka blockade.'),
(93250,0,1,21044,2000,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Courier',500001,0,0,'Transport 2,000x Pistols (4,000 m3)','Because of the volatile situation here in Ihakana, we''ve been planning on funding a local militia to participate in the defenses of our station. CONCORD and the State have a very loose hold on the entire constellation, and Ihakana is no exception. We can''t afford to ask them for any favors, we have to take matters into our own hands. Because funding for our project here is limited, we''ve had to make due with cheap small arms, aka pistols. I''ve been promised a shipment of them at Vouskiaho III - Genolution Biotech Production, if you could be so kind as to transport them to the S.R.B. station in this system I would be very grateful.'),
(93251,0,3,20480,25,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500001,16796,5,'Provide 25x Gunslinger Spur (2.5 m3)','Unfortunately your previous assignment for me was not a complete success. I was wrong about the bandits abandoning their plans of causing havoc near the State and Region bank in Ihakana when they start to get a taste of their own medicine. Despite a number of their ships having been destroyed, I''ve noticed a surge in their activity near the station. They are mainly compromised of the natives of Ihakana who are poor and jobless, and angry at the State for the lack of interest this system receives from the government. For some reason they believe attacking the State and Region Bank will help their cause … foolish if you ask me. But when their leaders fall, we believe they will become discouraged and this temporary surge of unrest will dissipate. Bring me evidence of their demise and you shall be rewarded.'),
(93252,0,3,21885,1,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500010,16796,5,'Acquire these goods: 1x Caldari Navy Convoy Disposition File (0.1 m³)','Gurista High Command has tasked me with a very important assignment. Our intelligence reports that a Caldari Navy convoy is headed out here, bearing arms, supplies and equipment for Navy forces in the area. We intend to intercept this convoy and re-route the cargo to our own complex in Otitoh, but we need to do it covertly so contracting non-Gurista operatives such as yourself is a necessity. The convoy has an undercover scout headed through this system. What I''m gonna need you to do right now is find and intercept this scout, then bring me back the convoy disposition file so we can tell our strike force what they''re up against. The scout, Huriki Vunau, is known to be at a rendezvous point with an associate in the contested mining facility complex in system. Find him, kill him, and report back to me with the file.'),
(93253,0,1,22077,1,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Transport',500010,0,0,'Deliver 1x Encoded Gurista Intelligence Dossier (0.1 m³)','Our intelligence operatives have compiled the information you brought, along with information provided by others, in a dossier which should give our strike force all it needs to intercept that convoy and grab whatever goodies they''re carrying. They''ll never know what hit them. I need you to take the dossier to a station in Otitoh and leave it in your hangar there. One of our agents from the outpost in Otitoh will get to it, hopefully in time for us to make the strike as quickly and efficiently as possible. If you can do this quickly, I''ll throw in an extra reward for you. Good luck.'),
(93254,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500010,16796,5,'Eliminate the Gurista force.','As you may know, Ihakana and the surrounding systems are completely infested by Gurista pirates. In my work for Internal Security in this system, I''ve had a number of deputies under me, every single one of whom has fallen prey to these dirty dogs. Fiderer, my last deputy, was a particularly good lad, and I hated to see him go down to those bastards. I''m always on the lookout for people who know their way around a fight. If you''re interested, I can deputize you: Plenty of work to be done around here. If you feel like proving your mettle, there''s a small Gurista forward base in this area that''s been no end of trouble for quite a while now. It''s not a large outpost as outposts go, but according to our intelligence it plays host to some very powerful Gurista cronies, people not to be trifled with. If you can go in there and eliminate the Gurista force, I''d be much obliged. I''d also be likely to have more work for you.'),
(93255,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500010,16796,5,'Destroy the outpost''s storage silo.','Okay, listen up. I have some more Gurista butt for you to kick. Yeah, I thought you''d be happy. There''s another outpost in one of the outlying systems where the Guristas have a nice little drug lab going. This is a slightly bigger target than the last one we hired you to take out, so expect more opposition. Break through their defenses, destroy the outpost''s storage silo, and get back to me for your reward. Get to it, deputy.'),
(93256,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500010,16796,5,'Kill the detachment of frigates being trained at the facility.','I have a report here on my desk stating that the Guristas have been training a special frigate wing for hit-and-run operations in the vicinities of Ihakana and Friggi. Intelligence has given us the location of one of the training bases for this frigate wing, and we intend to put a dent in this little scheme of theirs. I need you to go out to the next system, where the base is, kill the detachment of frigates being trained there, and destroy their training bunkers. Beware: The instructors are accomplished pilots, and there may be a battleship or two guarding the facilities. Go in with caution. Good luck.'),
(93257,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500010,16796,5,'Track down Choiji Korakami at his hideout and kill him.','Deputy, we have a problem. The Guristas have brought in a special operative, rumored to be the cousin of Korako "The Rabbit" Korakami. His name is Choiji, and he''s known throughout this area for his fearsome prowess in battleship combat. Now, we''re not certain what exactly it is he''s doing here, but we''re not going to wait to find out. Internal Security High Command has given the go-ahead for us to eliminate him, and I''m giving the job to you. I''ve uploaded the coordinates of his hideout to your Neocom. Be careful - he has two fanatically devoted bodyguards who won''t take kindly to your attempt to kill their master. Good luck.'),
(93258,0,5,21588,4,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Trade',500001,0,0,'Trade 4x Spare Parts (0.4 m3)','Some bright light back at headquarters got the idea that SuVee was missing out on something good here in Okkelen. So they sent poor old me out here to map the riches. Yeah, right. If I ever find out who''s responsible, I''ll make him dance to the tune of my AK-107. This place is a real hellhole. All I''ve encountered is dust and danger. I''ve heard plenty of stories of fabulous riches, but that''s it --- just stories. My superiors are getting restless, wanting more than hints and rumors from me, so I''m looking for prospective pilots to lend me a bit of a hand. From what I''ve heard, the Guristas pirates have amassed an impressive amount of treasure and valuable information in the contested complex here in Friggi, but that stuff is pretty well defended, so you need some heavy armaments to have any chance of tackling that. A better bet is heading out of the Airmia system and enter the spy station the Guristas are operating in the contested complex there. If you have some basic hacking knowledge, I''m sure you can dig up something of value to me. Just be very careful --- a big gun is a man''s best friend around here so be prepared to face a few.'),
(93259,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Courier',500001,0,0,'Transport 3 Reports (0.3 m3) from agent to given destination.','I cannot believe somebody ratted me out! Somehow, those damned Nugoeihuvi agents found out about my plan and fixed their security flaws. Had I been successful, high command definitely would have given me a raise! Oh, sorry, I don''t suppose you''re interested in any of that. I do however have some tasks for you, perhaps we can get back at Nugoeihuvi some other way. This constellation is on fire, there are so many things to explore and discover. Everybody wants a piece of the action, and I''m here to make sure Lai Dai gets the whole cake Firstly, I need you to take these reports and deliver them to <station>. The reports contain data on all our discoveries within the constellation and it would be unfortunate if they fell into the wrong hands.'),
(93260,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Courier',500001,0,0,'Transport 1 Milk (0.5 m3) between two given stations.','My mother is very old and very sick. Yesterday she contacted me and asked me to buy her some milk. I''m afraid my duties here require me to stay, but if you could see to it that she gets her milk, I would be grateful. Take this and deliver it to <station>. Be quick about it and don''t get blown up. She gets grumpy if she doesn''t get her milk, and she usually takes her rage out on me.'),
(93261,0,3,21465,1,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500001,16796,5,'Acquire 1x Ancient Weapon (2.0 m3)','A few minutes ago, reports came in regarding Guristas pirates destroying a Wiyrkomi excavation operation. Apparently the Wiyrkomi scientists had come across some sort of ancient weapon. The Guristas found out and raided the place, killing almost all the scientists and capturing the weapon. I want you to investigate this matter. Go to the contested Lai Dai Refinery in Airmia, find this weapon and bring it back to me. I know the Nugoeihuvi are trying to get hold of it as well, but I want you to beat them to it.'),
(93262,0,3,21520,5,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500001,16796,5,'Acquire 5x Guristas Outlaw Dogtag (0.5 m3)','The damned Guristas are constant pain in the backside. Their spies are everywhere and there seems to be no way of getting rid of them for good. We have exhausted almost all methods but they always come back for more. This time I want something really radical to be done. Go to the contested Lai Dai Refinery and destroy all their bunkers and training facilities. If we destroy their roots, maybe the whole tree will fall. Bring back five Guristas Outlaw Leader Insignias as proof of your actions.'),
(93263,0,3,20551,1,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500010,16796,5,'Provide 1x Manchura''s Logs (0.1 m3) to agent.','So ... tired. Michi has been holed up here for longer than he can remember ... and he won''t leave until his broken heart has been mended ... his lost love must be returned! Old Michi won''t rest until he has found the truth! Been digging up these old ruins for years, but her body is nowhere in sight. Dead she is, Old Michi thought. Dead after those blasted Guristas scoundrels attacked the remnants of this once prosperous community. Dead after the metal walls of these beastly stations caved in from the assault. But then Old Michi stumbles upon an old pirate, in the Guristas stronghold of Otomainen, that he remembers from his younger years. A devilish man, who had a fancy for Old Michi''s lost love he did. This troublesome pirate scoffed at Old Michi he did, and claimed his lost love was still alive! But reveal her location he did not. Old Michi will pay handsomely for that information. Bring it to Old Michi and you''ll make him a happy man!'),
(93264,0,3,20554,1,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500010,16796,5,'Provide 1 x Wei Todaki (1.0 m3) to agent.','Now that Old Michi has the location of his lost love, <Pilot> needs to find her! ... Wei was the light of Michi''s life, back when he had a reason to live ... she was the cornerstone of his existence ... lost so long ago. But now he has a chance of regaining that precious lost love, and reclaiming what was lost to him so long ago ... the logs you retrieved indicate that she is being held prisoner at a Guristas base in an asteroid belt in this very system ... you must find her, and bring her back to Old Michi. Do this quickly, the end draws near for poor Michi ...'),
(93265,0,5,20554,1,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'Transport 1x Wei Todaki (1.0 m3) to Otsela VI - Moon 17 - Genolution Biotech Production.','Now that Michi and Wei have been reunited at long last, Michi has some worries ... Wei seems to have been brain washed by the Guristas scoundrels, she even thinks Michi is crazy! Wei needs to come to her senses, and Michi has lost all hope of convincing her himself. Therefore Old Michi has one final task for <Pilot> ... bring Wei to an old acquaintance of Michi ... this acquaintance runs a health clinic on Otsela VI - Moon 17 - Genolution Biotech Production. Bring Wei there and she will be taken care of, until her health problems have been dealt with ... do this for Michi and you shall be generously rewarded.'),
(93266,0,3,17206,30,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Security',500001,16796,5,'Bring 30x Guristas Diamond Tag (3.0 m³)','We have a policy here within the Caldari State that our more prominent members fly a suitable ship according to their status, both to give them an edge during combat and to uphold our image, especially within our borders. We have recently decided to extend this benefit to mercenaries or freelancers employed by us that have shown admirable bravery and skill in the field, or earned the right through countless hours of dedicated service to our corporations. As you undoubtedly already know I have been assigned the task of allocating these ships to their deserved owners. After looking at your record, we decided that you, <Character Name>, are worthy of such an honor. There is just one catch, since you aren''t an official member we need something in exchange for this gift. Cough up 30 x Guristas Diamond Tag and the Raven Navy Issue Blueprint is yours.'),
(93267,0,5,25273,20,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Trade',500001,0,0,'Trade 20x Golden Cytoserocin (200 m3)',''),
(93268,0,1,25467,5,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Distribution',500001,0,0,'Retrieve the corpses of Kakala Ikkawa''s colleagues [5 x Caldari Corpse (5.0 m³) from -0.3 ZXA-V6 (Low Sec Warning!)] and then report back to Pioneer''s Sanctuary in -0.1 ZH3-BS. (Low Sec Warning!)','Alright, I''ll tell you a little story. My expedition had discovered an area filled with gas clouds thicker than I had ever witnessed in my life, and we were ecstatic. For days we harvested the gas fields, with no end in sight. At that time I was already starting to daydream about where I would retire when I finished this job. It was probably the greatest moment of my life. Unfortunately, followed by the worst. Once we had filled our cargo holds, we started to align our ships for warp. It was then that they hit us. They came from nowhere and warp scrambled our industrials and jammed the two merc ships escorting us. They demanded over half of our cargo. We debated. But before we could give an answer, they attacked. Half the expedition was wiped out, including some of my closest friends. The ones who survived were told to go back to camp and relay our story to the rest of the miners and harvesters, so that the next time one of our expeditions runs into the Guristas we follow their orders immediately. Now I just want to leave this dreadful place, I knew I took a huge risk by coming here but now that I''ve seen the face of death ... I just don''t think I have it in me anymore. I know some of the families of my colleagues who perished on that fateful day, and I would like their bodies returned to me so that I can bring them back to Caldari space for proper burial. If you''re up for the job, I''ll give you a bookmark to the deadspace area where they lost their lives. You should be able to find the wreckage of their ships there. You''ll probably have to navigate through at least two pockets though to find all of them, once the Guristas attacked we tried to flee via the acceleration gates there, some of us only made it past one gate before being mowed down.'),
(93269,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Distribution',500010,16796,5,'Seek and destroy the Guristas commander Piran Keitosa within the Guristas complex at -0.1 W8O-19. (Low Sec Warning!)','Your success in the last mission has given me some hope. Perhaps my comrades can be avenged. The captain of the Guristas gang which attacked us is still at large. But some of my people have tracked him down, and I have the coordinates to his hideout. I will give you these coordinates, if you promise to destroy him and anyone under his command. You will receive a reward, of course.'),
(93270,0,5,25273,20,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Trade',500001,0,0,'Trade 20x Golden Cytoserocin (200 m3)',''),
(93271,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Security',500001,16796,5,'Warp to the Guristas constellation headquarters and deliver Lauka''s message to their leaders. Location 1QH-0K ({{ColorSecurityRating','Your observation is correct. And I''ve been watching you, <Pilot>, for a while now, and you seem to fit the criteria I''ve been looking for. Now I have a task for you that may prove to be extremely dangerous. As you probably know already we''ve had a long standing quarrel with the Guristas forces in 09-4XW. And it''s really showing a toll on the settlers here. But I want to propose a truce, and I want you to be the one that brings them the offer. I will supply you a bookmark to the Guristas Headquarters in 1QH-0K, all you have to do is warp in there and bring it to their leaders.'),
(93272,0,3,17245,1,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Security',500010,16796,5,'Acquire 1x Dread Guristas Diamond Tag (0.1 m³)','You are, huh. Unfortunately there is only one way to truly stop the Guristas from enslaving us, at least temporarily. And that is to annihilate their high command in 1QH-0K. I know it sounds foolhardy and it probably is, but it''s the only way ... if we don''t strike them down at the root they will just keep on coming. I''m probably getting way ahead of myself here, I really can''t ask you to try something insane like assault their most powerful stronghold in the entire constellation. But if you do, I will give you a very nice reward for the insignia from their leader.'),
(93273,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500010,16796,5,'Eradicate the Guristas presence near the acceleration gate leading into the Gas Cloud site, then report back to Nuomo Kaavunin in Pioneer''s Sanctuary.','I''m in a bit of a dilemma at the moment. I managed to find an area of deadspace filled with lucrative gas clouds, but as always there was a catch. The Guristas had apparently erected an outpost next to an acceleration gate leading directly into the deadspace pocket containing the clouds. I haven''t detected any signs of them actually harvesting the gas, but I dare not try to enter the area with them nearby. Could you please remove their presence for me?'),
(93274,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Encounter',500001,16796,5,'Loot the scanner data, Nuomo''s Scanner Data (0.1{{m3','Hmmm, yes there is one more thing. I have a long range scanner in I1-BE8 which I use to look for promising sites which may harbor harvestable gas clouds. The problem is I''m afraid of going back there and retrieving the data, the last time I tried I noticed a couple pirates nearby who I thought might be waiting in ambush. Anyway I don''t want to take any chances, but if you''re willing then I''ll pay you for getting me the data. This is an important mission, which will have significant impact on your faction standings.'),
(93275,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Security',500010,16796,5,'Destroy most of the Guristas invasion force to deter them from attacking Pioneer''s Sanctuary.','Have I got any? Are you mad? I''ve been sitting here all day looking for contractors with some combat experience. Now I need someone I can rely on for this job, and I have to say I''m impressed with the way you''ve dealt with some of your previous assignments for Caldari agents. So maybe you''re cut out for this ... Anyway, I''ve been informed that a few gangs of Guristas scoundrels have decided to attempt a full scale assault on our little town here. Inside sources tell me that they are not working for the core Guristas leadership in 09-4XW, so they won''t be as deadly and organized as I first feared. But they''re still a major threat, and as such I need someone to take care of ''em. If you can do the job, in other words take ''em out before they reach Pioneer''s Sanctuary, then I''ll reward you generously. It so happens that I know where one of their stopping points will be, I will give you the coordinates of course.'),
(93276,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Security',500010,16796,5,'Destroy the Guristas Relay Station.','Now I''d like you to target a Guristas Relay Station in ZH3-BS which has been transmitting orders to dozens of pirate gangs in 09-4XW. They''re the top dogs in this system, and get their information directly from the Guristas high command. By taking them out we will be dealing a serious blow to their plans. I will give you the coordinates, of course. This is an important mission, which will have significant impact on your faction standings.'),
(93277,0,5,25273,20,0,'COSMOS Caldari COSMOS / Trade',500001,0,0,'Trade 20x Golden Cytoserocin (200 m3)',''),
(93278,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','Something just came up that''s right up your alley. My name is Jannegiers Estacan, and I''m the Chief Indoctrination Officer for the Friends of Nature in this area. I bring new recruits in and teach them all about the wonders of nature and how awful the corporate behemoth is ... as the 12th Prophet put it, "trying to put an ISK sign" on everything that grows naturally in this splendid universe of ours. I also oversee most of the supplies that come to and from our fair little seminary. As a matter of fact, I have something on my desk right now that requires the attention of someone fast and competent. Couldn''t help but notice that fine-looking vessel you''re flying there. One of our fertilizer shipments was ambushed yesterday, and we need someone to replace what''s missing. If you can find us 100 units of fertilizer, we''d be much obliged.'),
(93279,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','Yes, I have something for you. Great job with the fertilizer. My thanks. Next up, we have a shortage of wheat on one of our outposts on Parchanier IV. There''s been a bit of a mix-up, it seems: A shipment of Quafe Ultra went to the planet instead of the wheat, and now those poor people have nothing to make their bread with. If you could pop over to the Egonics Inc. Development Studio at Parchanier V and deliver this wheat to them, you''d be greatly aiding the FON''s cause in this area.'),
(93280,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','I have just the thing you want. Good news! One of our teams has just pulled off a major coup against the Wiyrkomi corporation in the Augnais system. They''ve managed to intercept the third shipment in a row of batteries for the workers'' personal electronic entertainment systems. Things are at boiling point over there already, and I wouldn''t be surprised if we saw a mutiny there sometime in the near future. We need someone to go grab the batteries, though, so we can put them to good use and absolve our people in the area of any suspicions, should the powers that be decide to conduct a hangar search. Head over to the Pend Insurance Investment Bank in Augnais and grab the batteries for me, and we''ll reward you well.'),
(93281,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','Yes, I have something for you. This is kind of strange. I''ve just been handed a shipment of small arms that is supposedly bound for an outpost of ours in the Deltole system. I''m not sure what this means, but the shipping slip seems correct. I''ll have to get in touch with my superiors about this - we shouldn''t be ferrying weapons around. Something fishy might be going on here. Should you decide you want to take this job, the small arms will be placed in your cargo hold and since I know you''ll remain quiet about this, I''m going to throw in a little something special as a reward this time.'),
(93282,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','Sure, I''ve got something. Here''s the deal. I''m a senior journalist for the Scope, and I''m working on an in-depth piece about the Wiyrkomi project in this constellation and the FON''s (Friends of Nature''s) struggle to counteract their plans. It''s a big piece, and I have several reporters working on different strands in different places, so assistance from a fast-moving capsule pilot such as yourself is always needed. As a matter of fact, I have a job for you right now if you want it. One of my reporters just completed a few interviews with Colelie project workers who are on break from the project at the Wiyrkomi Factory in Fluekele. He says he managed to get some juicy tidbits from them about the way Wiyrkomi handles its workers; grist for the cause, to mangle a metaphor. Bring me back the interview transcripts from Fluekele, and I''ll pay you as much as the agency allows me to dole out. How about it?'),
(93283,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','Here is a mission suited for someone of your caliber. It seems the Wiyrkomi Corporation isn''t being entirely forthcoming when it comes to their labor practices. That was some very interesting material you brought back from Fluekele. So good, in fact, that I feel a sudden, almost physical urge to follow up on it. One of my top reporters just came in from Oursulaert. I want you to take him to the Wiyrkomi factory in Jolia, where some highly classified contacts are waiting for him. Since Wiyrkomi won''t give us the straight dope, we''re going to have to turn to alternative sources. I''ll find out the truth yet. Take my guy to Jolia and I''ll see to it that you''re rewarded handsomely.'),
(93284,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','Yes, I have something for you. Something fishy''s going on here. Word just came in over the feednet: apparently, a FON strike squad staged an attack on a surveillance outpost in Colelie belonging to Temko, a mercenary organization contracted by Wiyrkomi to protect their holdings and help them gain a foothold in this constellation. This doesn''t feel right at all. First, FON doesn''t engage in out-and-out terrorism; their battles take place on politico-ideological fronts. Second, had it been FON, why would they advertise that fact? Their tactic is the swaying of public opinion, not the destruction of their opponents'' assets. This has all the hallmarks of a frame-up. An old friend of mine who''s well-connected in this area says he''s managed to obtain the data core from one of the attacking ships'' computers as it was brought in by salvager vessels. If we can get it into the hands of our specialists here, they might be able to extract some clues regarding the attackers'' real identities and intentions. Head out to Parchanier and get me that data core. A lot may be riding on this.'),
(93285,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','Here is a mission suited for someone of your caliber. Okay, it''s about to hit the fan. We''ve stumbled on to something very very bad indeed. It''s so bad, in fact, that I''m not even going to come close to covering it in my article. The people behind this cannot know, under any circumstances, that we know about their plans. I can''t tell you any more at this moment, but I''ll tell you what I can do. I''m going to ask you for one more favor, and then I''m going to give you a contact within the FON. They have some work they need done, and since they''re generally not the travelling types they could use a big strapping capsuleer to help them. But first I need to ask you one more favor. I''ve collected the data I''ve accrued in the making of my article into one dossier, which I need brought to a safe place. Word''s just reached us that Wiyrkomi have this place under wraps, so I''ve become compromised. I''ll have to jack in and do the rest of this remotely. Bring my dossier to my contact in Parchanier, and I''ll hand over our analysis of the evidence you got for us. It''s bad, friend. It''s real bad. ---- Mission completed: Good work. I''m glad I found you. Take this data chip. On it, you will find evidence that the Wiyrkomi corporation have been engaging in terrorism against themselves in order to shift the public''s opinion regarding both them and FON. It''s not absolutely 100 percent reliable, but what there is seems solid enough. Bring this chip to Preaux Gallot in the Natura Seminary in Audaerne. There is more to be done yet, and I have a feeling this is all just beginning. Thank you for all your help. You''ve done us a great service.'),
(93286,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','First of all, do you have something for me...? If you know what I''m talking about, then hand it over, please. If you don''t, then I''m sorry, but I don''t have anything for you.'),
(93287,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','Something just came up that''s right up your alley. First, a proper introduction. I''m Preaux Gallot, one of FON''s chief coordinators in this area. As you may know, the Wiyrkomi corporation is trying to move into this area, corrupting the vast tracts of natural beauty found here with their horrible industry. Moreover, the piece of evidence you just brought me seems to indicate there are things at play here far worse than we originally suspected. It appears the Wiyrkomi corporation has been hiring mercenaries to stage attacks on their own outposts in the area, attacks which they then frame us for in order to lessen our stature in the public eye. We need to put a stop to this as soon as possible. If we lose our lobbyist support, the Federation is likely to succumb to the deals being proffered by the corrupt Caldari business machine, and this entire area will be turned into just another locale for these corporate bigwigs to ravage. An operative of ours, Suho Tatanal, has just returned from a protest on Parchanier II. He''s a canny investigator with an eye for details; I want you to bring him the aggregated evidence we''ve gathered on the case so far, then report back to me. I''ll have another assignment for you very soon.'),
(93288,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','I have just the thing you want. Okay, Suho''s gears have started turning. The evidence you brought him helped greatly. His investigation will be a tremendous boon in our struggle against the corporate monster. We''ll have to wait a while to see what he comes up with. I''m not worried about him, though; he works magic when he gets going. While we wait, <Character>, I have another job for you. Our organization is staging a massive protest tomorrow in the Wiyrkomi Corporation Factory in Jolia, but there seems to have been a slight miscommunication between some of our activists. If you could hop over to the Pend Insurance Investment Bank in Augnais and bring a few bags of fedo blood over to the Wiyrkomi station in Jolia, the Friends of Nature would be much obliged.'),
(93289,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','Here is a mission suited for someone of your caliber. You''ve proven yourself a trustworthy operative, <Character>, so I''m going to give you an assignment slightly more clandestine than the ones you''ve gotten from me so far. Technically speaking, we''re going to be breaking the law here, but I trust you realize we''re doing what we''re doing for a higher cause. Okay, that said, here goes. We just received word from our man on the inside that Wiyrkomi have just ordered 15 high-powered drills for their prospecting operations on Fluekele V, a planet home to many unique, highly endangered varieties of flora and fauna. The drills are currently sitting at the Wiyrkomi factory in Fluekele, awaiting transport to the site where they''re intended to be used. Our operatives at Fluekele have managed, through their connections with sympathetic station personnel, to pilfer these tools, but we can''t keep them hidden for long. We need someone to get the drills safely out to our people in the Poteque station in Augnais. Head out there and show me how devoted to our cause you truly are.'),
(93290,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','Yes, I have something for you. Something urgent just landed on my desk. One of our industrial ships, carrying a load of soil intended for our reservations on Deltole, was shot down yesterday with no survivors. We need to get some soil over there soon, or a large part of our efforts in the area will be wasted. Looks like Wiyrkomi are using our alleged aggression against them as an excuse to gun down innocent people whose aims they don''t agree with. Can''t say I''m surprised, frankly, although I wouldn''t have thought they''d go this far. Bring 200 units of soil to me, and you will have done us a great service.'),
(93291,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','For you, my friend, there''s always something. Suho has made a lot of headway in his investigation, and the results are disturbing as all hell. What I''m about to tell you is for your ears only. I want to make that absolutely clear. It appears the attacks we''ve been hearing about against Wiyrkomi assets are not being staged by Wiyrkomi themselves, as we originally suspected. The most recent threads of Suho''s investigation are, in fact, pointing squarely toward members of our own organization. I regret to say this, but it appears we have a vigilante rogue in our midst, someone who obviously has no conception of the harm he could be doing to our cause. Furthermore, there''s compelling evidence to the effect that this party, whoever he or she is, have been in contact with the Serpentis smugglers operating in this area, conspiring to strike against Wiyrkomi assets, murdering people in order to further our cause. Makes me feel dirty just thinking about it. This weed in our garden needs to be rooted out, but first we need to learn its identity. The information is being held by Suho at his office in Parchanier. Needless to say, it''s far too sensitive to be sent over normal channels, so I need someone I can trust to head out there and bring it back to me. That means you. We need to straighten this situation out, post-haste. And remember, not a peep about this to anyone.'),
(93292,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','Nice to meet you. My name is Ystvia Lamuette, and I''m one of the chief coordinators of FON''s activities in this constellation. Preaux tells me great things about you; apparently you can be of great help in our struggle. I''d like to get a feel for you myself, nonetheless. Show me how fast you can be. There''s a rare specimen of plant, a Colelian spider spruce, sitting in the Core Complexion Warehouse at Deltole. Bring it back to me within 15 minutes and I''ll reward you handsomely. Then we can talk about what needs to be done for our organization.'),
(93293,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','Nice work on the spider spruce. So here''s the situation, then. There''s a guy named Alarus Ekire. He''s the most militant person within our ranks - a real piece of work. Most of us have disagreed with his methods in the past, but he has an authoritative air about him which rouses admiration in the weak. For this reason he''s never short of followers, and has managed to maintain his position within FON. It has now been brought to our attention, due in no small part to your diligent work, that Ekire is the weed in our garden, the one that''s been causing all this trouble in the past few weeks. We have to get rid of him, but we can''t kill him. If the Wiyrkomi spin doctors have the opportunity to make him into a figurehead, we''re finished. So we need to try and smoke him out, lure him into revealing himself. We need to lay the groundwork first, though, and try to undo some of the damage he''s caused. First off, we need to send the clear-cut message that FON do not wish to cast their lot with known cutthroats and murderers. To this end, we need to put our own propaganda machine to work. There is a Serpentis outpost in one of the outlying systems. According to our intel, no detachments are stationed there at present. I want you to head out there, destroy the outpost, neutralize any opposition you may find, and report back to me. One of our other operatives will shadow you to the area and record the attack, so we can spin this to our advantage and hopefully countermand any bad publicity. Go to it. Good luck.'),
(93294,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','The photographer who recorded your strike has given his footage to the post-production people. We should see something from them soon. We''ve decided there''s no choice but to take the Ekire matter into our own hands. According to our intelligence, he has something like four hundred men under his command, conducting his terrorist operations. Some of them are our own FON activists, others are mercenaries - Navy rejects, working for the highest bidder. The Deltole system is a key tactical location; many of Ekire''s mercs are stationed at an outpost there, and we have solid reports that they''re preparing to stage some sort of attack on the Wiyrkomi factory there. This must not be allowed to happen. We need you to conduct a pre-emptive strike on the outpost, eliminating any personnel you find in the vicinity. As you''re not flying under our flag, there should be nothing linking you to the FON, and indeed there can''t be - we would never survive the political backlash. Please know that we don''t undertake the killing of people lightly. It''s our hope that this is the greatly lesser of two evils. Report back to me when the deed is done. I''ll be here.'),
(93295,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','We need to move fast. The situation is evolving in unexpected ways. No no, don''t sit down. I''ll explain this as fast as I can. While you were out on your last assignment, Ekire himself was mortally wounded in an assassination attempt by unknown assailants. We suspect Wiyrkomi, of course - they have the most to gain from his death, both politically and pragmatically speaking. Likewise, if he dies we stand to take a massive political blow. Ekire is currently at the Egonics Inc. Development Studio at Parchanier V, bleeding severely and fading fast. Due to a rare blood condition he contracted in an Umokkan jungle while serving as a Legion marine a decade back, transfusion via normal means would kill him. For the procedure to be at all possible he needs an aortal purifier, a seldom-used piece of medical equipment which they don''t have at that particular station''s med bay. I need you to head out to Auderne immediately, to the Poteque Pharmaceuticals Biotech Production plant there, and pick up what may be the only aortal purifier available in this whole damn constellation, then bring it out to the doctors in Parchanier. His life - and our success in our campaign here - may very well depend on your speed in this matter. Go! Fly swiftly.'),
(93296,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','Alarus Ekire is safe and sound, thanks to you. We''ve uncovered solid evidence of what he''s been up to in the sector, and we''re making arrangements to have him delivered to the proper authorities safe and sound. There''s only one loose end that needs tying up, after which we can go back to business as usual, sticking it to the man. You see, I have this large shipment of wheat here that desperately needs to get dumped in the cogs of the Wiyrkomi station in Fluekele… *grins wickedly* How about it, friend? ---- Completed: The Friends of Nature extend their thanks to you for your help in this whole situation. You''ve been a tremendous asset to our organization. Thanks to you, we''ll be able to continue our struggle to help the natural wonders of Algintal remain just that.'),
(93297,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','Do you have something for me? A letter, perhaps?'),
(93298,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','Great to hear that. Now the first task I have for you is pretty dangerous. We were expecting a large group of tourists here from Du Annes today but unfortunately their cruiser''s warp-drive broke down in Deltole. On top of that they stumbled into a deadspace pocket filled with rogue drones. The last we heard of them was their distress signal indicating they were under attack. I can only hope that they managed to escape, but at this time it''s impossible to tell. I would like you to fly into the deadspace pocket where they were last seen and search for them. Destroy every rogue drone ship that you find. If they are still alive they might need some help repairing their warp-drive, if not then they at least would need help fighting off the drones. Good luck. ---- Mission completed: You''ve done us a great favor, <Character>. The captain of the pleasure cruiser managed to contact us shortly after you finished your objective, and informed us that they were safe and on their way here. Their deaths would have been terrible publicity for the Information Center ...'),
(93299,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','The next mission in line is rather simple. A Federal Intelligence officer is scheduled to inspect our outpost this week. He was supposed to arrive later today but his ship was delayed. The Federal Intelligence Office demanded that we provide him with a quick transport so that he is able to complete his assignment on time. My take on this entire situation is that they did this on purpose just to see how far we''re willing to go to please Federation authorities. Now, considering that you completed your last assignment with flying colors I assume this will be a piece of cake for someone of your caliber. Just pick up the FIO officer at Eglennaert I - Moon 4 - Federal Intelligence Office Logistic Support and get him back here as quickly as possible. Dismissed.'),
(93300,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','Now that you''ve finished the most pressing tasks I have, it''s time to send my report to Miloise Roden in the Roden Shipyard headquarters. It contains some pretty sensitive information, so I want it kept safe and secure until it''s in the hangar of Alentene VI - Moon 6 - Roden Shipyards Warehouse. Don''t mess this up! Dismissed. ---- Completed: You''ve done all I''ve asked you to, with style. I suggest you take a look at the Wiyrkomi Survey Station in Colelie or the Command Center in Fluekele if you''re in need of some more work. Good luck!'),
(93301,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','<Character>! Please help me. My friend, Isone Flosin, has gone missing. We were just cruising around on our shuttles within the inner areas of this complex when we were attacked by rogue drones! I managed to escape, but in my haste I didn''t notice that Isone had stopped following me. I need to know what happened to her, and my ship is in no shape to venture back in there. Please, you have to help me. Find Isone and bring her back! ---- Mission completed:<br> How horrible! I never thought something like this could happen here. I don''t know how I will be able to face her parents, they told us never to venture any further into the complex than the first area but we just couldn''t resist. I''m so ashamed ... Could you at least talk to Isone''s father, in the Central Administration complex in Fluekele. Tell him I sent you, Isone''s DNA will prove that. Please tell him the whole story, I''m just too traumatized at the moment to meet him myself. Thank you.'),
(93302,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','Have you seen my daughter, Isone Flosin, by any chance? She went missing some time ago while inside the Roden Shipyard Outpost in Fluekele. If you find her, tell her I''m very displeased and she should come see me immediately. I heard Nilla Elermare was asking about Isone, too. You may want to start by talking to her.'),
(93303,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','Isone must be avenged. The Serpentis must be responsible for her death. We''ve catered to their needs for far too long. I couldn''t believe my ears when they told me we were supposed to treat the Serpentis living in the outpost as comrades! But enough of this rambling, back to the mission at hand. I want you to infiltrate the Corelum Drughouse again and look for clues which might lead to whoever is behind her death. I know of one person who might know, he serves as a guard at the Serpentis storage facility inside that deadspace area. His name is Jark something. Good luck.'),
(93304,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','While I interrogate the prisoner, I would like you to bring Isone''s things to her mother on Jel I - Roden Shipyards Warehouse as well as a note from me describing the situation. I am simply too busy to make the trip myself anytime soon, and I know she will manage to find some comfort in receiving Isone''s things as a memento of her short life. Everything you need to transport is in these sealed containers. Take care not to lose any, they might not be very valuable on the market but to me and my wife they are priceless.'),
(93305,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','I''ve managed to extract the information I needed out of poor Jark. It seems that my Isone was accidentally killed by ''rogue'' drone ships guarding the Serpentis drug storage area. Now I cannot really blame a computer for her death, but I can blame it''s creators. In fact these drones are not ''rogue'' at all, they are just programmed to act like them. An ingenious gallente scientist working for the Serpentis actually managed to reprogram these rogue drones to serve Salvador Sarpati and his wild schemes. The Federation Navy also tends to ignore areas infested with rogue drones, which is beneficial to the Serpentis. Fortunately Jark knew of a Serpentis science lab in Colelie which is behind all of the drones in the Roden Shipyard complex. I want this science lab destroyed. Whoever resides in there is undoubtedly responsible for Isone''s death, and must pay the ultimate price.'),
(93306,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','Ok, I''m here on official business from Federal Intelligence Office. I was sent here to inspect the Central Command station of Wiyrkomi in Algintal, and as a side project keep an eye out on Roden Shipyards, who''ve been Wiyrkomi''s primary allies in Federation space. Now my first objective is to make sure there isn''t any illegal trade going on here. I haven''t been able to discover any contraband during my stay here, but I''d like to test something before I fill my first report. I''d like to see how well prepared the Temko mercenaries guarding this installation are concerning illegal goods. So I want somebody inconspicuous to try to infiltrate the compound with drugs inside of his cargo hold. You look like just the person for that assignment. You''ll find the drugs on Decon VI - Moon 10 - Federal Intelligence Office Assembly Plant, simply grab them and bring them to me. Federation customs officials won''t touch you, they know it''s my crash. Temko don''t however, hence the test. If you get attacked by Temko, then flee and come back later, I''ll explain everything to them once the test is complete.'),
(93307,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','For your second assignment I''d like you to investigate a Wiyrkomi storage facility in Jolia. I stumbled upon some documents revealing it''s location while inside the Central Command control tower. They were a bit startled when I informed them of what I had discovered, so I''m thinking something fishy might be afloat there. I will upload a bookmark into your journal which sends you to a deadspace pocket. Inside you''ll find this storage facility. Take a look inside, and tell me what you find. Thanks. ---- Completed: So they replaced the sign on the acceleration gate leading to the storage facility with one leading to a drone hive? This will go straight into my report. I''ll also take a look at this data chip you found in the storage facility itself, but I''m sure there''s nothing of interest inside it. If they knew you were coming and managed to replace the sign on the acceleration gates, they probably had enough time to empty the storage containers as well. But good work anyway.'),
(93308,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','It''s now time to turn our eyes towards Roden Shipyards. They have always been a shady corporation, and their alliance with Wiyrkomi certainly raised a few eyebrows. I was specifically told to find out exactly what part they play in all of this. Yesterday I stumbled upon something that may be of vital importance to my investigation. My ship''s sensors picked up an encoded transmission from a Roden Shipyards outpost located in Fluekele. I haven''t been able to make much of it yet, but with the proper data decoder I will be able to tell what the contents of this transmission are. So my assignment to you is to find such a decoder and bring it to me. My suggestion is to scour the asteroid belts of Jolia, there is a Serpentis agent there called Pourpas Aunten who is renowned for decoding CONCORD and Federation Navy signals. If there''s anyone in the galaxy which has the decoder I need, it''s him.'),
(93309,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','I''ve managed to decode the transmission but I can''t make much of it. The interesting part though is that it originates from Maqeri Camcen''s ship within the Contested Gallente Roden Shipyard Outpost. I checked my database and Maqeri is in fact rumored to be part of the Angel Cartel. What the Cartel would be doing in a Roden Shipyard Outpost in Fluekele is beyond me, unless there are Serpentis there. My best guess is that there are Serpentis operating inside the same deadspace are as Roden Shipyard, and this Maqeri is some sort of envoy from the Cartel. Anyway I must get to the bottom of this. Meet with this Maqeri fellow and see if you can convince him to have a chat with me in person. If he''s hostile and refuses to speak with you then you have my full authority to eliminate him. If you choose the gun rather than your wit, then at least bring evidence of his demise to me. Dismissed.'),
(93310,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','Now that I''ve finished my report, I''d like you to transport it to my boss on Decon VI - Moon 10 - Federal Intelligence Office Assembly Plant. The information inside is confidential, so please do not even think about reading the document. Once the report is safely in the hands of my superiors, then you will have your reward. Good luck.'),
(93311,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','I have just the thing you want. My name''s Astroo Opeau, and I''m FON''s propaganda honcho. I could have some hoity-toity title, sure, but I like to keep things down-to-earth and formalities just get in the way. I have a few things I could use a big strapping capsuleer like you for, if you''re interested. Tidbits of information are in constant swirl around this constellation, like electrons in an atom, and we need to cast as many nets as far and wide as possible if we want to stand a chance against the corporate behemoth of Wiyrkomi. One of my eyes in the Audaerne system just got a recording of one of Wiyrkomi''s brass indulging in some, shall we say, languorous activities in a pleasure resort not far from here. Head over to the Modern Finances Investment Bank in Audaerne and pick up the tape for me, and we''ll see what we can do with it.'),
(93312,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','have just the thing you want. The tape you brought back of the Wiyrkomi scumbag proved ideal for our purposes. We''ve made a holoreel of the "incident," and we need it copied and distributed to key points in the constellation so we can mount a full-scale broadcast offensive against the bastard. Take this holoreel over to my distributor in the Fluekele system. We''ll see how big a shot the bigshot is after this.'),
(93313,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','Yes, I have something for you. Well, our little gambit worked. The bigwig''s been driven out of Wiyrkomi and a blow''s been struck for the little guy. Thanks so much for your help. One last favor, if you will. Some of our guys are founding an environmentalist education facility on Deltole III - Moon 1 - Core Complexion Inc. Warehouse and they need some construction materials brought over. You think you could do this for me? I''ll pay you well.'),
(93314,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','I was sent here by Roden Shipyards to help gather ore for Wiyrkomi''s construction workers in the Survey Station. They''re hoarding up minerals and ore for the eventual construction of the power plant in Azure Canyon. The only problem is I''m not much of a combat pilot and I didn''t expect there to be such an abundance of pirates festering the asteroid belts in Colelie. So I was thinking, maybe you could help me out a little? I''ll split the earnings I would have received for doing the same job with you. What do you say, <Character>?'),
(93315,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','Your second job is to get me 4 portions of Omber, or 2000 units to be exact. You might find it a bit difficult to find that type or ore around these parts, but you''re in luck. I know of a great spot to mine some. You see I was in Fluekele a few days ago scouting for some ore, this is before I decided the job was too dangerous for me, and I managed to stumble upon a small cluttering of asteroids in the middle of nowhere. And lo and behold, there was an asteroid brimming with minerals, which on closer inspection was Omber! Unfortunately as soon as I had discovered this magnificent find, a group of Serpentis who had been following me attacked. I believe they were being led by that scoundrel Ansedon Blat, I could be wrong though. I met him while I was at the Roden Shipyards Outpost in Fluekele, and he must have decided to follow me when I left on my expedition. That backstabber and his goons must pay. On second thought, I''m not satisfied with just getting the omber. You''ll have to kill those Serpentis bastards too, if you find them. Return to me with the omber when you''re done.'),
(93316,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','Ok, my boss is located in our warehouse in Ane. Just drop this report at his desk and he''ll wire the payment to my account. I''ll give you something in return for your efforts as well. Just some items that I think you might find useful, and frankly I have no need of. Take it or leave it.'),
(93317,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Distribution <!-- Distribution is a agent division, not a mission type. Needs to be changed -->',500004,0,0,'Acquire "Threaded Waypoint Map" and return this to the agent.','I am a professor of archaeology at the University of Caille. Behind this ancient gate beside me you will find one of the most fascinating enigmas in existence. It is a small and seemingly insignificant object, but one that holds massive powers. The origin of this relic is still vague, though most now agree that it was built by the Yan Jung nation. Perhaps you''ve heard of it? The Yan Jung nation immigrated into our world through the EVE Gate eons ago. From where, we do not know, though the fragments of texts we''ve managed to translate talk about a mysterious middle kingdom. They settled here in Deltole, though we suspect they also colonized other systems, even in far off places. But what we''ve uncovered so far is here in the Deltole system, especially on Deltole V and VI, which seem to have been much more inhabitable back then. So what happened to the Yan Jung nation, you must be wondering? Simply told, we don''t know yet. Heck, I''m not even sure what the relic I just described to you was used for. I''ve been studying it for months and still its purpose eludes me. It has some sort of a repelling force that''s almost impenetrable. It also has regeneration mechanics and perpetual power source, meaning it''s as good as eternal. What the Yan Jung built it for, or used it for, is a complete mystery. Unfortunately, the Serpentis pirates have taken an interest in Yan Jung relics too. They''ve sent out dozens of treasure hunters and scavengers. They don''t tolerate others to interfere with their efforts, which explains why I''m hiding out here instead of being at the relic studying it. The Serpentis periodically send expeditions here and are always scouting the place. Their methods are crude, but they''ve got much more manpower and resources than I can ever dream of having. I''ve heard rumors that they''ve uncovered an important piece of the biggest riddle surrounding the Yan Jung nation. Over at Deltole X, close to the stargate leading to Colelie, is the entrance point to a Yan Jung site that is possibly the largest Yan Jung ruins in space still in existence. I can only imagine what riches might await there. The only problem is that a passkey is needed to activate the gate. And from what I''ve heard the Serpentis are now in possession of one of the key elements in constructing one. You look like an energetic pilot. I''m interested in hiring you for a bit of work. The Serpentis relic hunters are operating from a base within the Skeleton Comet site here in Deltole. I haven''t been there myself, but somewhere within it you''ll find a Serpentis Survey Site, which is the right place. Therein the Serpentis store all the data and items they''ve found throughout the whole constellation. What I want you to search for is a map of some sort. I''m sorry for being so vague, but that''s all the info I have. I''m sure you''ll know what I want as soon as you see it. There''s only one problem. The Serpentis are a paranoid lot, and they''ve encrypted all their data and storage containers. I hope you possess some hacking skills, or know someone that does, for that is what is required to get to the information I need. Get that map from the Serpentis and bring it to me and I will reward you handsomely. I feel dirty having to resort to petty theft, but when you''re up against scumbags such as the Serpentis the only way to play a fair game is to follow their rules.'),
(93318,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Distribution',500004,0,0,'Aquire "Yan Jung Micro Processor"','The map you got me is only one piece in the puzzle of getting into the hidden relic site. You remember what I told you about that strange device that lies behind this gate beside me? It is of Yan Jung origin and I believe it can give us another vital puzzle piece. In order for me to construct a usable passkey to enter the relic site I need to understand better how the Yan Jung nation approached technology. The force repeller has a micro processor, which would give me just those insights. I am a hopeless fighter, so I don''t stand a chance against the Serpentis ruffians in there. I need someone of your capabilities to get the micro processor for me. So what you need to do is enter the Yan Jung ruins through the gate beside me. Take out the Serpentis scouts and proceed to tackle the force repeller. You can''t get close to it while it''s still active, so you need to shoot it from a distance. Once it blows up get the micro processor quickly before the regeneration nano-bots kick in and rebuild the repeller. Oh, and one more thing. The Serpentis periodically send expeditions to the ruins. I hope you don''t run into them, but if you do make sure you have plenty of firepower on your side.'),
(93319,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Distribution',500004,0,0,'Aquire "Binary Transpositional Code" and return it to the agent.','The Yan Jung were more clever than I gave them credit for, it seems. The micro processor is highly advanced and my analytical methods are limited in cracking its secrets. However, what little information I''ve managed to glean from the processor gives me hope that we can still solve this mystery. The encryption methods employed by the Yan Jung nation are in many ways similar to those used by a new strand of rogue drones that a colleague of mine have told me exist in this very constellation. My guess is that the rogue drones happened upon some lost Yan Jung artifact here in Algintal and in assimilating it learned some new tricks. But however it happened is beside the point. What really matters is that the local pirates that frequent the asteroid belts here in Algintal have been harassing this new breed of drones out of fear it will grow to become too powerful for them to handle. And as pirates usually do, they loot those they destroy. This colleague of mine has been doing a research on this new rogue drone breed and he tells me that the drones have developed a sophisticated binary code to interact with the Yan Jung technology they assimilated. My theory is that if we get this binary code we can use it to unravel the mysteries of the micro processor in my possession. In doing so we should have no problem in constructing a useable passkey. And the belt pirates, having hunted the new drones so excessively, are certain to possess this binary code. In essence, I want you to go into the asteroid belts and hunt down belt pirates. From what I''ve heard the Serpentis are employing tough marauders to hunt the rogue drones, so your best bet is to focus on them. Return to me once you have the binary code and I will construct a passkey that you can use.'),
(93320,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','Something just came up that''s right up your alley. Hi there, stranger. I''m Croir Arghe, and I''m in charge of what we like to affectionately call FON''s guerilla wing. Not for anyone, what I have. No sirree. We''ve received some information recently that gives us reason to believe Wiyrkomi are up to some very clandestine things in this sector. In light of that, we''re planning to mount a large offensive against a Wiyrkomi mercenary outpost in the Colelie system. Now, this is not something that''s technically sanctioned by the top tiers of FON''s command structure, but a certain portion of us feel that this must be done anyway. If you have a hauler handy and are willing to help with the logistics of this endeavor, I can pay you very well. Just keep quiet about it, OK? First off, I need some recon speeders brought to Deltole. There''s quite a large amount of them, so you''ll need a good deal of cargo space. Are you up to it?'),
(93321,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','Here is a mission suited for someone of your caliber. Preparations for the attack are going well, but a slight problem has presented itself. The squadron we have stationed in Fluekele has run out of rocket fuel for their ground-based missile systems. This doesn''t bode well for the offensive, so if you could head over to Audaerne, grab the supplies we have there and bring them over to Fluekele, we would much appreciate it.'),
(93322,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','Something just came up that''s right up your alley. We are almost ready for the offensive. Only one thing is missing. The squadron spearheading the attack is going to be mounting custom-built guidance systems, ones which will give them an unsurpassed ability to track ground-based targets on a flyby. We''ve had top engineers working on these systems for a while now, and they were finally completed yesterday. Go get the finished batch from Barmalie and bring it to Deltole, and we will be ready for our strike.'),
(93323,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500004,0,0,'','You don''t know what FON stands for?! Friends of Nature of course! We ... errr they stand for everything that''s good about the Federation. Originating from a group battling to save rare animal species from extinction, it has grown somewhat after space travel became more common. Now it also fights for the preservation of the natural phenomena which decorate our night sky. Now you said you were looking for some work. As a matter of fact there is something that you could do for me which would really make my day. Temko are evil corporate peons who care nothing for our heritage, the Azure Canyon. They work for a no-good money-grubbing Caldari corporation which intends to destroy our natural reserves for its own gain. It so happens that one of Temko''s commanders, Maschteri Markan, had the audacity to try and blackmail us when we sabotaged one of Wiyrkomi''s construction sites, where they were building a survey station. He recorded the event and threatened to release it to The Scope and the Federation authorities if we wouldn''t give in to his demands. Find these records and bring them to me, or somehow convince him to hand them over himself, and I will reward you generously. I suggest you refrain from accepting this mission if you have no idea how hard finding Maschteri is. Otherwise you might be in for a rude awakening. ---- Mission completed: I didn''t tell you to kill him! I''m ready to die for my beliefs, but I won''t take part in cold-blooded murder! I guess I owe you your reward, but this is the last time I''ll do business with you, <Character>. You''re a bad, bad man.'),
(93324,0,3,12538,30,5,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Security',500004,11076,5,'30x Serpentis Silver Tag','We have a policy here within the Gallente Federation that our more prominent members fly a suitable ship according to their status, both to give them an edge during combat and to uphold our image, especially within our borders. We have recently decided to extend this benefit to mercenaries or freelancers employed by us that have shown admirable bravery and skill in the field, or earned the right through countless hours of dedicated service to our corporations. As you undoubtedly already know I have been assigned the task of allocating these ships to their deserved owners. After looking at your record, we decided that you, <Character Name>, are worthy of such an honor. There is just one catch, since you aren''t an official member we need something in exchange for this gift. Cough up 30 x Serpentis Silver Tag and the Federation Navy Comet Blueprint is yours.'),
(93325,0,3,12539,30,5,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Security',500004,11076,5,'Item Drop-off 30x Serpentis Gold Tag (3.0 m3)','We have a policy here within the Gallente Federation that our more prominent members fly a suitable ship according to their status, both to give them an edge during combat and to uphold our image, especially within our borders. We have recently decided to extend this benefit to mercenaries or freelancers employed by us that have shown admirable bravery and skill in the field, or earned the right through countless hours of dedicated service to our corporations. As you undoubtedly already know I have been assigned the task of allocating these ships to their deserved owners. After looking at your record, we decided that you, <Pilot>, are worthy of such an honor. There is just one catch, since you aren''t an official member we need something in exchange for this gift. Cough up 30 x Serpentis Gold Tag and the Vexor Navy Issue Blueprint is yours.'),
(93326,0,3,17216,30,5,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Security',500004,11076,5,'Transport 30x Serpentis Diamond Tag (3.0 m³) to 0.5 Timmothy Sawyr''s Dominix in Jolia.','So you''ve come at last, <Pilot>. I have been expecting you. I assume you''re here to acquire your new ship blueprint. If so you''re in luck, I still have a few Megathron Navy Issue Blueprint copies in stock.'),
(93327,0,1,23679,1,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Distribution',500011,0,0,'Transport 1x Latent Submission Tapes (0.1 m³) from Auberulle VIII - Moon 1 - Egonics Inc. Development Studio({{ColorSecurityRating','Well, well, what have we here? An eager puppy pilot all raring to go? Asking every stranger to be his friend. Tut, tut, did your mother never tell you not to talk to strangers, <Pilot>? But now that you''re here, what to do with you? Ah, well, maybe you''re not as green behind the ears as you seem. Might be I have something for you after all. You might not like it, but it''s all I have at the moment. What I''m talking about is a simple errand, so it shouldn''t tax your skills too much. My friends at Egonics Inc. have come up with new tapes for the Latent Transmitter that I need to collect from them. I can see you''re curious about the transmitter, but what you don''t know can''t hurt you. Hm, I guess that''s not exactly true, is it? Well, anyway, don''t worry: I''ll keep you all safe and tucked in. Run this errand for me and perhaps my opinion of you will rise above the level of "haughty indifference." Then I might allow you to sink your teeth into a juicier bone next time around.'),
(93328,0,1,23680,5,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Distribution',500011,0,0,'Acquire 5x Smuggler Tag (0.5 m³)','Perhaps on your long journey to Auberulle and back you spent the idle minutes wondering what a member of the Angel Cartel was doing here in Algintal? I asked that exact same question when our chief told me he was sending me here. What is there here in Algintal for the Cartel? We have no presence to speak of here and even less authority. The few Angels who frequent the area are loners and nuts, acting pretty much of their own accord. Well, to put things bluntly, we want to usurp the stranglehold the Serpentis and Thukkers have on smuggling and other lucrative activities here on the Gallente side of the Federation/Republic borders. The Thukkers, those devious buggers, are putting the latent transmission technology of Egonics Inc. to good use, but I''ve managed to worm my way into the deal. But while I''m engaged in political machinations with the Thukkers and Egonics, the Serpentis are running rampant. I need you to take them down a peck or two. One of their main areas of operation is over in the Skeleton Comet complex in Deltole. They wrenched the place from Federation hands some years ago and now consider it their own little haven. Hitting them there would send a clear message that there''s a new player in the sandbox and that they''d better watch out. To put it simply: Go over there, locate some Serpentis smugglers, and pop them. Return with the smuggler tags they drop to claim your reward ... and of course glowing praises from me.'),
(93329,0,1,23681,1,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Distribution',500020,0,0,'Acquire 1 x Shattered Forgery Tools (1.0 m³)','The Serpentis are not taking us seriously enough, it seems. My spies tell me their leadership thinks your strike was a one-time occurance that they need not concern themselves with. And more importantly, it did little to weaken their grip on the smuggling in the constellation. So we need to take more drastic steps to show them that we mean business. With all the hype surrounding the Wiyrkomi''s presence here in Algintal, smugglers have to be extra careful. The Serpentis are no idiots, and they''ve reacted fast. They built a huge repackaging factory in the middle of nowhere, where they ship all their illegal goods to be repacked into something looking a bit less suspicious. I understand they learnt the technique from the Thukkers, who''ve done the same for years. Be that as it may. What I''m asking of you is no small feat. Take out the repackaging factory, and the Serpentis will not only become very aware of our presence here, but their operation will take a severe hit. My informant has given me the coordinates of the repackaging factory, but I have only very limited information about the defenses around the installation. No doubt they''re formidable, so taking a few friends along is a good idea. But I''m pretty sure the defense systems are not yet fully operational since the factory only recently opened.'),
(93330,0,1,23682,1,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Distribution',500011,0,0,'Acquire 1 x Strike Force Gear (2.0 m³)','Oh, we got their attention now, <Pilot>! The Serpentis are seething, and it''s all thanks to you. There''s only problem: Now that the Serpentis know that we Angels are barging in, they''re planning to retaliate. How very idiotic of them! Heh. Well, of course we must counter their counter-threats. My most loyal and reliable source within the Serpentis tells me that an elite strike force is arriving from Fountain. I''m already quivering in my boots, as you can see. No, seriously, the fools have made one grave error. The strike force''s gear arrived ahead of the team itself. It is now sitting deep inside the Skeleton Comet complex over in Deltole. "Only by exploiting the errors of others can we enlighten the world," my mother always told me, and who am I to defy my mother, eh? We must act quickly. Go to the Skeleton Comet complex, locate the Serpentis Command Outpost, and destroy it. Then return with the strike force''s gear to me. That should paralyze their whole operation. This is an important mission, which will have significant impact on your faction standings.'),
(93331,0,1,26791,3,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Courier',500001,0,0,'Transport 3x Crates of Construction Blocks (210.0 m³)','As I''ve already told you we have some problems with our transportation service. We''re using some of our own freighters now to transport goods from Caldari space, but we''re short on manpower. If you could stop by Balle VII - Moon 17 - Center for Advanced Studies School and bring the 50 construction blocks I had ordered to me, then I''ll give you a reward. We need them for the next habitation module we''re building for the workers stationed here.'),
(93332,0,1,23274,18,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Courier',500001,0,0,'Pick-up and deliver 18x Caldari Surveyor (54 m³)','I have something slightly more dangerous for you this time, <Pilot>. We have 18 surveyors stranded on Tendhyes VIII - Kaalakiota Corporation Factory after Prompt Delivery backed out on our deal to get them moved here a few days ago. Apparently they decided the risks of transporting them through Gallente space were too great. The Federation Navy has threatened to attack any corporations under the Caldari State other than Wiyrkomi, and even with our surveyors on board we fear they might hold true to their word. If you can get the surveyors here today, I''ll give you a hefty reward. Just watch out for those FON fanatics, they''re everywhere these days.'),
(93333,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Encounter',0,0,0,'Destroy FON ships','I have a matter of urgency for you this time, <Pilot>. Temko, the Gallentean mercenary organization that we hired, reported to us that one of its surveillance posts in Colelie has been attacked. All of their personnel are currently unavailable, so they pleaded with us to find someone else to investigate the attack. And I think you are the man for the job. It''s been a while since the attack was reported, so we have absolutely no idea what the situation is out there. Hopefully you will be able to track down whoever is responsible and punish them. Good luck.'),
(93334,0,3,23234,1,5,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Encounter',0,0,0,'Retrieve 1x Azure Canyon Tourist Pass','This time I''d like you to obtain a pass into the Azure Canyon in Colelie. The Azure Canyon is located in a pocket of deadspace which has unusually dense ion clouds, which makes it ideal for creating a massive power plant. The reason we are in Colelie is to start constructing the power station, but so far we''ve been stuck at square 1 due to our inability to clear the area of Serpentis pirates and FON terrorists. To get to the point, we''re sending in a few squadrons of Temko mercenaries to conduct a quick reconnaissance operation in the Azure Canyon area. But we haven''t been able to get past the first acceleration gate since Serpentis agents reconfigured the lock, and it would take far too long to manually navigate through the deadspace pocket. Hence we need the keycard. You''ll find a group of FON ships blockading the gate against anyone affiliated with Wiyrkomi. We believe their leader has the keycard we need in her possession. Her name is Apte Donie, and she should be located at the forward point into the complex. Use whatever means necessary to acquire that keycard, <Pilot>.'),
(93335,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Security{{Verify',500001,16796,5,'','Veko?? You will address me as sir, peon! I will not have some rug-rat insult me like that in public ... Now where were we? Ah yes, your mission. Well I have a number of nuisances for you to ''take care of'', and the first in line is a Gallentean called Alarus Ekire. He''s the commander of the military arm of FON, the cowardly tree-huggers who''ve been sabotaging our operations in Federation space ever since we made that deal with the Gallente government. With him out of the picture, FON''s terrorist groups will become more disorganized and less deadly, until they find a suitable replacement anyway. You''ll probably find Alarus in the Tourist area of Azure Canyon in Colelie. They''ve apparently made a pact with Serpentis to defend that area of deadspace against our attempts to move our own people in there. So you might have a bit of a fight on your hands, but I''m sure you''ll manage. Bring back something to prove that Alarus is no more, and I''ll give you your reward.'),
(93336,0,3,22231,1,5,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Encounter',500001,16796,5,'Acquire 1x Recruitment Center Data Log (0.1 m³)','Your second mission is to investigate the theft of a batch of drills we ordered recently. They were being shipped to our survey station in Colelie when their convoy was ambushed by unknown assailants. We have so far not retrieved any witnesses, and have not found any evidence at the crime scene linking FON or Serpentis to the attack. However gut feeling tells me it must have been FON. Serpentis would have taken the crew and held them for ransom, but we have found no evidence that they are still alive. I''d like you to get to the bottom of this, <Pilot>. Fly to the FON recruitment center in Fluekele and see what you can find there. Return to me with anything that might implicate their involvement in the attack. Dismissed.'),
(93337,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Security{{Verify',500001,16796,5,'','The next job is going to be a bit more difficult than your last two assignments. This time I want you to infiltrate the Azure Canyon complex and find a place called ''The Black Market''. We have reliable information that a regiment of Temko mercenaries are being held in a prison facility there. They were sent on a reconnaissance mission into the complex a few days ago, but never returned. I advise you to avoid a direct confrontation with the Serpentis forces at the Black Market. Just grab the mercenaries and flee, they are your number one priority in this mission. We are running out of mercenaries already, we can''t afford to lose these Temko personnel. I also recommend that you finish this assignment in a timely manner. My time is precious.'),
(93338,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Encounter',500001,16796,5,'Destroy the FON ships','Something urgent just came up. The Survey Station in Colelie was attacked by FON, probably in retaliation for our recent actions against them. Many of our people have been killed, and more importantly we lost billions of ISK worth of equipment. This heinous act must not go unpunished. Our surveillance teams are currently on their tail, and I would like you to take care of them. I''ll supply you with a bookmark to their approximate location, you do the rest. And do hurry this time, you can hang around the cafe lounge some other time.'),
(93339,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Security{{Verify',500001,16796,5,'','Now I want you to get us some Zemnar. The Survey Station in Colelie suffered heavy casualties, and their antibiotic supplies are stretched to the limit. On top of that there has been a viral outbreak which could cause many deaths if we don''t get them the Zemnar they need fast. Now a few surveyors and engineers are expendable, but this threatens the entire outpost and could compromise our operation in Colelie! You''ll find a stock of Zemnar not far from the Pend Insurance station in Fluekele, in their storage bin. They refuse to share it with us, probably as a result of pressure from the various nature lover groups which have been protesting our presence here. So we are going to have to take it by force. Do whatever it takes to get a hold of that Zemnar, and drop it off at our factory in this system. One of my lackeys will transport it to Colelie. Just don''t reveal who you''re working for, to anyone! Now get moving!'),
(93340,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Security{{Verify',500001,16796,5,'','You''ve proven to be fairly reliable so far, <Pilot>, so I believe I can trust you for a rather sensitive assignment. We have a traitor in our ranks, or to be more precise in the ranks of the Temko mercenaries we hired. His name is Eule Vitrauze and he''s apparently working for Friends of Nature on the side. We believe he''s the reason the last Temko operation in the Azure Canyon complex failed. I would ask the Temko to deal with him themselves, but Gara believes that if we make an outsider do the job and make it seem like we weren''t involved in his death then our agent within FON will not be compromised. You''ll probably find Eule orbiting a security outpost inside the Central Administration complex. But don''t worry, the other Temko ships will not come to his aid, all you have to do is face him one-on-one, and then return to me once his ship has been turned to dust. Dismissed. This is an important mission, which will have significant impact on your faction standings.'),
(93341,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Trade',500001,0,0,'Acquire 1x Wyirkomi voucher (1 m³)','As a matter of fact I do have something suited for you, <Pilot>. But first you''re going to have to supply me with a voucher from one of the other agents around here. I recommend stopping by the Survey Station, they need some help there as well.'),
(93342,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Encounter',0,0,0,'Destroy the storage facilities in the FON complex','Since you''ve been approved by Veko Tallaja, I guess you''re suited for a few missions vital to our plans here in Algintal. To get straight to the point, we are currently on a campaign to rid the deadspace areas we purchased from Federate sources of pirates and violent protesters, namely the Friends of Nature organization which has been causing us much grief since we came to Algintal. To complete our objectives we have been forced to hire mercenaries which are permitted entrance into Federation space, considering that the government steadfastly refuses to allow any Caldari State military presence in their sovereign space. Which is understandable considering the current political climate. Wiyrkomi sacrificed much to get this deal, and we definitely are not backing out with our tails behind our legs. Our CEO has publicly announced that we are firmly against any Caldari State incursions into Federation space, incurring the wrath of the State Chief Executive Panel which has fined us for rediculous reasons simply out of spite. And on top of that our lease on the deadspace pockets within Federation space could be annulled at any time if the Senate gives in to the protesters. So now that you''re briefed of the situation, it''s time to get started. Your first target is an old abandoned Federation Navy ammunitions storage in Jolia. We have confirmed reports that the military arm of FON uses the facilities located there to store their weapons of mass destruction. Take it out and their terrorist operation in Jolia will be crippled. Over and out.'),
(93343,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Encounter',500020,11076,5,'Destroy Serpentis convoy','As I said earlier, it''s time for us turn our attention to the Serpentis. The Serpentis problem should in fact be easier to deal with than our war with the Gallente environmentalists, but at the same time they are the deadlier foe. The Serpentis are not at war with us due to some fanatical idealogy, instead they are simply here to protect their financial interests. I''m quite certain that as soon as they see this ''war'' becoming unprofitable in the long run, they will retreat from their positions in our territory. So to start off we need to make them know we mean business. And to do that I want you to take out one of their drug convoys. I had the Temko mercenaries under my command conduct a massive surveillance operation, which eventually revealed one of the Serpentis''s drug convoy routes. I''ll supply you with a bookmark that should lead you to one such convoy. Destroy it and report back to me. And remember, the cargo should not be brought back here, I want nothing to do with their contraband.'),
(93344,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Encounter',500020,11076,5,'Retrieve Elere Febre''s Data Log','Your next assignment is a pretty important one. Elere Febre is a Serpentis agent working in Fluekele, which we believe is their contact with Friends of Nature, as we''ve detected FON agents visiting her habitation module multiple times in the past week alone. FON are desperate to not let news of this alliance between them and Serpentis leak to the public. I''m not even sure if the majority of FON''s members know of their dealings with pirates. Public opinion in favor of FON will undoubtedly plummet once people believe there is a connection between them and violent criminals. Now killing her should be simple. The difficult part is retrieving evidence of her involvement with FON. I''m counting on her leaving some sort of evidence in her habitation module, which is located at Fluekele IV''s sixth moon. Find the habitation module and destroy it, search the wreckage for anything that survived which may implicate FON''s relationship with Serpentis. Return to me with your findings. Hopefully we''ll be able to kill two flies in one swing with the completion of this mission.'),
(93345,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Encounter',500020,11076,5,'Retrieve Serpentis Transaction Log','The Serpentis have so far refused to meet any of our demands. I expected as much, a few convoys and agents are expendable in their eyes. But it''s time to turn up the heat. This time I would like you to gather the best pilots you can muster and launch an offensive directly into the Azure Canyon of Colelie. Head straight towards the Black Market pocket and destroy the Serpentis Stronghold. If you can, try to recover something that will allow us to blackmail them, such as computer logs, prisoners, anything. I suspect that Salvador Sarpati will think twice about going up against Wiyrkomi after suffering the loss of such a costly installation. If all goes as planned, the Serpentis will retreat from the Azure Canyon, giving us full access to the ion clouds.'),
(93346,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Encounter',0,0,0,'Destroy the Asteroid Outpost','As your final assignment for me, <Pilot>, I want you obliterate the FON headquarters, located in Deltole. As you probably know, Friends of Nature mainly consists of civilians which are protected by Federation law. They claim to be a peaceful organization fighting for ''the environment'', but in fact a large portion of its members are nothing but terrorist scum who are willing to sacrifice human life to protect a heap of rocks and gas clouds. I''ve come to realize that no matter how hard we hit them, they will always come back for more. So the only course of action I see is to exterminate the lot of them. Unfortunately, the Federation will not look kindly upon us killing its civilians, despite them being affiliated with Friends of Nature. They don''t have the same view of FON as we do. So it is vital that you do not reveal who you are working for to anyone. If you do, I''ll make certain you won''t live to see another day.'),
(93347,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Trade',500001,0,0,'Bring Veko Tallaja''s Voucher','Before I let you work for me you''re going to have to supply me with a voucher from Veko Tallaja, located in Central Command in Fluekele.'),
(93348,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',0,0,0,'','Welcome to the Nickel & Dime Store, <Character>. It is a humble little shop owned and operated by the Thukker tribe, catering to the needy souls in this beautiful constellation. Hm, something tells me you can be of some assistance to us ― perhaps you''ve worked for the Thukkers in the past? Let''s see if you''ve got what it takes to help our fledgling business grow. I have a small task for you: nothing complicated or risky, but it should let me gauge your talents. Deliver a few crates of goods to a nearby station for me. The rewards are modest, since this is such an easy task, but it''s only the start.'),
(93349,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',0,0,0,'','Good work on your previous assignment. Despite it being a tedious one, you pulled it off without any qualms. Now for something a little more interesting. You see, things have not been easy around here lately. The Caldari mega-corp Wiyrkomi is intent on tapping into the vast natural resources found in the constellation, much to the dismay of the many environmentalists here in the Federation. The struggle between the two sides draws unwanted attention to our little enterprise here and is making our operation difficult. Down the road, I might be tempted to have you help us with this unpleasant situation. But not just yet. First, we have to take care of another small problem that just came up. The Serpentis drug lords are out in force here in Algintal, overseeing traffic between Federation and Republic space. We Thukkers are not into the drug scene, so we generally leave them alone. The same applies for them, for the most part. Live and let live, huh? Thing is, many of the Serpentis have grown too fond of their own goods and can get a little wild at times. One such incident occurred the other night when a gang of renegade Serpentis junkies stole some goods we were receiving from our associates in the Republic. The goods aren''t all that valuable, but we must send a clear sign to the Serpentis that our goods are to be left alone. I know that the fools who stole our goods are relaxing at the Skeleton Comet complex over in Deltole. If you''re willing to go over there and teach them a lesson, a hard lesson ― a permanent lesson, get me? ― then I would be much obliged. And if you could return with some of the goods they stole, I''d be even happier.'),
(93350,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',0,0,0,'','Oh, <Character>, you''ve come at an opportune moment. Things are progressing as I feared they would. The continuous struggle between Wiyrkomi and the activists have cast a spotlight on the constellation. While we here are the Nickel & Dime Store are running a perfectly legal business, our associates and clients like to operate in the dark. Already, I''ve lost several important clients, and some employees are getting restless. So much so that I''m having difficulties making my more demanding deliveries. Unfortunately, I do not have the means or the knowledge to do much about the situation, but my business associate Iliere Angetyn is a most resourceful Gallentean, and I''m sure he''s already contemplating how to put things right. But Angetyn doesn''t deal with just anyone. Only those clearly in favor with the Trust Partners company get his attention. So I have a proposal for you. Run an errand for me that one of my just-departed couriers was supposed to, and I''ll give you a Trust Partners Business Card. Show this to Angetyn and he''s certain to offer you something lucrative. The errand in question is a simple delivery over the border into the Republic. It has a very small chance of getting you in trouble with the customs, but I''m sure a resourceful pilot such as yourself can pick the right route to avoid any unwanted attention.'),
(93351,0,3,23542,1,5,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Encounter',500001,16796,5,'Acquire 1x Surveillance Recordings (0.1 m3)','Hm. Alright. You see, Algintal was such a nice place a few years back. The traffic through its systems and the many tourists meant we could operate with minimal risk. But now that has all changed with the arrival of the Wiyrkomi corporation and their lackeys, Roden Shipyards. What were once standard border-running operations now require much more time and effort to pull off. What is worse, the Caldari think they own the place just because they exploited a loophole in the trade agreement between the State and the Federation. They''re trying to muscle us out. I want to nip that bullshit in the bud and strike back at the Wiyrkomi. That''s where you come in, [Character]. The Wiyrkomi have installed a surveillance outpost here in Augnais. The problem is, I only found out about it a few days ago, after I''d just completed an important deal with a Republic contact of mine. If the Wiyrkomi listened in on the deal, they could compromise the Thukkers'' position here in Algintal. I thought it was too late to do anything about it, but the security measures of the Wiyrkomi are working against them here. The surveillance outpost operates in total radio silence and only sends out its recordings in a shuttle once a week to the Wiyrkomi headquarters over in Fluekele. The shuttle will depart tomorrow, so there is still time to take care of this ... problem. I want you to head over to the surveillance outpost and take out that shuttle. Make sure you locate the surveillance recordings and confiscate them. Bring them back to me, and we''re back on track.'),
(93352,0,5,23543,2,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500002,0,0,'Acquire 2x Spoiled Drugs (0.4 m³)','Head over to the Skeletal Comet in Deltole, locate the wrecked ship, and get the drugs out'),
(93353,0,1,23544,1,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Courier',500002,0,0,'Transport Cargo 1x Sealed Container (50.0 m³).','Yes, in fact. I''m feeling very confident in your abilities, so I''m setting up a big job for you. But before that, I need you to take care of a smaller matter for me. I have acquired certain items that cast Veko Tallaja, the operation supervisor for Wiyrkomi here in Algintal, in a rather negative light. I''m not going to use this stuff just now, but I need to store it somewhere safe. I want you to head over to Fluekele and drop it off at the Pend Insurance station there. A friend of mine will then place it in a safe-deposit box there. I know it''s a trivial thing I''m asking, but this is very sensitive material that absolutely can''t get into the wrong hands ... and, besides, I need more time to prepare for your big mission.'),
(93354,0,3,23545,4,5,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Encounter',500020,11076,5,'Acquire 4x Smuggler DNA (0.4 m³).','Algintal has always been a favored spot for smugglers. It''s far enough out of the way so as not to attract too much attention from the authorities. Besides us at Trust Partners, the Serpentis are out here in force, as well as several independents. Usually we try to stay well clear of each other, but sometimes a group arrives that thinks it can muscle everyone else out. One such group has been making a nuisance of itself recently, and it''s time to take them out. We''ve played Mr. Nice Guy until now, but no longer. The smugglers in question have built themselves a nice little hideout near here. We''re not playing any games here, so killing them is the only item on the agenda. It was hell to track them down, so make sure you take them all out in one go so I don''t have to repeat the process later. If you pull this off with style, I''m sure some associates of mine would love for you to work a bit for them. When you bring me those dead smugglers'' DNA, I''ll give you some ship logs that my associates need to tamper with a bit to make them seem as innocent as a virgin''s butt. Those logs should be ample proof to them that you''re a trusted friend.'),
(93355,0,5,23554,1,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500002,0,0,'Acquire 1x Trust Partners Business Card','Try talking to some in the vicinity and get back to me once you have a Trust Partners Business Card.'),
(93356,0,5,23552,1,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / R&D/',500002,0,0,'Transport 1x FON Banner (1.0 m³) to 0.6 Amakkit''s Thrasher in Parchanier.','You probably know already that we''ve been subtly manipulating FON and Serpentis into working together against Wiyrkomi. While this is not without risk we feel it''s the best chance of driving the Caldari megalomaniacs out of Algintal so we can get back to some serious smuggling. But things are now rapidly progressing out of control and we have to get more directly involved to get things under control again. There''s this Serpentis agent by the name of Elere Febre that we linked up with a FON contact. Febre is the main liaison between the two sides and has worked wonders in the short time she''s been involved. But according to this message you brought me her cover is blown. Wiyrkomi is on to her and is probably planning to take her out as we speak. Or worse, take her into custody and interrogate her. We cannot let that happen as she could then reveal the Thukkers involvement. Time is of the essence here, so the first thing we need to do is distract the Wiyrkomi until we come up with a real plan. I don''t have time to assemble squad of my own so some improvisation is the order of the day. You''re the only one here, so I guess I must rely on you. We must instigate a fake attack on the Wiyrkomi by FON. To do that we need an authentic FON banner. I know that FON has an operation station inside the Skeletal Comet complex over in Deltole. It''s overlooking the huge rogue drone hive in there. What do you say about raiding the place and steal me a FON banner? Return with it here and we''re half way home in throwing Wiyrkomi off the scent.'),
(93357,0,5,23552,1,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / R&D',500002,0,0,'Transport 1x FON Banner (1.0 m³) from Pickup Location in 0.6 Parchanier to 0.5 Jolia VII - Moon 12 - Wiyrkomi Corporation Factory.','I must congratulate you on being so quick in bringing me the banner. I wasn''t feeling all that optimistic about our chances in thwarting Wiyrkomi as they were already on the move, but now things look different. I''ve already put in motion a fake sabotage attack on one of the Wiyrkomi stations in the system. All my agents there need is the banner to leave behind after the raid. The Caldari are a suspicious lot, so any member of the Thukkers entering one of their stations is bound to attract attention. But you''re presence there will not. To complete your recent success in getting the banner all you need to do now is getting the banner into the Wiyrkomi station and we''ll take care of the rest.'),
(93358,0,3,23551,1,5,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / R&D/Encounter',500002,17138,5,'Kill all the FON ships in the area (0.5 Barmalie) and retrieve the DNA from the FON contact to complete the mission. Transport 1x FON Contact DNA (0.1 m³) to drop-off location in 0.6 Parchanier.','The sabotage attack on the Wiyrkomi station in Jolia was only a limited success, but it was enough to divert their attention long enough for Elere Febre to cover her tracks. She''s abandoned her habitation module and gone into hiding for the time being. Wiyrkomi is bound to raid her place soon, but she was careful in leaving no traces of her own DNA there, though she left a fake one that hopefully will have them running in circles. But there is still one loose end we need to tie up. Febre''s contact within the FON is making a nuisance of himself and before he does something rash we must take him out. Before Febre went into hiding she set up a meeting with the guy to discuss the future. She gave me the coordinates for that meeting and I want you to go over there and kill the guy. Just remember, even if he''s a pansy activists doesn''t mean he''s a walkover and he may very well have some backup with him. So take care. And perhaps take some backup with you. The situation is intense and you never know what might be lying ahead.'),
(93359,0,1,23556,1,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / R&D/Courier',500002,0,0,'Transport 1x Warning Message (1.0 m³) to 0.6 Amakkit''s Thrasher in Parchanier.','Give Drusk the message from Krester Rupptofs.'),
(93360,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',500002,0,0,'','We try to keep our operation here at the Forgery under the radar, with a little bribery on the side to take care of over-zealous bureaucrats. Still, even if we''re not exactly advertising our services we''ve established a rather formidable reputation in the underworld. We like to keep things as they are and sometimes we have to engage in some aggressive weed-killing to rid ourselves of unwanted baggage that can come back and haunt us later. Which brings me to the job I want to offer you. A few months ago we entered an agreement with some local thugs here in Deltole. At the time we were anxious as to what the Serpentis druglords at the Skeleton Comet were up to, so we hired these guys to snoop around for us. Things went well for awhile, but now we have reason to believe the thugs have been playing both sides, offering their service to the Serpentis as well. That won''t do, of course. We gave the thugs a ComLink encoder/decoder for secure communications. But what we didn''t tell them was that the encoder also acts as a bug device. We only put it in their as a precaution, never intending to use it, but now we need to retrieve the encoder to confirm our believe that the thugs are two-faced bastards. Get me that encoder so I can exact my punishment on them. I''ve already hatched a devious plan, if I say so myself, for framing those thugs and setting them up for the Serpentis to chew on. But first I need that encoder. The thugs have entrenched themselves deep inside the Skeleton Comet complex, acting as any other small time smuggling cartel. The encoder should be located in their Relay Station, so target that. Note- Get a friend to help clear rats to get the object here as the room before is difficult to self clear.'),
(93361,0,1,23547,100,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Courier',500002,0,0,'Bring 100x Dolls (100.0 m³)','I''m glad you came along, <Pilot>. As you probably already know the arrival of the Wiyrkomi corporation in the constellation has stirred things up a bit. Tourism is way down and the authorities are unfairly blaming us smugglers. It''s getting harder and harder to conduct any decent smuggle run and we have to be twice as careful. Not that it harms us here at the Forgery much, if anything it only makes our services even more sought after. A Minmatar associate of mine needs to get a large quantity of high quality X-Instinct into Gallente space, but he''s not willing to risk the Federation customs at times like these. That''s were we come into the picture. I need a small favor from you. I ordered a large quantity of dolls, but they''re sitting in a TranStellar Shipping warehouse over in Adiere. Are you willing to fetch them for me? It''s a trivial assignment, I know, but I''m positively swamped at the moment, as you can well understand.'),
(93362,0,1,23548,100,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Courier',500002,0,0,'Transport 100x Tampered Dolls (100.0 m³)','I''m having the dolls ''enhanced'' as we speak. Your next assignment is much more tricky. Are you willing to take the drug-filled dolls deep into Gallente space? The risk is less than it sounds, as only very thorough scan of your vessel will reveal what hides inside the innocent looking dolls. But occasionally it does happen and then you''d be in deep trouble. I''d understand if you back down now, but it would be a real shame after having accomplished so much for us. But as it''s your ass on the line, I won''t pressure you any further. The choice is yours.'),
(93363,0,3,23549,5,5,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Encounter',500011,17138,5,'Obtain 5x Smuggler Signet (0.5 m³)','You''ve come through for me big time in the past, <CHARACTER NAME>. So I have an important task for you now. First, I''ll let you in on a little secret. You''ve probably already encountered some of the activists here in Algintal, fighting to get Wiyrkomi out. Well, we Thukkers are in the same boat. We also want Wiyrkomi out. Not because we care for the environment, but because Wiyrkomi''s presence here is hitting our business hard. But the problem is we can''t draw attention to ourselves. If Wiyrkomi or the Federation start perceiving the Thukker tribe as a real threat in the constellation they will come down on our heads real hard. And we don''t want that to happen, now do we? So we''ve been trying to manipulate things as much as we can behind the scenes. By discreetly supporting the more militant elements of FON we hope the activists can be of enough nuisance to the Wiyrkomi that the Caldari will flee with their tail between their legs. We''ve used every method we can come up with for this, including stirring some of the Serpentis druglords into action. A few weeks ago a powerful druglord associated with the Angel Cartel, known as Don Rico, agreed to help out. At the time we didn''t think that FON would amount to much, so we invested pretty heavily in getting Don Rico involved. The results were immediate and at first his diligence thrilled us. But recently it has started to get out of hand, with Don Rico getting ever more outrageous fighting Wiyrkomi and their cronies. Our sources close to the druglord tell us that Don Rico has grown much too fond of his own product and is completely out of control. We need to restrain Don Rico before his actions jeopardize the whole operation. I know that the Federation Navy and CONCORD are starting to take notice and the last thing we need is for him to fall into their hands. He knows too much. So we need to take him out quickly. And you''re just the pilot for the job. Unfortunately, I don''t know the exact whereabouts of Don Rico. He likes to cruise around in his pleasure yacht and he could be lurking anywhere in the constellation. We need to flush him out and I know just the thing to stir him into showing his face. He owns a drug factory not far from here and I want you to raid it. Kill a few of his henchmen. Don Rico''s greatest weakness is his vanity and vengefulness. A direct attack on his possessions will certainly make him come screaming in revenge. And that''s our chance to take him out. But first, the raid. All Don Rico''s henchmen have a smuggler signet. Collect a few of these signets and bring them to me. Let''s see what happens then.'),
(93364,0,3,23550,1,5,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Encounter',500011,17138,5,'Obtain 1x Don Rico''s Head (0.1 m³)','Just as I predicted the raid on the drug factory got just the results we wanted. Don Rico is screaming fury on all the underworld channels trying to find the culprit. Don''t worry, we''ll keep you identity hidden long enough for you take him out for good. It''s a dangerous assignment, but if you don''t do it you''ll have Don Rico''s revenge hanging over your head for the rest of your life. Sorry to put you in this position, but look at it from my point of view, it was a win-win situation. Anyway, you''re getting handsomely rewarded for all of this, so don''t sulk too much. When you accept this mission I''ll give you the coordinates to the place where Don Rico is hiding out at the moment. Like all druglords he''s even more paranoid than I am, so rest assured he''s got artillery and plenty of it. Perhaps bringing a few friends along would be a good idea.'),
(93365,0,1,23555,3,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Courier',500002,0,0,'3x Ship logs (3.0 m³) (Obtained from Agent Angetyn)','Ah, they''re from Angetyn. Excellent! Yes, I can doctor them for him. Not that I haven''t done so many times in the past, mind you. But what to do with you? Angetyn only sends me pilots he thinks highly of, so let''s see if you''re as talented as he thinks. By the way, I have another mission prepared for you already...'),
(93366,0,3,23678,4,5,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Security',500002,17138,5,'Acquire 4x Aether Hive Link (8{{m3','"Algintal is one of the primary smuggling routes between the Federation and Republic space and Deltole is the main hub for smugglers in the constellation. The Serpentis have taken over a local complex, a natural beauty spot called the Skeleton Comet, and made it their own. Us Thukkers do our best to keep up and fortunately we''re in good enough standing with most of the Serpentis to be allowed in their haven for some RR But a week or two ago the Serpentis asked us to pay them back some of their hospitality. It seems parts of the complex are crawling with rogue drones. And not just any rogue drones, but pretty lethal ones. I understand their presence there contributed greatly to the Gallenteans evacuating the Skeleton Comet in the first place. And now it seems the rogue drones are stirring once more and the Serpentis are edgy what they might do. My superiors asked me to look into the matter and I''m interested in hiring you to do some reconnaissance for me in the complex. What I want you to do is enter the complex and locate the rogue drone hive. Kill a few of their perimeter guards and return to me with whatever they drop. Until we know more about what makes these drones such a threat we should tread carefully, so don''t try to act the hero and take on the whole hive in one go. Just pick out a few outer guards and we''ll take it one step at a time from there."'),
(93367,0,3,23677,2,5,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Security',500002,17138,5,'Acquire 2x Neural Bio Link (4{{m3','"This Aether Hive Link you returned with is a puzzle. It looks as if these drones are capable of more intimate communications than otherwise believed, but there are also hints that even more advanced hive mind links exist. I''m not a technician, so I can''t go into all that much details, this information is just something relayed to me from our techies at the Thukker Mix. They say that they suspect that a truly symbiotic drone hive might be evolving. They sound exited about it, but they are safe in their labs, so what do they know? It''s us that have to deal with these drones face to face that have to worry. In any case, we must verify whether this is true or not. I need you to go back into the complex and now I need stuff from drones closer to the hive. There are some drone workers orbiting close to the hive that seem like ideal targets. Take a few of them out and, again, return with whatever they drop. I will then forward it to our techies and see what the situation is. Just be extra careful when you take the workers out, you never know what might be protecting them. Maybe nothing, maybe something heavy."'),
(93368,0,3,23675,1,5,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Security',500002,17138,5,'Transport 1x Drone Observation Data (0.1{{m3','"The techies have taken a quick look at the links you brought me and they''re telling me it''s something they''ve never seen before and are totally baffled by. I''m not sure what to make of their comments, is this radical new design a threat or not? I must get a definite answer before deciding how to proceed. My observations and the data that you and others have collected for me, as well as information on these links, needs to be looked at by more talented techies. Take this data over to the Illinfrik system, to the Trust Partners station there. They will analyze this data and give me feedback I can work from."'),
(93369,0,3,23676,1,5,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Security',500002,17138,5,'Acquire 1 x Cognitive Hive Mind (0.1 m³)','"I''ve received a preliminary report from Illifik. It seems a new strand of rogue drones evolved in that hive over in the Skeleton Comet complex. At first, this new strand was incorporated into the existing hive and used to augment it. These strange links you got me are a case in point. But here''s the interesting thing. It seems the queen in the drone hive in the Skeleton Comet eventually turned against these new rogue drones and chased them away. The techies in Illifik managed to extract imbedded commands in the hive links you brought them that showed that the queen has ordered her drone army to destroy all these evolved rogue drones. Obviously she fears they might pose a threat to her authority. I don''t know if her drone army is already on the prowl, but I do know where one group of these evolved rogue drones is located at. I''ve been ordered to retrieve a functional hive mind from these new drones for further analyzes of their capabilities. Getting in a cross-fire between two opposing rogue drone factions seems kinda dangerous to me, thus I''m asking you if you''re up to the job. I have no idea what you should expect in this drone hive location, be on the lookout for the drone army sent by the queen in the Skeleton Comet. This is an important mission, which will have significant impact on your faction standings."'),
(93370,0,5,25274,20,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Trade',500004,0,0,'Trade 20x Viridian Cytoserocin (200{{m3',''),
(93371,0,1,3707,20,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Distribution',500020,0,0,'Acquire 20 x Blue Pill (4.0 m³)','Ah, <Character>! It is good to see there are freelancers who still maintain some loyalty to the Federation. It pleases me greatly that capsuleers like yourself still prove willing to help us out at need. Anyway, if you are looking for something to do, I know a little job that might just mix profit with pleasure. The Serpentis are setting up a little shop in this area where they are training their fighters, intending to bring them into the tournament. Now, we aren''t afraid of a little competition, but these fighters aren''t all-natural, if you know what I mean. We''re going to need them kidnapped and brought back here. Chances are you''re going to find the substance the Serps have been feeding their fighters as well, and I know some people who are very interested to see it recovered. Purely for research, of course. I wouldn''t dream of touching the stuff myself.... OK, OK, so maybe years ago when I was younger I might have tried some, but everyone experiments a little. No harm in that. Right? Just don''t let me find out that you''ve kept a little for yourself. I need ... I mean, I want it all. To give to our researchers, of course. Ahem. Yes. So, well, before you go ... listen, I would appreciate it if you could keep this matter to yourself. I''m sure you''ll agree that not everybody needs to know about this, hm?'),
(93372,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Distribution',500020,11076,5,'Destroy Serpentis ships and stronghold.','Thanks for meeting me in person, <Pilot>. We have a problem: My superiors have transcripts of our earlier communication and know about the drugs you brought back. It''s okay, though, they''ve given me a chance to get rid of the stuff. I need you to head out to Q-UA3C. The Serps have had a small shipping checkpoint there for a while, one which our investigative reporters have been monitoring for a big exposé on the way Serpentis supply chains work. Since my bosses want this little "mistake" of mine rectified quietly in order to prevent a scandal, they want the drugs taken there and the outpost destroyed. And that''s what will happen. Between you and me, though, I can''t stand the idea of letting such a valuable commodity go to waste. So what I want you to do is head out there and kill everything you see, but leave the drug disposal to me. I''ll convince my superiors and anyone else who asks that the drugs were destroyed at the outpost, and everyone will be happy ? at least, assuming that you can keep this a secret. And that is what you will do, I trust. This is an important mission, which will have significant impact on your faction standings.'),
(93373,0,5,25274,20,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Trade',500004,0,0,'Trade 20x Viridian Cytoserocin (200{{m3',''),
(93374,0,5,12541,30,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / ?',0,0,0,'Acquire and deliver 30x Serpentis Crystal Tag (3.0{{m3','We have a policy here within the ORE that our more prominent members use certain implants to boost their mental ability, since it''s important that our people in key positions perform at a level above what''s considered normal for a human being. It''s a competitive world we live in, and sometimes one has to take risks to achieve one''s goals, even if it means meddling with the brain. You may not be a full-fledged member of Outer Ring Excavations, but you''ve created such a name for yourself that we feel obliged to treat you as one of our own. And considering your record, we feel that our policy pertains to you as well. So I''ve been authorized to give you this implant in exchange for one simple task. Bring me a few insignias and the reward is yours.'),
(93375,0,5,25274,20,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Trade',500004,0,0,'Trade 20x Viridian Cytoserocin (200{{m3',''),
(93376,0,3,3814,2,5,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Encounter',500020,11076,5,'Acquire 2 x Reports (0.2 m³)','You seem eager and willing to work for me. I have this little problem you could help me out with. Yesterday I was tricked into telling my supervisors I would take care of a situation in the area, not fully knowing all the details. Next time I´ll be more careful and not be baited. Anyway, I looked into it and scout reports indicated a large Serpentis operation in the ppg-xc system. It appears they''re setting up their own tournament to compete with the Legends Trial. Some of our advertisers have a real problem with this, so they need the operation brought to a halt. Naturally, I''d do it myself, but I figure since you are such an eager puppy you would just love to do it for me, wouldn''t you?'),
(93377,0,3,25869,5,5,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Encounter',500020,11076,5,'Acquire 5 x Harlots (5.0 m³)','Those blasted Serps just keep bouncing back. They seem determined to profit from the proceedings in some way. After we took out their tournament site, they appear to have immediately put their backup plan into action, namely to put up a brothel for tournament visitors in need of some after-hours entertainment. Their hiring practices leave a lot to be desired. They''ve abducted some of the finest exotic dancers this system has to offer. My immediate superior, bless his heart, has a particular affinity for one of these dancers, a girl who goes by the name of Layla. I need you to head out to the brothel, blow the living you-know-what out of it and bring the girl back. The Scope will be in your debt, friend. This is an important mission, which will have significant impact on your faction standings.'),
(93378,0,1,25879,1,0,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Courier',500004,0,0,'Transport 1 x Ovon Flac''s Container (10.0 m³)','Hey there, <Pilot>. I have a task I want you to complete. If you do it right, I might have a small reward for you. The next Legends Trial battle starts at midnight tonight, and as head of security around here, my job is to make sure it goes as smoothly as possible. However, there is a small problem. The documents detailing the fighters and their ships were scheduled to be delivered to me from 9GYL-O V - Moon 13 - Intaki Space Police Assembly Plant this morning. However, the courier assigned to the task has obviously failed us, and as such I need you to step up and fill his place. Go get the documents and bring them to me. Do it quickly and I will have a little something extra waiting for you. Fly safe.'),
(93379,0,3,25878,3,5,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Encounter',500020,11076,5,'Acquire 3 x Ovon Flac''s Documents (0.3 m³)','The container you delivered to me was completely empty! Those damned Serpentis must have snatched the documents as you were loading the container aboard your ship. I''m putting the blame for this mess squarely on your back. You need to solve this, <Pilot>! If my superiors find out the documents have been lost, we can expect some heads to roll ... your head, to be precise. Find the documents and bring them to me straight away. They cannot have gotten very far; I''m actually pretty sure they''re in this very system. This is an important mission, which will have significant impact on your faction standings.'),
(93380,0,3,3685,5,5,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Encounter',500020,11076,5,'Item Drop-off 5 x Hydrogen Batteries (5.0 m³)','Good day. Looking for a job, are you? I have just the thing for a strapping capsuleer such as yourself. We''re helping with putting on the Legends Trial, that great and massive confrontation. We''ve hit a snag, though; we had a shipment of supplies that were supposed to get here this morning, but the convoy ran into some technical difficulties and it appears they won''t get here in time. We''ve had wind of a Serpentis outpost in the vicinity, though, so we''re thinking we might just outsource and play them at their own game. How about it? You up for a little hit-snatch-and-run?'),
(93381,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Gallente COSMOS / Encounter',500004,11076,5,'Destroy these targets Location XG-D1L ({{ColorSecurityRating','Great job on the supplies. We seem to be good to go, now that most of the logistical details are taken care of. This will be greatest tournament ever. And I''m sure the Serpentis don''t mind us borrowing some of their things. I have another mission for you. Just another small supply run, one for which I''ll reward you handsomely, to show our appreciation for... hold on. Give me a second, here. I have something coming in over the wire. ... Oh, lord. Oh, sweet sister of mercy. Looks like we made the Serpentis mighty mad. In retaliation for our little loan of goods, they''ve gone all-out and attacked a Gallente station in XG-D1L Navy squadrons are already on the way, but it''s going to take them some time to get there. What we need now is someone to repel the first wave of attack, buy some time for the reinforcements to get there. What do you say, pilot? In the mood to be a hero today?'),
(93382,0,5,25268,20,0,'COSMOS Guristas COSMOS / Trade',500010,0,0,'Trade 20x Amber Cytoserocin (200{{m3','Ah, it''s nice to see a friendly face around here for a change, <Pilot>. But to answer your question, I came here to investigate Constellation E-8CSQ, which has been reported to contain massive gas clouds full of material used in booster manufacturing. There have been a lot of rumors about it within Guristas, and I thought I''d take a look for myself. Unfortunately, the number of rogue drones and outlaws here has me quite worried, so I dare not go looking for the clouds myself. Hence, I might have a job for you... However, I suggest you refrain from accepting my task unless you have access to a gas cloud harvester module. Without that, you will just be wasting my time.'),
(93383,0,1,15599,2,0,'COSMOS Guristas COSMOS / Distribution',500009,0,0,'Deliver 2x Caldari Navy Captain Insignia I (0.2 m³)','Aha! I knew that broad liked me. Whatever kind words she has for me, tell her it''s mutual. Or better yet, I have some flowers I''d like you to give her... Get something for Gue Mouey that will convince him to give you the information Isana wants.'),
(93384,0,5,15654,1,0,'COSMOS Guristas COSMOS / ?',500010,0,0,'Acquire and deliver 1x Caldari Navy Squad Leader Insignia (0.1{{m3','We have a policy here within the Guristas Pirates that our more prominent members fly a suitable ship according to their status, both to give them an edge during combat and to uphold our image, especially within our borders. We have recently decided to extend this benefit to mercenaries or freelancers employed by us that have shown admirable bravery and skill in the field, or earned the right through countless hours of dedicated service to our corporations. As you undoubtedly already know I have been assigned the task of allocating these ships to their deserved owners. After looking at your record, we decided that you, <Pilot>, are worthy of such an honor. There is just one catch, since you aren''t an official member we need something in exchange for this gift. Cough up 1 x Caldari Navy Squad Leader Insignia and the Worm Blueprint is yours. Dismissed'),
(93385,0,3,25394,1,5,'COSMOS Guristas COSMOS / Security',500010,16796,5,'Bring Item 1x Gue Mouey''s Message (0.1 m³). (Low Sec Warning!)','As a matter of fact, I could use a hand in finding out what has actually become of Black Jack. A colleague of mine in UL-4ZW, Gue Mouey, might know something. He''s one of the overseers of the Syndicate Trade Hub in that system, you''ll find it near UL-4ZW IX. He has had extensive dealings with agents of the Guristas and Caldari Navy, if anyone is qualified to scrounge up information on what happened to Black Jack, it''s him.'),
(93386,0,3,25398,1,5,'COSMOS Guristas COSMOS / Encounter',500009,11076,5,'Bring Item 1x Tikui''s Message (0.1 m³). (Low Sec Warning!)',''),
(93387,0,3,25401,1,5,'COSMOS Guristas COSMOS / Security',500009,11076,5,'Acquire 1x Expeditionary Data (0.1 m³) in -0.5 E-8CSQ. (Low Sec Warning!)','I think it''s time for you to know the objective of my mission here in E-8CSQ. We were to infiltrate Kois City, the central administrative complex in G5ED-Y, from where the Caldari send all of their expeditions, and answer the question that has been nagging my superiors back home, "Why are they here?". Now getting into Kois City will be no easy task. It''s heavily fortified. But on the bright side I think I know exactly what we''re looking for. My sources tell me that the expeditionary forces store most of the data they have collected in a computer within the city''s science labs. Backup data is also stored in data chips within their storage facility in the civilian sector of the city. Therefore your task is to somehow get into the civilian quarter and acquire at least one of those data chips. From this data we will hopefully be able to piece together their objective, and find out if it''s worth our time to get involved. This used to be Black Jack''s task, but I assume he discovered something that convinced him to cut ties with us and go solo. But I will tell you this, it is in your best interest to complete this task at any cost. Should you fail, or decide to ''keep'' the data for yourself, the Syndicate will hunt you down like a dog and force you to watch your own family executed in the cruelest of ways.'),
(93388,0,5,15655,1,0,'COSMOS Guristas COSMOS / ?',500010,0,0,'Acquire and deliver 1x Caldari Navy Raid Leader Insignia (0.1{{m3','We have a policy here within the Guristas Pirates that our more prominent members fly a suitable ship according to their status, both to give them an edge during combat and to uphold our image, especially within our borders. We have recently decided to extend this benefit to mercenaries or freelancers employed by us that have shown admirable bravery and skill in the field, or earned the right through countless hours of dedicated service to our corporations. As you undoubtedly already know I have been assigned the task of allocating these ships to their deserved owners. After looking at your record, we decided that you, <Pilot>, are worthy of such an honor. There is just one catch, since you aren''t an official member we need something in exchange for this gift. Cough up 1 x Caldari Navy Raid Leader Insignia and the Gila Blueprint is yours. Dismissed'),
(93389,0,5,25268,20,0,'COSMOS Guristas COSMOS / Trade',500010,0,0,'Trade 20x Amber Cytoserocin (200{{m3','Ah, it''s nice to see a friendly face around here for a change, <Pilot>. But to answer your question, I came here to investigate Constellation E-8CSQ, which has been reported to contain massive gas clouds full of material used in booster manufacturing. There have been a lot of rumors about it within Guristas, and I thought I''d take a look for myself. Unfortunately, the number of rogue drones and outlaws here has me quite worried, so I dare not go looking for the clouds myself. Hence, I might have a job for you... However, I suggest you refrain from accepting my task unless you have access to a gas cloud harvester module. Without that, you will just be wasting my time.'),
(93390,0,3,25364,1,5,'COSMOS Guristas COSMOS / Security',500001,16796,5,'Acquire 1 x Black Jack''s DNA (0.1 m³)','I''m in charge of security for the Minedrill expedition forces stationed here in E-8CSQ. As you probably know this is risky space, but even so we''ve been harassed by the same pirate far too many times for it to be coincidence. Also upon investigating the matter further, I discovered that this pirate is in fact called ''Black Jack'', a notorious felon who terrorized Molden Heath not too long ago. There was a documentary about him released by The Scope ... Anyway, if you find him then kill him for me, please. He''s been the bane of too many of my colleagues and has been making quite a fool out of my security division in fact. There are many stories floating around which tell of his greatly exaggerated victories over my men and those of the Navy guarding the civilian excavators. Now if you could bring me something to prove he''s dead, his DNA would probably do, then I''ll be able to vindicate the reputation of the security division here in Kois City. Now as for finding Black Jack, I have absolutely no clue. You could try searching for him with your scanners, but that''s about all I can tell you. I''ve tried looking for him near the habitation module they call ''Black Jack''s Shack'', but he''s never there. Somehow I doubt you''ll find him, but good luck regardless ...'),
(93391,0,3,25369,1,5,'COSMOS Guristas COSMOS / Security',500001,16796,5,'Acquire 1 x Airkio Yanjulen''s Corpse (1.0{{m3','Now on to the big fish. As you undoubtedly know, our biggest threat in E-8CSQ has been the Guristas organization. Although they seem to be quite disorganized, as you would expect for a pirate organization, their top man here is rumored to be Airkio Yanjulen, a commander residing in O-LR1H. Killing him should weaken them considerably ... at least I hope so. Bring me proof of his death and I''ll reward you generously. The last I heard he was stationed in the Guristas War Installation in one of their outposts within O-LR1H. You will have to use your system scanner in that system and search for the ''Iacta Space Plain'' to find him. This is an important mission, which will have significant impact on your faction standings.'),
(93392,0,5,25268,20,0,'COSMOS Guristas COSMOS / Trade',500010,0,0,'Trade 20x Amber Cytoserocin (200{{m3','Ah, it''s nice to see a friendly face around here for a change, <Pilot>. But to answer your question, I came here to investigate Constellation E-8CSQ, which has been reported to contain massive gas clouds full of material used in booster manufacturing. There have been a lot of rumors about it within Guristas, and I thought I''d take a look for myself. Unfortunately, the number of rogue drones and outlaws here has me quite worried, so I dare not go looking for the clouds myself. Hence, I might have a job for you... However, I suggest you refrain from accepting my task unless you have access to a gas cloud harvester module. Without that, you will just be wasting my time.'),
(93393,0,5,15657,1,0,'COSMOS Guristas COSMOS / ?',500010,0,0,'Acquire and deliver 1x Caldari Navy Fleet Commander Insignia (0.1{{m3','We have a policy here within the Guristas Pirates that our more prominent members fly a suitable ship according to their status, both to give them an edge during combat and to uphold our image, especially within our borders. We have recently decided to extend this benefit to mercenaries or freelancers employed by us that have shown admirable bravery and skill in the field, or earned the right through countless hours of dedicated service to our corporations. As you undoubtedly already know I have been assigned the task of allocating these ships to their deserved owners. After looking at your record, we decided that you, <Pilot>, are worthy of such an honor. There is just one catch, since you aren''t an official member we need something in exchange for this gift. Cough up 1 x Caldari Navy Fleet Commander Insignia and the Rattlesnake Blueprint is yours. Dismissed'),
(93394,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Guristas COSMOS / Security',500006,11076,5,'Take out the CONCORD Army General then report back to your agent.','Makeinu has a thorn in its side that I want drawn out, the sooner the better. As you might know, some of our residents have had a fairly violent history. And it so happens that DED felt the urge to send assassins all the way out here to settle the score with a couple of my people who had some run-ins with the law some time ago. Or this could be a private vendetta by an angry DED commander. Who knows? But either way, they need to be dealt with before they find us. We''re ill equipped to deal with an encounter like that, and quite frankly most of us are too old and worn out to fight. I''ve had the DED squadron tracked for some time now. I''ll upload a bookmark to their current location into your journal. Find them and take out their leader ― that should be enough to send them crawling back to their homeland with their tails between their collective legs.'),
(93395,0,3,25408,1,5,'COSMOS Guristas COSMOS / Security',500010,16796,5,'Transport 1 x Akkeshu Karuan''s DNA (0.1 m³) to -0.2 Rakka''s Rattlesnake in Y5J-EU. (Low Sec Warning!)','Yes, your next assignment is a little more personal in nature. You see, I was born and raised in the Venal system, and during my teens I joined the Guristas militia. I never knew my parents, but I assume they were loyal to the Guristas. I did have a few comrades that I could call friends, and my life was relatively stable. But then came the assignment that would change everything. I was sent to E-8CSQ to find and apprehend a traitor, Akkeshu Karuan. My orders were specific, to bring him back dead or alive to Jirai Laitanen at the Guristas headquarters. I was not to return, not ever, until and unless this task was accomplished. I never questioned my orders, and frankly I don''t give a damn what Akkeshu was accused of. For my entire life, I have known nothing other than the Guristas, the organization that fed and clothed me during my darkest of times, and I owe them my life. But unfortunately the mission did not go as planned. I fought Akkeshu and his men inside what is now known as "Cadaver Reef." I was victorious in that battle, but Akkeshu still slipped through my grasp. He and what remained of his gang fled deeper into the deadspace pocket, and of course I followed with the fleet under my command. That action turned out to be a terrible mistake. Akkeshu knew the area like the back of his hand, and he managed to use that knowledge to his advantage. Once he warped away from our targeting systems, all we could find was an acceleration gate. When we activated it, it propelled us deeper into the rock-filled deadspace complex. But somehow Akkeshu had managed to reconfigure the gate, and instead of finding him on the other side, we were sent straight into a massive drone hive. We put up a brave fight and managed to destroy the hive, but at enormous cost. The fleet was shattered, and I was left with a force so small we could not hope to face Akkeshu again. So here I am, all these years later, rotting in a town filled with hopelessness and depression. I so yearn to return to my roots, but I know that if I do so, I will be promptly executed for my failure. I am now too old and out of practice to attempt to find Akkeshu again. But considering how well you dealt with your last mission, I have hope that perhaps you can succeed where I failed. All I ask for is evidence of Akkeshu''s death; with that, I can return to my homeland and hopefully redeem myself, dying in peace among my own people. I do not have many years left, and you cannot imagine how much I wish to spend them in the land of my birth instead of a place like Makeinu Town. Find Cadaver Reef. Use scan probes. Bring me proof of Akkeshu''s demise, and I will give you my most prized possessions.'),
(93396,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Guristas COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'','During my research of the Guristas movements through E-8CSQ, I discovered that most of the Guristas squadrons flying through G5ED-Y originate from a certain outpost within O-LR1H. I believe that''s where their command post in E-8CSQ is located. Not only that but local rumor has it that many of the Guristas ships currently stationed in E-8CSQ have only recently arrived to the constellation. So my conclusion naturally is that a large portion of the Guristas forces that have been harassing us here lately are part of an assembly of fighters recently allocated here by the Guristas central command in 6NJ8-V. With this in mind I would also assume they are acting on specific orders and not randomly attacking us when the opportunity arrives, like is often the case with pirates in these parts. Now if I could only get a hold of their plans, I would have some good news finally to present to Admiral Aurobe Kois. Knowledge of their next move would give us a huge advantage. Acquiring this knowledge is of course easier said than done. This is where you come in. Your job, obviously, is to acquire this data. And I know of two ways to do it. Your first option is to befriend one of their leaders within the Iacta Space Plain in O-LR1H and somehow acquire the information through him. This is of course highly difficult and only possible if you are in good standing with the Guristas organization. Your second option is to rescue the last agent I sent on the very same task, Otsalen Mano. He found something, but before he could return to me his identity was discovered. He''s currently being held in one of their prison facilities near the Iacta Space Plain in O-LR1H. And there''s nothing I can do about it until I get more firepower ... Anyway, don''t return until you have the Guristas war plans!'),
(93397,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Guristas COSMOS / Encounter',500001,16796,5,'Destroy Guristas armory and retrieve Guristas Armory Codes (0.1{{m3','The most important task is behind us, but there are a couple more assignments that I''d like you to accomplish before you leave. The first of these assignments is to destroy a small armory near G5ED-Y II. It''s being used to re-supply Guristas fighters in the system, and therefore must be destroyed. You may keep any of the supplies found inside, but do bring back some evidence of its demise. The armory is in a deadspace pocket hidden from passive sensors. You will need to use probes to scan it down.'),
(93398,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Guristas COSMOS / Security',500010,16796,5,'Wait for the Guristas squadron, then destroy it','The last thing I want you to do for me is to intercept a squadron of Guristas fighters who recently came through the stargate from O-LR1H. They''ve been following a certain expedition of ours, no doubt waiting for the right time to attack. Little beknownst to them we''ve been tracking their every move. Now I expect them to show up at a certain point in G5ED-Y any moment now, and I want you to be waiting there for that to happen. Once they appear, shoot them down immediately.'),
(93399,0,5,25268,20,0,'COSMOS Guristas COSMOS / Trade',500010,0,0,'Trade 20x Amber Cytoserocin (200{{m3','Ah, it''s nice to see a friendly face around here for a change, <Pilot>. But to answer your question, I came here to investigate Constellation E-8CSQ, which has been reported to contain massive gas clouds full of material used in booster manufacturing. There have been a lot of rumors about it within Guristas, and I thought I''d take a look for myself. Unfortunately, the number of rogue drones and outlaws here has me quite worried, so I dare not go looking for the clouds myself. Hence, I might have a job for you... However, I suggest you refrain from accepting my task unless you have access to a gas cloud harvester module. Without that, you will just be wasting my time.'),
(93400,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500002,0,0,'',''),
(93401,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500002,0,0,'',''),
(93402,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500003,0,0,'',''),
(93403,0,3,21810,5,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500011,17138,5,'Retrieve 5x Spy ID Slice',''),
(93404,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500011,17138,5,'Retrieve',''),
(93405,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500003,0,0,'',''),
(93406,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500003,0,0,'',''),
(93407,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500003,0,0,'',''),
(93408,0,1,43,1000,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Courier',0,0,0,'Deliver 1,000 x Antibiotics (200m³)','Hello there, friend. I have come to this wicked place in order to help out the surviors of the conflict that has been going on recently. Drug barons, murderers, hoaxers and other scum infest this constellation, and they show no mercy when dealing with the defenseless locals. We need to reach out and lend our aid to those in need of it. I need you to deliver these antibiotics to <Station>. Some kind of epidemic seems to be spreading out there and hopefully this should be enough to cure the infected ones.'),
(93409,0,1,3717,5,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Courier',0,0,0,'Deliver 5 x Dairy Products (2.5m³)','Those antibiotics you delivered were useless, the epidemic has spread across the entire planet and I don''t think there''s anything we can do to help those people any more. The doctors there have become infected themselves and nobody has any idea what the sickness is or what it''s made of. However, my friend, I do have other jobs for you. The refugee camp at <Station> is running low on supplies. I want you to deliver these dairy products to the officials there for them to give to the needy. Please complete this as quickly as possible, people''s lives are at stake.'),
(93410,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500002,0,0,'',''),
(93411,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500002,0,0,'',''),
(93412,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500002,0,0,'',''),
(93413,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500002,17138,5,'Retrieve Kutill''s data chip','If you look over near the ruins of the old Pleasure Gardens, you''ll see that no-good thief Rozor Mothrus. He appeared here at the Carnival a few months ago, claiming to be ''just another passerby''. What a rotten lie that was. From the moment I saw him I knew there was something out of place ... Anyway, we spent some time in the Carnival pub, and I happened to get caught up in a conversation with him about this and that. I was fairly intoxicated at the time, so I can''t remember much of it, but somehow he managed to drag out of me the location of my hideout in Barkrik. It''s a nice little spot inside an area of space which we call ''deadspace'', near an asteroid belt filled with low-life miners and rogue mechanical drones, not exactly a family resort if you know what I mean. But for someone like me avoiding those pests is not much of a problem, and it''s the perfect hiding place when you have a run in with the law. Now if allowing him to discover my favorite hiding place isn''t enough, it so happens that I stashed my latest invention, a very valuable hacker-program, in a storage container right there! It''s my only copy, and very very illegal here in Minmatar space. If Rozor gets his grubby hands on it, I''m ruined! Now you might be thinking, why don''t I just run over there and pick up the data chip? Well, the problem is Rozor has apparently hired some Maru mercs to do the dirty work for him. The last time I tried to enter the asteroid belt leading to the storage bin, I noticed some of them hiding by the miner''s quarters. I escaped without them noticing me, and after some info-digging I found out they had been hired by Rozor. I want you to fly out there and see if the Maru have miraculously not found the data chip I had hidden in the storage bin. If you find it, bring it to me for a sizable reward.'),
(93414,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500002,0,0,'',''),
(93415,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500002,0,0,'','There''s just one last thing I need done before we''re through, MeatWar. Ever since you retrieved that data chip for me, Rozor Mothrus has been extremely ''excited''. I''m afraid he might strike at any moment, if he learns what I''m up to. But I can''t take him and his buddies by myself. You''ll probably find Machul and 3 Brutor mercenaries orbiting Rozor''s ship. When you do, take them out, and bring me Machul''s head from the wreckage if you can. I''ll use it to tease Rozor ... right before I put an end to his miserable existence.'),
(93416,0,3,22254,1,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500002,17138,5,'Acquire 1x Rekker''s Keycard (0.1{{m3','I settled here in Nakugard many years ago, lured to this place by tales of riches and glory spread by the Republic Parliament who''ve been desperate to populate Ani with loyal supporters of the Republic. But I''ve never felt at home here, and ever since I discovered I was sharing space with minions of the Amarr Empire I''ve felt betrayed and depressed. These people are responsible for some of the most terrible crimes in human history! And they''re living under the protection of those that have sworn to protect us, the Republic government! I couldn''t believe it at first ... Apparently Karin Midular made a deal with Joint Harvesting a few years back to allow them to build a few stations and plantations in Ani. I don''t care how much ISK they had to pay to get this deal through, or the fact they pretended to apologize for the Empire''s crimes before the Rebellion. An Amarrian is an Amarrian, they''ll never change, and as long as their people are located within Minmatar space I will not be at peace. And fortunately there are more within the Krusual Tribe who think the same way. There is a growing movement within the Krusual settlements in Ani which aims at uprooting the Amarr presence in this constellation. We already have a large fleet of ships ready to strike at any moment. Our first target is a ''secret'' plantation within Hjoramold, called the Jakela Plantation. We managed to discover it by using system scanners, and we''ve even heard rumors from there that they are using slaves to work the fields! Our only problem is that our agents haven''t found a way through their second acceleration gate. It''s being guarded by an Amarrian called Rekker, and a few of his henchmen. They aren''t much of a problem for our forces, but we''re afraid that if we send in an entire battalion he''ll simply flee at the first sight of us and take his keycard with him. What I want you to do, Pilot, is take a small fleet of ships and launch a surprise attack against Rekker. Loot his keycard and bring it back to me, that way we''ll be able to access the acceleration gate leading deeper into the plantation grounds. You''ll have to do this fast, before they change the gate''s security system when they figure out Rekker has been killed. Once you''re back here with the keycard I''ll supply you with your reward.'),
(93417,0,1,9844,500,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Courier',500002,0,0,'Transport 500x Small Arms (1,000{{m3','Since you managed to accomplish my first task with aplomb, I''ve decided you''re worthy of another highly important mission for our cause. There are a large number of civilians in Ani who have offered to join our ranks during our campaign to rid the constellation of Amarr, but we don''t have the weapons to spare to arm them. One of my contacts within the Republic Security forces has promised us a large shipment of small arms which we''ll use to equip our new troops with. The only catch is that this shipment is currently located in Floseswin, which is a pretty dangerous area. Which makes this job perfect for someone like you, <Pilot>. Get the shipment of small arms here in one piece and I''ll give you a generous reward.'),
(93418,0,3,22277,1,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500002,17138,5,'Acquire 1x Kyan Magdesh''s DNA (0.1{{m3','If you''re still willing I have one final mission that I think you''re suited for. The Joint Harvesting corporation has become aware of our presence and we believe they are preparing for a counter-attack against our forces. Finding a Mordu''s mercenary in Ani confirmed our suspicions, we''re certain these Mordu''s goons were hired by Joint Harvesting to sabotage our operation. Not only that, but they apparently sent a Magdesh after us. The Magdesh are a powerful family within the Mordu''s Legion, highly respected bounty hunters. One of their members, Kyan, is currently hauled up in Barkrik I - Asteroid Belt 1. He''s been spotted on numerous occasions snooping around near our outposts there, but never long enough for our guards to catch him. I would like you to take care of this pest, before he manages to do us any harm. Just be warned, he operates a Caldari battleship and is not to be taken lightly. You might need help on this one, <Pilot>. Good luck.'),
(93419,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500003,0,0,'',''),
(93420,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500003,0,0,'',''),
(93421,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500003,0,0,'',''),
(93422,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500011,17138,5,'Kill, and Retrieve DNA Samples of Republic Commandos',''),
(93423,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500002,0,0,'',''),
(93424,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500002,0,0,'',''),
(93425,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500002,0,0,'',''),
(93426,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500002,0,0,'',''),
(93427,0,5,21570,4,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Trade',500002,0,0,'Acquire 4x Sleeper Manuscripts (4{{m3','A clan sister of mine owns a quaint little curiosities shop back in Pator. She sells all kind of weird and wonderful items from around the known EVE universe. When she heard I was coming here to Ani, she asked me to have a look around for items for her shop. Of course, I''m happy to oblige. I expected to pick up a few Nefantar artifacts at most, but something else has caught my eye. While digging through an old spa here in Lanngisi, I came upon a most fascinating old manuscript, written in a language I''m unfamiliar with. I sent it to my clan sister and it thrilled her. She wants me to search for more. I haven''t found any more here in Lanngisi, but I''ve heard from reliable sources that more can be found over in an old ruin in Inder. So I''m looking for pilots such as you to help me out. Bring me some manuscripts and I''ll pay you 15 000 ISK. Of course, you have to have some basic knowledge of archeology before you can make head or tail of what you find.'),
(93428,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',0,0,0,'','Welcome to this humble refugee camp operated by us, the Sisters of EVE. I am Fynnir Torsont, please call me Fynnir. We''re swamped here at the camp and I''m on the lookout for volunteers of gentle spirit to lend aid. Even if no one will admit it, there is a war raging here in Traun. Every day numerous skirmishes take place all over the system. I have no idea which side is winning, if any. If there are any sides, that is. No one seems to know who exactly is fighting whom. There are Republic forces here, Minmatar freedom fighters, Angel Cartel pirates, Thukker tribe nomads, Amarrians, you name it. We Sisters of EVE try to stay impartial in this chaos, it is often hard and always thankless. But someone needs to care for the weak, and I don''t see the empires volunteering anything. Every war, no matter the scale, always has its share of atrocities and this one is no different. I can''t even start describing them, its too long and too sad a tale. Yet one requires mentioning. Recently a group of refugees arrived here in the camp. They are workers from an independent asteroid colony in a distant part of the system. When they arrived some of them showed symptoms of some unidentified illness and thus they were quarantined. Now, all of them are sick, many dying, or are already dead. We don''t have the resources here in the camp to determine what is causing this illness, but I have my suspicions. I don''t think any of the factions slugging it out here are beneath chemical warfare and I fear that may be the case here. But investigating those suspicions must wait for another time. What matters now is getting the infected refugees to our station in the Lanngisi system, where they can be properly treated. Or at least receive their last rites in some peace and quiet. Time is of the essence here, their condition is grim and grows worse by the hour. If you''re willing to take the task of ferrying some of them over to the Lanngisi system I will reward you well, but you can earn much more if you get them all there safely in just 40 minutes. Oh, and don''t worry, they will be properly quarantined on the journey too.'),
(93429,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500011,17138,5,'Kill all the pirates and destroy the infected laboratory. Get the formula (Formula for Septicemic Agent 0.1 m³) and bring it back to finish the mission.','I''ve been doing some investigation while you were away and I''ve managed to dig up some promising leads. It''s amazing really the amount of information one can get here in the camp. Here you can find people from all the warring factions all mingled together. It can get hairy at times. But some are more talkative than others and if you know what you''re looking for you can get some valuable insights around here. Anyway, from the clues I''ve pieced together it seems that my suspicion was indeed correct. A very dangerous man-made viral agent was indeed involved in the tragic demise of the colonists. But they''ve got no one but themselves to blame. It seems they were not telling the truth when they pleaded their ignorance about the whole thing. I already suspected as much from earlier rumors, but it was confirmed when I was contacted by a fellow Sister in our station in Lanngisi. Turns out one of the colonists spilled his beans on his deathbed and confessed. The colonists were hired to manufacture the deadly agent. By whom I do not yet know. I can understand why the colonists agreed; the constant warfare in the system has not treated its inhabitants well. It was probably a matter of either accepting this deal or abandoning their homes for them. Yet though I can understand their actions, I can not condone them. Viral agents are an abomination and one so potent and this one obviously is could utterly destroy whole eco-systems. We need to determine exactly what this viral agent is and whether it has gotten into the wrong hands. If you''re up to it, I would be ecstatic if you could head over to the asteroid colony and snoop around. You should be able to locate the lab quite easily; it''s probably not part of the main colony. Blowing it to pieces is a good first step in eradicating this evil viral agent from the world. If you could also get your hands on the agent formula, that would be even better. For that kind of information I would be willing to give you a solid implant as a reward.'),
(93430,0,3,21852,1,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500011,17138,5,'Acquire 1x Sample of Septicemic Agent (0.5 m³)','Your work has been of immense value to us, <Pilot>. Not to mention the service you''re doing the world. Not that it will thank you, mind you. It''s something us Sisters get used to. Anyway, our scientists are already pouring over the formula you brought us. I hope they will be able to come up with an antidote soon so the threat can be neutralized. I''m still trying to get to the bottom of who hired the doomed colonists to manufacture the viral agent. There are many candidates, but I''m especially interested in one group. They call themselves the Cybertrons. Pretty lame name if you ask me. They hang out at the local contested complex, though I think they''re only loosely connected to the cartel. Might be some Amarr lord is behind this mysterious group, but I can''t be sure. I need some proof that the Cybertrons are behind this. Then I can approach the appropriate authorities with my knowledge and hope they do something about it. Or deal with them the Sister''s way. Let''s not get into that. The Cybertrons are pretty tough, so I''ll understand if you decline to take them on. But if you''re willing, I''ll give you a rare BPC as a reward. Start taking these Cybertron guys down until one of them drops something I can use against them.'),
(93431,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500002,17138,5,'Find and destroy ST58 and bring his AI chip (ST58 Memory Chip 0.1{{m3','Well, it''s rather complicated. But to keep it simple, I''ll give you the short version. A few days ago, I completed my latest project, the ST 50 series. They were supposed to be ultra-intelligent fighter drones, specifically ordered by the Minmatar Fleet to serve in our armed forces. In all of the tests I performed on them, they seemed to be in fine condition, easily dispatching all the previous models in our combat simulation tests. However, shortly after they were released from our lab and sent into action, they went missing. The loss was an enormous blow to Boundless Creation, especially considering all the time, effort, and money we spent creating those things. The sortie that they were on when they went missing was to attack a massive rogue drone hive within Barkrik. They were accompanied by over a dozen human pilots, who also haven''t been seen since. I''m not sure exactly what happened there, but a rumor is spreading that they were overwhelmed and captured by the rogue drone mothership. I can''t imagine such a thing happening, but... Anyway, a few days later we heard of a terrible tragedy in Hjoramold. An entire settlement was destroyed by rampaging rogue drones. I didn''t think much of it at the time, considering rogue drone attacks are pretty frequent in these parts, but later that day I turned on the evening news I heard something that chilled me to the bone. The recent rogue drone attacks were led by none other than one of my own ST drones! I couldn''t believe my ears at first, but it was true. I don''t know how, but the rogue drones have somehow managed to reconfigure the ST''s AI chip and turn it into a rampaging monster! It must be stopped at all costs; its existence is a terrible blow to my career, and the more damage it causes, the more likely I am to lose my job. You must help me! Unfortunately, the rogues seem to have deactivated the tracking devices I had installed into the STs. However, I have managed to triangulate the location of two of them, and the third has already been destroyed by local independent capsuleers. You''ll find ST 58 at the bookmarked location that I''m about to upload into your NeoCom, floating around a deadspace pocket filled with asteroids. Please bring back its memory chip so that I can study it and find out what went wrong.'),
(93432,0,3,22203,4,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500002,17138,5,'Acquire 4x Angel Drug Addict Tag (0.4{{m3','Why have you come here? You don''t actually believe that you''re good enough to receive my training? Well, perhaps. I''ll give you one chance, if you don''t screw it up, then maybe there is hope for your misguided soul. Set your destination for the solar system of Tvink. There is an old Guerilla outpost there, and currently it is being fought over by several different factions. I want you to go there and kill as many Angel Cartel Officers as you can. Bring their dogtags back to me as proof of you actions.'),
(93433,0,1,22102,1,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Courier',500002,0,0,'Transport 1x ST 59 Memory Chip (0.1{{m3','Model ST 59 has somehow ended up in Evati, many jumps from here. It was destroyed by militia forces in the system, and its remains transferred to the Republic Justice Department station there. I made a deal with them to allow me to access the memory chip to investigate the cause of the malfunction, but I couldn''t find a convoy heading to Hjoramold in time. Could you fetch it for me ASAP? I have to return it in a couple of weeks, so the faster you get it here, the better.'),
(93434,0,3,22205,1,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500002,17138,5,'Acquire 1x Godun Sakt''s Diamond Drill (10{{m3','You have gained a little trust now, complete another mission for me and I will consider you not entirely useless. A few months ago, my personal quarters were broken in to and a few items very dear to my heart stolen. One of these items was a special diamond-edged drill I use to cut rare minerals and rocks. I want you to retrieve this item for me. Go back to the contested Guerilla Outpost in Tvink and retrieve it for me. I''m certain that one of the criminals hanging out there must be carrying it.'),
(93435,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Trade',500002,0,0,'Acquire ST 60 Memory Chip (0.1{{m3','The last drone memory chip I need you to fetch is ST 60''s. The ''60 is my finest drone of the ST series, a prototype, and certainly a force to be reckoned with. I think you might have to find some friends to help you take it on ― yes, it''s really that tough, if I do say so myself. It''s currently orbiting a rogue drone installation near Hjoramold XII Moon I, located deep within what we call "Glittermore," the xenon gas cloud of Hjoramold XII. It''s a very hostile part of space, but a magnificent sight nonetheless and one frequented by tourists. Good luck finding those drones, <Pilot>.'),
(93436,0,3,22214,1,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500002,17138,5,'Acquire 1x Godun Sakt''s Questionable Holoreel (0.5{{m3','Another task for you, I have. I want you to retrieve one more of my stolen item for me. This time it is a holoreel that is very dear to my heart. It contains... personal videos of questionable quality and legality. I ask that you do not look at it, but only go and find it and deliver to me. I''m certain that the pirates at the contested Guerilla outpost in Tvink must have it.'),
(93437,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500002,0,0,'',''),
(93438,0,5,3683,25,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Trade',0,0,0,'Acquire 25x Oxygen (5{{m3','Perhaps you have heard about what goes on here? If you have, then take some friendly advice and keep it a secret; it''s for your own good. If you haven''t heard about what we do here, then I suppose you''re no threat to us. Anyway, I suppose you''re here for work. Well, that´s good ― working is what we do. This operation flourished before the Republic started meddling in our business. Of course, they have no idea we work for Thukker ... and if they did we would be in big trouble. Now, on to your first task. To maintain the integrity and security of our laboratories, we have a constant need for antibiotics. Find me some, and I will give you another task.'),
(93439,0,1,22218,1,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Courier',0,0,0,'Deliver 1x Drug Delivery Package (10{{m3','I have a large order that needs filling. Perhaps you''d be up to the task of delivering it for me? The customer is waiting at Tvink. His payment has already been taken care of, so you needn''t worry about that. Deliver this package and report back to me for your next assignment. Declining a mission from a particular agent more than once every 4 hours may result in a loss of standing with that agent, except in the case of special missions that clearly state otherwise in their description.'),
(93440,0,3,22194,4,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',0,0,0,'Acquire 4 x Minmatar Republic Narcotic Officer''s Tag (0.4{{m3','Those cursed Republic agents are constantly trying to discover where our operations are based. They have officers all over the constellation searching for illicit substances. Can you believe they think we´re in the agriculture business? Hah, that''s a good one! We need to show these cops that we aren''t afraid of them. I want you to be the one to carry out that task, Maydie Chieves. Go to the contested guerilla base and kill as many of their officers as you can. Bring five of theirs tags back to me as proof. Declining a mission from a particular agent more than once every 4 hours may result in a loss of standing with that agent, except in the case of special missions that clearly state otherwise in their description.'),
(93441,0,1,22208,2,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Courier',0,0,0,'Deliver 2x Prostitute (2{{m3','Finally, business is back on track. Well, doing better than before you arrived, at least. Your assistance has helped us a great deal, my friend. I have one more task for you, though, before I give you your reward. We have a friend in the Minmatar police ― some would call him a "dirty cop," but I, like many others, prefer to think of him as a patron of free trade. Heh. Anyway, he´s been having some trouble with women lately and we like helping out our friends, so I want you to take these to Hjoramold III - Joint Harvesting Plantation and leave them there. I''m certain they´ll bring a smile to his face, if you know what I mean ... and I think you do.'),
(93442,0,3,22074,1,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500002,17138,5,'Acquire 1x Gist Database Codes (1{{m3','Ah, a capsuleer. I see. In that case, you might be of some use after all. Fair enough. I''ve been trying to hack into the Gist database in their stronghold within Hjoramold for some time now, but I can''t get by their security codes. Get me those codes, and I''ll make you rich. Deal? Oh, yeah, you might find them off the Gist overseer Arrak Nutan. He usually roams around Hraldar''s ruins, within the old Legendary Stronghold. {{Co|red|The acceleration gate leading into the complex is inaccessible for anything bigger than a battlecruiser, but the Gist have manufactured a few battleships inside the deadspace pockets.}} Needless to say, this Overseer Nutan flies one of them.'),
(93443,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Courier',500002,0,0,'Transport reports (0.1 m3)','Get these reports to the Republic Security Forces base in Uisper. My cousin works as an officer there. The reports contain information on Angel Cartel plans and smuggling routes, which I extracted from the Gist database within Hjoramold. This information is way too important to just send through conventional means; I can''t risk the transmission being hacked. Once my cousin gets a hold of these reports and presents them directly to Bjongausen Agnake, I''m sure he''ll get a promotion.'),
(93444,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500011,17138,5,'Eliminate Kael Nutan and his henchmen, then report back to Jippon Frain.','Something''s come up that''s perfectly suited to your ... er, talents. The Gist somehow managed to track down the signal from my computer while I was busy hacking their database. They shut me out and changed their codes. Fortunately, the interference from the Hyperbole Nexus prevented them from finding my exact location, but they at least know who I am. Apparently, the assassin they sent to deal with me is none other than Kael Nutan, the son of the Gist overseer you killed earlier. Kael is a much better combat pilot than his dad ever was, certainly a force to be reckoned with. He completely obliterated my residence here in Barkrik, despite all the booby-traps I had laid for his men. If you could fly to the coordinates of my residence and take care of Kael and his henchmen, I would be eternally grateful. Just don''t expect it to be easy: You''ll have to face a large squadron of Gist ships, including Kael''s battleship, which is one of the best in their entire armada. I wish you luck, <Pilot> ― you''re gonna need it.'),
(93445,0,5,3683,150,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Trade',500002,0,0,'Acquire 150x Oxygen (57{{m3','I own and operate a portable arena of cyboerians, cybernetically augmented gladiators who fight each other for show, demonstrating a wide range of Matari martial arts. I was having problems generating revenue in my old home, so I relocated to Nakugard. Shortly after I got here, though, a problem reared its head. Obviously I''d underestimated the extend of influence wielded by the criminal element in this area. Within weeks, most of my fighters were strung out on various illicit drugs, and I''ve since had to close up shop. Can''t have a show if you don''t have performers. And to make matters worse, my contract with the Leisure Group is still in full effect; if I''m nit generating my revenue they''re not going to be happy, and we most definitely do not want the Leisure Group unhappy. There are a few things I need to be able to get mu arena up and running again. Among these is oxygen; I can''t very well run the place if no one can breath, you understand, if you can go out and find me 150 units of oxygen, I''d be much obliged.'),
(93446,0,3,22321,1,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500011,17138,5,'Acquire 1x Grace Tarsis (1 m3)','I have three fighters on hand right now, but I need more to be able to run my show. I just received word, that one of my best, Grace Tarsis, is being held by a group of Cartel thugs in a deadspace location here in Nakugard, on account of some unsettled debts. If you can find her and bring her back to me in one piece, I''ll be a step closer to re-opening my arena and evading the Leisure Group''s wrath. They''re keeping her in a brothel in their lair. one that''s not really that heavily guarded. If you kill the guards and blow up the brothel, you should be able to get her out and bring her back. If you can do that you will have my heartfelt thanks.'),
(93447,0,3,21809,8,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500002,17138,5,'Acquire 8x Hacker ID Slice (0.8{{m3','Welcome to the frontline. You may not see it, but it''s here all the same. I was sent out here three months ago to take care of a ''minor pirate problem'', as I was told. It was only supposed to take a month, but I''m still here and I don''t think I''ll be going home any time soon. See that station, or what''s left of it, over there? That station was supposed to be our headquarters. It was sabotaged a month ago, someone infiltrated the station and planted one big bomb in its bowels. I was one of the lucky few out on a patrol that day, or my body would by floating around here along with the rest. I''m telling you, it''s a total mess around here at the moment. Poor Murchor over there is trying to install some order, but he''s in way over his head. Me? I''m just trying to stay alive in all this chaos. A lot of soldiers have fled and I can''t blame them. But I''m not a deserter. All I can do is try to do my job and hope it will get easier. Like the Republic actually acting up on its promise to send reinforcement out here. There are pirates all around here, and something much more. But I''m mainly concerned with the pirates; they''re my top priority. And I want to make them your top priority too. I''ll pay you good money to bring me some Hacker ID Slices. These hacker scums have been causing us all sorts of trouble, lurking in the shadows all the time. It wouldn''t surprise me if they are behind the sabotage of the station. You can find them in the contested military complex in this system, and elsewhere too.'),
(93448,0,1,21930,1,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Courier',500002,0,0,'Transport 1x Sealed case of GI Paradise Missiles (250{{m3','I''m finally starting to see some progress around here. No thanks to the Republic though. It''s mainly down to independent pilots such as yourself that the system isn''t being totally overrun by pirates. And to the rebels. Yeah, I know they''re whacky and delusional, but at least they''re actively fighting all those opposing the Republic here in Ani. I can''t count the number of times they''ve saved my ass in the last few weeks. Though I can''t agree with their agenda, I can approve of their methods. But let me get to the point. In the chaos we have here whole shiploads of army goods are being misplaced, mishandled or simply stolen every day. I got my hands on some pretty neat GI Paradise Cruise Missiles the other day, don''t ask how. These GI versions are the blast. I''ve befriended some of the more sane rebels and I want to pay them back for all the help they''ve given me. I have a crate of the missiles sitting in a hangar on a station in Hek. I''m not stupid enough to have them in my own cargo hold in case old Merchor over there gets nosy all of a sudden. There''s a rebel guy waiting on the Sister of EVE station here in Traun waiting for the delivery. All I need is someone capable to get the missiles to him. Interested? I can offer you some pretty rare Republic ammo as a reward.'),
(93449,0,3,21971,1,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500002,17138,5,'Acquire 1x Broken ComLink Scanner (2{{m3','I''ve been ordered to support our troops in the contested complex here in Traun. We''re trying to wrench control for it from the Angel cartel. It''s not going all that well, so I''ve been expecting this for some time. I don''t like jumping into a situation totally unprepared, so I''ve been gathering what information about what is really going on there. The general Republic communication lines don''t yield all that much useful information, but through the contacts I''m building with the rebels I actually found out some pretty important thing. It seems the Angels in the complex, or one of the groups associated with them, have managed to tap into the Republic communication links. No wonder nothing has been going for our troops, all they''re movements are known beforehand. Beats me how they did it, but it needs to be dealt with. I''m trying to get the brass to act upon this, but they just point at each other. I know it''s hopeless for me to talk directly to our guys in the complex, it will only be intercepted. But you''re not part of the Republic''s line of communications so you can act freely. I know the Angels are using a scanner housed in an old Nefantar tactical depot in the complex. I don''t know if it''s the only one they''re operating, but let''s start by hitting that one and see what happens. At least it will make me feel a little bit better when I move in there myself sometimes in the near future. Get me a piece of the scanner array. You may have to hit several of the scanners before a useful specimen comes up. Do this for me and I got this rare BPC to give you.'),
(93450,0,1,22220,10,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Courier',500003,0,0,'Transport 10 x Mind-Altering Drugs (10 m3) from a station to agent.','Hello there. You are here for work? Well, you might just be the one I´m looking for. We can look out for each other´s interests. I have a few tasks in mind for you: If you complete them in a timely fashion and without making any mistakes, then I will give you a handsome reward. I''ll be honest with you; I run a highly lucrative business that some people claim involves illegal substances and slavery. I won´t deny that some people would find my line of work somewhat ... hm, distasteful is the word, I guess. Heh. Anyway, I control my slaves using mind-altering drugs that few people know or care much about. Of course, keeping this a secret is now for your own good. Nobody likes mishaps where people get killed, if you know what I mean. Okay, you seem solid so far. You want to know more? Alright. I have a delivery coming in from Uttindar V - Moon 17 - Minmatar Mining Corporation Mining Outpost. Go pick it up for me, alright? Some of the slaves get restless without their medicine.'),
(93451,0,1,3814,3,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Courier',500003,0,0,'Transport 3 x Reports (0.3 m3) from agent to a station.','Dammit, dammit, dammit! Once again, the narcs are causing me bloody trouble. My inside man just told me that they launched an official investigation against my operation. They''re on to me and are trying to figure out what it is that I actually do here. This is bad news for us, character_name. We have to get them to close their investigation. I´ve got an idea how to solve this mess, though. If we co-operate with them and get them to think we have nothing to hide, maybe they''ll go away. Take these reports to Inder VII - Moon 11 - Sisters of EVE Bureau. They contain fake data on all our assets, journals, and transaction logs. If this isn''t enough to convince them we''re not up to anything, I don''t know what will.'),
(93452,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500003,0,0,'Acquire 1 X Godun Sakt''s Diamond Drill (10 m3)','Frack, it didn''t work. The investigation''s still going on, and I''m thinking you and me are in some hot water. Hey, don´t try to back out of this now, compadre ― you´re an accessory after the fact, like it or not. Don´t worry, though, loyalty among thieves, and all that. Still, maybe you should start making preparations as well. I wouldn''t want both of us to go down just because I screwed up some paperwork. We don''t have to worry just yet, though; my contact will fill me in on how the investigation is going, so if they decide to come for us, we''ll know. Meanwhile, I have another task for you. There is an agent nearby who''s been getting on my nerves lately. I hired a small guerilla unit to enter his personal quarters and rob him blind. They were successful, apart from one thing: When they saw how much the stolen goods were worth, they broke the deal and decided to keep the loot for themselves. Go to the contested guerilla base, kill the treacherous Angels, and retrieve the item for me.'),
(93453,0,5,22194,3,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500003,0,0,'Acquire 3 x Minmatar Republic Narcotic Officer''s Tag (0.3 m3)','Good news! My guy in the Republic''s narcs has just informed me that, due to lack of evidence, the investigation has been closed. We don''t have to worry any longer, character_name. I still feel a grudge against those cops, though. They meddled in affairs they shouldn''t have come near, and I wan''t blood. Go back to the contested guerilla base, find the narcotics officers there, and do your work. Leave none alive. Bring me back five of their tags, and I''ll reward you handsomely.'),
(93454,0,5,17192,30,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Trade',0,0,0,'Trade in 30x Angel Diamond Tag',''),
(93455,0,1,3687,450,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Courier',500004,0,0,'Deliver 450x Electronic Parts (450{{m3','A few words of introduction are probably in order. I''m Mattheu Rochet an investment banker and sometimes independent trader. I made my fortune a while back trading robotics after the great capsuleer influx two years ago. Since then, I''ve been constantly seeking ways to further the cause of the Matari, a proud people with a tragic history for which proper reparations have not been made. I recently decided to make the Ani constellation my stomping grounds. The situation here is an intriguing one: the simmering conflict between the Amatarr and the old Republic is more evident here than in most other places I''ve been to, and there is much good work that can be done. In fact, I have a job for you if you feel like lending a hand. Some associates of mine have set up shop in the Barkrik system''s Joint Harvesting Food Packaging stations. They are going to install some equipment so they can keep tabs on some of the shadier elements in there. I need you to bring them a shipment of electronic parts, which they can use to assemble their covert surveillance gear. Do this quickly and efficiently and i''ll have another job for you.'),
(93456,0,1,9844,180,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Courier',500004,0,0,'Deliver 180x Small Arms (360 m3)','According to my sources, there are some interesting times ahead in the Nakugard system. A group of unscrupulous individuals is planning to illegally move in Matari slaves under the guise of contract workers. Some of my contacts in Nakugard are working towards fixing this problem their own way but I want my people standing by in case worst comes to worst. I have a shipment of small arms comming into the Sisters of EVE Bureau in Lanngisi. The Sisters themself have nothing to do with it of course, but they trust me enough to look the other way in this case. I need the weapons delivered to the Krusal Tribe bureau at Nakugard V, where my people will pick them up and put them to good use, if need be, will you do this for me.'),
(93457,0,1,19399,650,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Courier',500004,0,0,'Deliver 650x Confiscated Vitoc (325 m3)','I''ve just received word from one of my Nakugard associates that the group I mentioned earlier, the ones who are bringing in the slaves, have stashed away a sizeable portion of Vitoc in one of the Joint Harvesting stations in Barkrik presumably to keep better control of their "contracted labor." Fortunately some of the station personnel in there are on my payroll, so I''ve managed to have the whole load of it "confiscated." If you head over there and bring the Vitoc back to the Sisters of EVE Bureau in Lanngisi, we will be one step closer to resoundingly sending out the message. You don''t try to bring Minmatar slaves into this constellation, right under everybody''s nose.'),
(93458,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500022,16732,5,'Retrieve injured slaves (168 m3)',''),
(93459,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500003,0,0,'',''),
(93460,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500003,0,0,'',''),
(93461,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500003,16727,5,'Destroy freedom fighters',''),
(93462,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Courier',500002,0,0,'Deliver 4x Strange Construction Block (16{{m3','I heard you were interested in working for Thukker Mix, perhaps I can be of assistance on that matter.<br><br>I have a shipment arriving in Hjoramold IX - Moon 14 - Joint Harvesting Refinery in just a few minutes. The person who usually picks up my wares got himself killed last week and I''m looking for a replacement. Let''s see if you can do this quickly and without screwing anything up. Bring the wares back to me after you have picked them up.'),
(93463,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Courier',500002,0,0,'Deliver 25x Strange Construction Block (100{{m3','Remember, Maydie Chieves, nobody is ever to know that you work for me, or for Thukker that is. If the Republic knew about our little operation here, or found out that we deal in... questionable wares, they would most certainly close us down.<br><br>I recieved a small order of "construction blocks" from one of our regular clients. Take this to his quarters at Hjoramold IX - Moon 14 - Joint Harvesting Refinery. The stuff is already paid for, you''re just the delivery boy. Be quick about it, and don''t mess up.'),
(93464,0,3,22204,1,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500011,17138,5,'Acquire 1x Red Hammer''s Personal Effects','Sometimes, the work we do is dirty. It''s not every day that we can just sit back and watch the money roll in. There is a man who goes by the nickname "Red Hammer". I don''t know why or what his real identity is, but that''s irrelevant. About a week ago he placed a large order, stuff worth about 500 million ISK. Based on his reputation, we delivered the items and he told us he would get the money within a day or two... but he never did. We sent a team after him but he managed to slip away, into the depths of the contested Guerilla Base here in Tvink. I want you to go there and kill the bastard. Bring me back something of his as proof of your actions. I will reward you well if you complete this. Declining a mission from a particular agent more than once every 4 hours may result in a loss of standing with that agent, except in the case of special missions that clearly state otherwise in their description.'),
(93465,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'',''),
(93466,0,3,22231,5,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500011,17138,5,'Retrieve 5x Recruitment Center Data Log','Since you did so well in your previous assignment, here''s another mission for you. Each of our scouts conducting reconnaissance missions keeps a digital recording of what transpires during their expedition, stored in a secret compartment within some cargo crates they''re carrying on board. A few of the teams we recently sent out went missing, and we''re hoping the recordings survived and are being kept by whoever attacked them (if that''s in fact what happened). I''d like you to scour the asteroid belts in the Ani constellation in search of these logs. Assuming pirates are at the root of this problem, they might still have the cargo crates on board that hold the recordings, likely quite unknown to them, of course. We''ve lost dozens of ships, but all I ask for you to receover five of their logs. I don''t care where you find them; I just need that evidence brought to me ASAP so I have something to bring back to my superiors when they launch a formal investigation.'),
(93467,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'','Since you''ve been so successful at kill missions, I''ll give you one final assignment that involves exactly that. There is a Thukker Tribe envoy to the Angel Cartel, Vanir Makono, who''s been stirring up the Cartel against us; according to our intelligence, he''s currently located within the Minmatar Military Depot in Inder. I don''t know what his motives are, but they''re probably related to the fact the Thukker Tribe hate our guts. Heh. He''s been a thorn in our side for long enough. The Gist attacks on our assets have increased tenfold since he started spreading those rumors about us. I already sent two of my best pilots out to kill him, but I haven''t heard from them since. I suggest you prepare yourself well before you attempt to infiltrate the Military Depot; it''s completely overrun by Gistum thugs. You''ll probably find Vanir in the headquarters of the deadspace complex. Good luck.'),
(93468,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500002,0,0,'','I am an agent working for the Republic Parliament, and I was sent to Barkrik to investigate rumors of an incredible breach of Minmatar law by the Amarrian corporation Joint Harvesting. This corporation was given rights to this patch of space a few years ago, after some of their key members were the first major Amarrian figures to officially expressed ''regret'' for the crimes committed by the Empire, and so far we have had little trouble with them, other than the strong opposition from hard-liners within the government. But certain rumors are afloat within the inner circles of the Republic, and beyond, that Joint Harvesting actually employs slaves on at least one of their plantations within Barkrik. This rumor has never been proven, and therefore we have not yet taken action. Powerful ''elements'' within the Minmatar government have been pressing for the military to directly intervene and make a political scene out of this mess. This is exactly what Karin Midular does not need. If this rumor turns out to be true, her agenda of peace between the Republic and the Empire will go up in smoke, and all our hard work for the past years will be for nothing. The skirmishes you see today between our forces will be nothing compared to what follows if war is officially declared, and I''m sure the hard liners within the Republic will be pressing hard for that to happen as soon as this gets out. Now you''re probably asking yourself, where do you come into all of this? Well, I was sent to Barkrik on a mission, which unfortunately I can''t complete due to a breakdown in my ship''s engine. I''d like you to complete my objectives for me, as I don''t have much time. I''ll pay you for it, of course. Your first job is to escort the Republic ambassador, Hugo Farin, from Barkrik II - Moon 10 - Joint Harvesting Food Packaging to his office in Orduin V - Moon 7 - Republic Parliament Bureau. He was visiting the Joint Harvesting chief of staff in Barkrik, as well as taking a good look at their plantations here. I was assigned to transport him back home, but obviously I can''t complete my assignment on time.'),
(93469,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500002,0,0,'','Your second job is to bring one of our inspectors, Layna Whizon, to me. She is one of two plantation inspectors that we haven''t retrieved yet after our ambassador''s visit to Barkrik. I warn you, the trip will be a long one, the Amarrians there had the crazy idea of placing the beacon leading into the deadspace pockets very far away from the acceleration gates linking the rooms. I suggest you take a fast ship on this trip, and I''m also afraid your micro-Warpdrive will be inoperable due to the effects of deadspace.'),
(93470,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500002,0,0,'','Now that I''ve gotten Layna''s report, it''s time for her to return to our bureau in Orduin. Please take her there, Pilot. After this is done, please prepare yourself well for the final assignment.'),
(93471,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500002,0,0,'','After we came to Barkrik on our mission for Republic Parliament, we stumbled upon some local rumors of a hidden Amarr slave plantation within the system. We tried investigating it for some time, but to no avail. However, one of our top secret agents, Bono Zakan, went missing during the investigation. The last we heard from him was a transmission from a remote area of Barkrik where he called for help. We couldn''t trace it unfortunately, but I firmly believe he found something he wasn''t supposed to. I don''t know if Bono''s alive or dead, but I want him or his body returned to me for proper burial. I also want you to investigate the claims of this hidden plantation while you''re at it, perhaps the two are linked. To search for the plantation, I suggest you use scan probes within Barkrik. With luck the Amarrians will have placed some sort of cosmic signature near the entrance to lead their own convoys to the area. You could also fly to every moon within the system and hope to stumble upon it''s entrance, if you have no way of acquiring a scan probes. Good luck.'),
(93472,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500011,17138,5,'Kill','I have a job for you, <Pilot>. I became quite concerned today when we lost contact with our commanders in one of the Holy Grounds within Hjoramold, which my people have sworn to protect. I do not have enough pilots on hand to deal with this matter. Investigate the site and report your findings to me. If you find any hostiles there, such as rampaging rogue drones or pirates, then eliminate them at once. Do this and take the blessings of the Kulutor with you.'),
(93473,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Courier',500002,0,0,'Deliver Reports x 1 (0.1 m3)','While I scrounge for information on the Maru here in Hjoramold, I would like you to fetch a top-secret report for me that I ordered from our headquarters in Abudban.'),
(93474,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500002,0,0,'','Apparently Ketta Tommin, a Maru Rebel commander, has been seen visiting Sispur''s Estate in Hjormaold several times in the past few weeks. As far as I can see, there are two clues that point directly to her as far as the Maru attack is concerned: First of all, it''s well known that Ketta organizes most Maru operations in Hjoramold, which would make her the most likely candidate for being the architect of their terrorist attack; secondly, Ketta was spotted on numerous occasions in the pilgrim camp within the Hjormaold holy site shortly before the attack, which strikes me as odd since she is not exactly known for being the religious type. I have a feeling that Ketta''s trip to Sispur has something to do with your encounter with the Maru. Sispur is one of the staunchest opponents of my campaign to modernize the Brutor, and he therefore has a motive for instigating this attack against us. The Maru themselves have no reason to attack us, so I suspect they''ve done so only at Sispur''s bidding. I want you to bring me Sispur''s security camera logs; there''s a good chance they''d prove Sispur''s involvement with Ketta''s agents in Hjoramold. Once I have the digital recordings of his security cameras, I will hopefully be able to prove that Ketta was working for Sispur, and thus cause him considerable embarrassment. Your first problem is getting into Sispur''s estate. You need a keycard to access the acceleration gate leading further into his estate, and this keycard is not easy to acquire. I suggest you pay a visit to Famon Gurch, a sleazy dog of a merchant who resides in the Carnival in Barkrik. He has often been seen in Sispur''s company, and I would be surprised if he didn''t have a keycard into the estate. This is an important mission, which will have significant impact on your faction standings.'),
(93475,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500003,0,0,'','Are you proficient codebreaker? If you are I have need for your talents. The Sisters of EVE are conducting some very secretive research here in Ani and my master sent me out here to find out what it is. I''m already engaged in breaking into the Sister''s mainframe, but it''s proving to be troublesome. My master is getting restless and wants to start see some result. So I figured I could buy myself some time by sending him some interesting tidbits from around the constellation, preferably ones that have something to do with the Sisters. I know that the Angels are actively gathering information themselves, so perhaps they''re sitting on something of value to me and my master. I''ll pay you a bit of money if you collect some tidbits for me. The Angels operate a listening outpost in a complex over in Traun. Head over there and snoop around. If you have the skills for it, that is.'),
(93476,0,3,3643,300,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Security',500011,17138,5,'Transport 300 x Soil (450.0 m³) to 0.5 Tromkurt''s Vagabond in Tvink.','Interested in getting into the drug business, eh? Well, I''ll tell you, it isn''t as easy as people think. You''ve got to start at the bottom and work your way up. Perhaps if you complete a few tasks for me, I will reward you with something that''s worth your trouble. We''re setting up a new plantation of ... well, you don''t need to know what. All you need to know is that for the plants to grow well, we need many components, and one of them is soil. Makes sense, huh? Get me 300 units of soil and deliver them here, and then I''ll give you your next mission.'),
(93477,0,3,22219,5,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Security',500011,17138,5,'Transport 5 x Replacement Laboratory Equipment (5.0 m³) from 0.6 Barkrik IV - Moon 4 - Joint Harvesting Food Packaging to 0.5 Tromkurt''s Vagabond in Tvink.','Back already? Alright, here''s your next task. The condition of our laboratories has been deteriorating lately. Some of the equipment is getting old and needs replacing. Go to Barkrik IV - Moon 4 - Joint Harvesting Food Packaging and pick up replacement laboratory equipment. When you have it, bring it back to me immediately.'),
(93478,0,3,22194,4,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Security',500011,17138,5,'Transport 4 x Minmatar Republic Narcotic Officer''s Tag (0.4 m³) to 0.5 Tromkurt''s Vagabond in Tvink.','The number of narcotic officers in the constellation has been on the rise lately. This is bad for business, as people don''t like dealing when there could be somebody watching behind their back. I have a feeling those cops are planning something, so I want you to head over to the contested Guerilla Base and take some of them out. Hopefully, that will throw them off balance. Bring be 5 of their tags so when you come back, I''ll know you won''t be lying.'),
(93479,0,3,22194,8,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Security',500011,17138,5,'Transport 8 x Minmatar Republic Narcotic Officer''s Tag (0.8 m³) to 0.5 Tromkurt''s Vagabond in Tvink.','Bad news, <Character>. One of our most trusted drug carriers got ambushed and killed just a few hours ago. His death matters little, but what is important is that the police managed to confiscate the entire shipment. He was on his way here when the attack occurred and fortunately, our agent managed to erase all travel and destination logs. Those cops ego''s are growing, they think they can walk all over us without having to face the consequences. I think not. Go back to the contested Guerilla Base and return until every single one of them has been hunted down and killed.'),
(93480,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',0,0,0,'',''),
(93481,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',0,0,0,'',''),
(93482,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',0,0,0,'',''),
(93483,0,1,14358,5000,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Courier',500002,0,0,'Deliver 5,000x Zemnar (1,000 m3)','Oh, it''s worth quite a bit, I''m sure you''ll be satisfied with your end of the deal. But although I''m sure you''re itching to get into combat, I''d like to put you to a small test first... to see if you''re really sincere about helping us out. There''s the minor task that needs to be done, which involves ferrying a load of medical supplies to this system. You see, Nakugard has been hit by strange viral infections of late which have devastated a few outlying settlements there and put a scare into the local populace. Not only that but it''s really having a negative effect on our efforts with bringing more Krusual Tribe civilians here, a system with a viral outbreak is not exactly the first place on your list when you''re thinking of relocating your family somewhere. The Vherokior Tribe were kind enough to give us access to their Zemnar supplies on Teonusude VII - Moon 1 - Vherokior Tribe Treasury. Zemnar has proven to be an effective antidote against the latest outbreak, and we desperately need a large supply of the drug to prevent any more deaths and more bad publicity. I would like you to pay a visit to the Vherokior station in Teonusude and pick up the shipment and bring it to me. I''ll see to it that it''s distributed to all the affected settlements in Nakugard.'),
(93484,0,3,22248,1,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500002,17138,5,'Retrieve 1x Ancient Nefantar Sculpture (5{{m3','As your second assignment, I need you to fetch a valuable Nefanter artifact from one of the Nefanter ruins trough Ani. Most people consider the Nefanter ruins a lost cause when it comes to treasure hunting, as they were all looted for decades after the Rebellion, and are now either used as a pirate forces or guarded by local militia intent on saving ''valuable relics of the past'' from looters. I would like to reverse this myth by proving to the people of the Republic that Ani is in fact still full of surprises, including treasures from the past. All I require is some evidence of this to present to the media, in other words our propaganda machine. To be more specific, I''d like some kind of Nefanter relic that will raise eyebrows. They were vey keen on creating portraits and sculptures of their leaders, which were unfortunately mostly destroyed by the freedom fighters during the Rebellion, and I''m certain one of them would interest all sorts of people. The Krusal Tribe are renowned treasure hunters, so finding these nefanter objects here would undoubtedly increase their interest in Ani. Now if you''re completely clueless as to where to start looking, I''ll suggest one promising spot. There are some Nefanter ruins in Barkrik which have been claimed by the Maru Rebels as one of bases. Maru is a criminal organization that is not to be taken lightly, most of it''s members are wanted by the law and can be killed on sight. And other than being prepared for a fight, I suggest you bring someone along that has experience as an archaeologist, you might need someone like that to dig up the artifact for you. Good luck.'),
(93485,0,3,22249,1,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500011,17138,5,'Retrieve 1x Lagaster Malotoff''s Tag','The last mission I have for you is the most difficult. The heavy pirate presence in Ani has a very negative effect on our mission, as I told you before. And the [[Angel Cartel]] are at the heart of it. Their operations in Ani must be stopped, at all costs. As the saying goes, cut the head off the snake and you kill the snake. I''m not sure if this holds true with the Cartel, but it''s worth a try. Their leader within Inder is Lagaster Malotoff, by killing him we hope to paralyze their forces for some time at least, and give the local populace a morale boost. This is the final task I have in store for you, once you have accomplished it my mission in Ani should be complete.'),
(93486,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500002,17138,5,'Acquire 5x Republic Pilots (5{{m3','Someone once told me that the road to eternal damnation is paved with good intentions. Welcome to that road, friend. I know people are already mocking the Republic Fleet for its lack of progress here in Ani, but those people don''t have a clue about what''s really going on here. The Parliament obviously thought it would be enough for us to show up here like we were on some damn military parade and the pirates would fall all over themselves trying to get out of the way. This political blunder has already cost many a good soldier his life. We''re not getting any support from back home and morale is at an all time low after we lost our headquarters. You can see what''s left of them over there. Command decided to launch a retaliation attack against the pirates and most of our forces are currently embroiled in the local complex trying to wrench control of it from the Angel Cartel. But the Cartel and us are not the only players out here and I''m not even sure the Cartel was behind the attack on our headquarters. All the same, most of my time is spent on rebuilding our outpost here and give logistic support to our troops in the contested complex. I''m woefully short of staff, meaning many important tasks are not being done. Such as going through the ruins of our former headquarters and retrieve the bodies of our fallen comrades. But such a trivial job is beneath someone of your caliber. I have something more important to ask of you. One of our squadrons in the contested complex was ambushed recently by particularly mean Angels. The pirates are still hovering around the squadron''s remains, gloating over their victory. I need someone well acquainted in the arts of war to teach them a lesson, and most importantly, to retrieve the bodies of the Republic pilots so they can be properly treated. I think you''re ideally suited for a task such as this, my best men are already engaging the pirates around the system and the soldiers I have here are too green to be of any use. Interested?'),
(93487,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Courier',500002,0,0,'Deliver 20x Body Bags (20{{m3','Thanks to the efforts of you and other good pilots, a lot of families are getting the bodies of their loved ones back. You can well imagine how important that is, not having to sit in anguish over the fate of those you love. But having those bodies sitting in the Redoubt''s freezer isn''t accomplishing this, I need to get these bodies to a Fleet station where they can be properly taken care of. I know it sounds as a menial task, and in many ways it is, but getting the bodies of these soldiers quickly and safely back to their loved ones is critical if we''re to have any public support back home. Take care of this for me and I''m bound to have something more suitable to your talents next time around. Just to make it a little more interesting I''ll throw in a good amount of bonus reward if you can finish this quickly.'),
(93488,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500002,17138,5,'Kill all the deserters and bring back whatever remains (4x Republic Fleet Deserters, 4 m3) you get from the wrecks of their ships.','The loss of our headquarters was a tremendous shock to us. Not only did many good man and women lose their lives there, but it also gave the rest of us a serious fright. The combat efficiency of our troops is abysmal and the worst part of it all is that the desertion rate has climbed dramatically. Only in the last month almost hundred pilots deserted. Most have fled home and they''re are out of our reach and not our concern. But some are still around, having joined the rebels, or worse, become brigands themselves. It is the latter I''m especially keen on tracking down. I need to get out a strong sign that deserters will not be treated kindly. Deserting from the Republic Fleet is treason and is punishable by death. Morale is bad enough as it is and if people start thinking that desertion is the easy way out, our cause is lost. Unfortunately, those that desert, particularly those that go and join the pirates, know this. So they have dug themselves in, waiting for the inevitable repercussion to arrive. That means that those that go after these brigands must have exceptional battle prowess. They will be going up against trained soldiers caught in a corner with nowhere to run. That makes them desperate, and desperate people are always more dangerous. I have marked you as someone capable to handling such a difficult assignment. You will be well rewarded if you choose to hunt these deserters down and bring them back to me. Dead or alive.'),
(93489,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Courier',500002,0,0,'Deliver Republic Repair Kit (1{{m3','Thanks again for a job well done with those deserters. One of the pilots I''ve hired to hunt them down managed to catch one alive. He''s been in interrogation for awhile now. He was stubborn at first, but we''ve been persistent and now he''s squealing like a pig. Most of it is just gibberish, but some of it''s been sensible. And if what he''s telling is true, we''ve got a serious situation on our hands. It seems that many of these desertions are not just some random panic attacks. There''s a Thukker tribe leader, going by the name Norak Pakkul, hiding out in the contested complex here in Traun that actually has the nerve to recruit Republic pilots for his band of gangsters. And with the jittery nerves of our pilots, he''s actually been quite successful. Needless to say, this guy has to be brought down before he damages our cause further. The only problem is that you cannot access the room he''s in without the proper authorization. The Angels keep a tight control on their access cards, so I''ve been at a loss on how to get to this guy. But I''ve been digging around and found out that there is another way. It seems the old Nefantar access cards are still useable. I heard about a guy out by the Sister Camp that had repaired some damaged cards he received and made them operational again. My pilots have brought back all kinds of stuff they''ve picked up in the contested complex and I actually have a good number of these old Nefantar keycards. All I need are the tools to fix one of these keycards. I want to do this quickly before this Pakkul guy discovers we''re on to him and makes himself scarce. So I''m asking you to whisk over into Minmatar space and bring me one of those Fleet repair kits that makes this kind of a job a breeze. Again, I''ll make this interesting for you by giving you a good bonus reward if you hurry. Once this is done, we''re all set to take this Norak Pakkul out of the picture for good.'),
(93490,0,3,22038,1,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500002,17138,5,'Acquire 1x Norak Pakkul''s DNA (0.1{{m3','Ok, we''re all set to take this Norak Pakkal out of business. The card I gave you gives you and your friends entrance to the inner most room of the contested complex. And you''re going to need your friends for this one. You can only enter the room in cruisers, but you should expect some very heavy resistance in there, from what I''ve heard. Nothing that a pilot of your caliber can''t handle, but if my army life has taught me anything it is that the careful survive. Bring me Pakkul''s DNA and I''m authorized to give you a very rare BPC as a reward.'),
(93491,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500002,0,0,'',''),
(93492,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500002,0,0,'',''),
(93493,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500002,0,0,'',''),
(93494,0,1,22206,1,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Courier',500002,0,0,'Deliver 1x Blood Sample (0.1 m3)','They''re hiding something, I''m sure of it! Lately, rumors have been spreading that there is a deadly virus on the loose, and that nobody knows how to cure it. If we don''t do something about this fast, this might grow into being a threat bigger than we can imagine, millions could be killed! I need you to help me get to the bottom of this, I''m sure my superiors know more than I do, but are not revealing any information. This virus has spread to the facilities of <Station>. Luckily, they were able to contain the virus and the infected ones are now being held in quarantine. I want you to go there and pick up an infected blood sample. I''m going to analyze it and see if I can find a cure for this thing.'),
(93495,0,1,22207,4,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Courier',500002,0,0,'Deliver 4x Analyzed Blood Sample (0.4 m3)','That sample you delivered was essential, thank you. I have discovered the identity of this virus. It''s an age-old sickness dubbed the Alobe Virus. Last time it surfaced, dozens of planetary societies became extinct and over 20 billion people were killed. If we don''t do something about this now, history might repeat itself. You must help me spread the word on this, if we contact doctors and scientists around the constellation, then we might be able to raise awareness and help reduce the spreading of the Virus. Take these samples to <Station> and give it to the scientists there. They will get the word out and help us prevent an epidemic. Make haste, <Pilot>. Lives are at stake here.'),
(93496,0,5,3806,3,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Trade',500002,0,0,'Acquire 3x Refugees (0.3{{m3','We seem to have the worst of luck, <Pilot>. Not only do we have the life-threatning virus on our hands, now the Angel Cartel is making trouble as well. The cartel has kidnapped helpless refugees from a nearby camp and is demanding that we pay ransom. If we don''t pay up, they''re threatning to kill the refugees. Our policy has never been to negotiate with terrorists. I want you to go to the contested Guerilla Base in Tvink and retrieve as many refugees as you can. Please hurry, people''s lifes are at stake!'),
(93497,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Courier',500002,0,0,'Deliver 10 Frozen Livers (100{{m3','If that''s the case. I got something I think you''re suited for. People here avoid me like the plague, and I can''t fathom why, I just make my living like the next guy... I got a family to feed, ya know. Anyway, to get straight to business, I deal in body parts. Now don''t get al pale and shocked on me, eh? I am not one of those crazy Blood Raider flesh-eaters, ya know. All I do is acuire body parts of the deceased and sell them to the highest bidder, usually to the medical divisions within some of the major corporations of the Republic. You know, for research or cheap transplants to needy patients. Anyway, i need some frozen livers i recently purchased to be transferred to the Eifyr and Co. research center in Eram. I''ll provide you with a bookmark and everything: all you need to de is drop of the goods in your hangar there and my associates will pick it up.'),
(93498,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500011,17138,5,'Retrieve the corpses of the Gallente tourists from the wreckage of their ship and take care of the ships guarding it, then return to Rozor Mothrus at The Carnival.','I don''t know if you''re up for risking that ship of yours, but if you are then I got just the job for ya. This morning I was contacted by a distraught Gallente traveler. Apparently he came here with a group of colleagues from Quafe Company while on vacation. They decided to pay Barkrik a visit along their route. Yesterday they had planned to visit some ancient ruins near one of the outlying settlements within this system ... bad idea. Fortunately for my Gallente friend, he was sick that day, so he decided to stay behind on the station while his companions went on their "sightseeing" trip. Well, it didn''t end to good for them. The ancient ruins are located inside a deadspace pocket frequented by the Gist. Of course, the local who suggested they visit the ruins didn''t tell them that, and I hazard a guess he was in league with those scoundrels as well. Anyway, to cut the story short, these tourists where massacred by sentry guns as soon as they appeared near the ruins. Now here''s where you come in. The Gallente who contacted me wants his colleagues'' remains to take back with him to their family when he returns home. He was asking some mercenaries to brave the ruins and retrieve the bodies, and I overheard their conversation. I offered to get the job done for a very low price. Of course, any organs left intact after their deaths will mysteriously disappear before I let the Gallente have them, but that''s a detail I left out of our conversation. Ha, ha. You''ll find the wreckage of the craft carrying the Gallente tourists near the ancient ruins. there are a couple Angel sentry guns that will attack you on sight. I suggest ignoring them: if you retaliate it will only cause more Gist to arrive at the scene. The ships guarding the wreckage will have to be taken care of, though. But like most Gist they will probably to arrogant to call for backup, at least until it''s to late. If you feel you''re up for this task, then let me know. I''ll pay well for these corpses.'),
(93499,0,3,21893,1,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500002,17138,5,'Acquire 1x Kutill''s Data Chip (0.1{{m3','There''s just one last thing that I need. I was contacted a few months ago by one of the elders within the Brutor Tribe about a rogue Sebiestor agent operating from The Carnival in Barkrik. Altough I may be Sebiestor myself, I bear no love for those I used to call family. The suspected rogue agent is none other then Dagras Kutil, a filthy wench who deals in drugs and other illegal wares. I''ve spoken to her on numerous occasions, and in one of our conversations I stumbled upon some pretty interesting info. She claims to have discovered a way to hack into the Brutor Tribe''s stations database, giving her enormous power over any Brutor station. Apparently she uses some kind of program that is stored on database chips she keeps hidden in one of her compounds. When I tried to ask her more questions about this program, she became extremely agitated and started accusing me of being a traitor to the Sebiestors. A few weeks later, I was almost killed by a gang of Maru thugs, and I''m sure she was behind it. She has been after my neck ever since, so I''ve has to call in a group of Brutor mercenaries to keep me safe. Without them, I''d probably be dead now. Sine she doesn''t know you yet, <Pilot>. I''m sure you will have an easier time acquiring this data chip than me, If you do, I''ll pay a hefty price for it.'),
(93500,0,1,22140,1,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Courier',500002,0,0,'Deliver 1x Tri-Vitoc (0.5{{m3','Did you bring me that Tri-Vitoc I need? No? You''re not the guy Tarkur sent out to me? Damn! Where is that guy? I''m starting to think he was waylaid by CONCORD on the way. Friggin'' cops! I need that Tri-Vitoc! Man, what am I gonna do now? Hey! Maybe you''re willing to help. Could you scoot over to Eystur for me? My pal Tarkur works in the cargo hangar on a Security Service station there. Lousy job, excellent location. Gets him close to all kinds of good stuff. Got me hooked on that Tri-vitoc a while ago, brilliant stuff, highly recommend it... Oh yeah. Now where was i? Oh, yes, you. Go to Eystur, bring Tri-Vitoc from Tarkur. Bring it to ''''me''''. It sounds so simple a monkey could do it. So, stop this monkey business and get going! Har, har! Sometimes I kill myself... Mm. Vitoc yeah.'),
(93501,0,5,21811,3,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Trade',500002,0,0,'Trade 3x Sniper ID Slice','Good job on the Tri-Vitoc delivery. Ooh, yeah. I feel like a new man. Heck, with the potency of this stuff, I probably am! My DNA''s probably all screwed up. You''re a pilot after my own heart, direct and brutal. So perhaps we can work together, what do you say? If you''re interested in bringing a bit of mayhem to this uptight world, then follow my lead. I''ve been out hunting pirates in this constellation, there sure are a lot of them around here these days. Why do I hunt pirates, an inquiring pilot such as yourself might ask? Because they don''t belong here, that''s why. This is my home sweet home, and these pirates can go play their little bandit plays somewhere else. This is my territory. Are you with me? I now you''re with me - if you weren''t you''d be dead. No, that''s just a little joke I make. Don''t be alarmed. Heh. Man. this is some good Vitoc. Uhm... oh, yeah, so some of the pirates around here, particularly those in the contested complexes, are sporting those new ID slices. I''ve become quite the avid collector of them, and I''m willing to reward you well if you bring me a few. The tag''s I''m looking for are dropped by tough cruiser pirates, so take care. Ah, what am I saying, it''s those pirates that should take care. Yoy''re <pilot> the menace! Har, har, I''m joking again of course. You know I am.'),
(93502,0,3,22146,1,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500002,17138,5,'Kill the Colony ship and the Colony leader. Retrieve the forged logs (1x Forged Waypoint Logs 0.1{{m3','Well done on that tag-collecting business. These Sniper ID slices now hold a place of honor in my collection. The blood spatter on one of them, man, that was pure genius! Makes it so deliciously eerie! I feel like we''re really bonding here, uh... whats your... oh, yeah Schebag Korten. No, wait, that''s me. Ehh, <Pilot>, right? This might be the beginning of something beautiful, I tell you. I have such a good feeling about you I''m even willing to let you in on one of my schemes: A while ago, I came into the possession of some forged documents from the Amarr Empire. I have a bit of skill in forgery myself, so I altered them a bit to make them look like imperial orders instructing the bearer to head to a certain location here in Ani for coloniation purposes. These Armarrians are always looking to expand, so it''s easy to bait a group of wannabe colonists into thinking they have in their hands official permission to settle here. As if the Empire had any say in who settles here and who not? Bah, the fools! Needless to say the location here in Ani is in the middle of nowhere; just some old rogue drone hive long since cleaned out. I''ve already taken out several settlers in the past myself, but with you and me getting on so well, I thought I''d give you e shot at it. It''s nasty business, I can tell you, killing innocent Amarr civilians in cold blood when thy''re only looking for a place to call home. But I know you have the stomach for it. After all, how innocent can they be, with the blood of my ancestors on their hands? Kill them all, and good riddance to them is what I say. Spit in their eye as they die, mother, father, child and all. Show me you got the guts and I''ll reward you with a rare BPC. Oh, one more thing. Bring the forged documents back to me. This little trap is too sweet not to spring a few more times before they get suspicious.'),
(93503,0,3,22162,2,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',0,0,0,'Acquire 2x Runic Tablet (0.2{{m3','Look at that ugly structure over there. They call it the Culture Recess and its solemn decay fits my mood perfectly these days. Once I was a proud member of the Sister''s research efforts. I had my own lab and staff and every day I woke up with joy in my heart for what wonders I would discover. But the Sisters are a bickering lot, don''t let the outer facade of calm and serenity fool you. Behind closed doors you can find fierce rivalry and constant jostling for a higher place in the pecking order. I was adept in playing their games of backstabbing and politics, bur not adept enough. One day I found myself out of a job. I was offered a lowly assistant''s position on an insignificant little project. I refused to take it and have been a renegade sister since. But I still hope to regain my former stature within the Sisterhood. If I''m to have any hope of ousting my rivals I must make a crashing entrance, showcasing something magnificent. So here, in the shadow of this ruined monument of past follies I aim to rebuild my career. I will make a discovery so grand, so momentous, that the Sisters will be forced to accept me back in on my own terms. I''m finding it hard to do this alone. Material things have never interested me, so I haven''t squandered my life savings on something trivial like most. Now I can put my money and my belongings to good use. I''m interested in hiring pilots with the skills and talents to aid me in my task. If you''re interested. I want to hire you for a small job that is too dangerous for a mere scientist such as myself. Over in the Traun system you can find the ruins of an old Nefantar fortress. The Angel Cartel currently holds it and has launched an effort to restore it. Just before I left the Sisters one of our informants within the cartel reported that the repair drones in the old fortress discovered a stash of ancient tablets with strange indecipherable markings on them. The Angels haven''t bothered with the tablets beyond storing those the drones return with in their repair stations. Now here''s the interesting part. A few year ago I was working on a project that compelled me to dig trough the ancient history of the Nefantar tribe, from times long before the Amarrians ever arrived in Minmatar space. While traveling in Hjoramold, the tribe''s ancestral home, I came upon several tablets with runic inscription, filled with very thought provoking information. I can''t go into details here, but it is the key to my work. I suspect that the tablets that the Angels discovered in Traun might be more of these runic tablets. If so then those tablets could give me a breakthrough in my research efforts. I need someone well versed in the art of war to retrieve those tablets in Traun for me. I will reward you well if you''re willing to take this on.'),
(93504,0,1,22163,1,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Courier',0,0,0,'Transport 1x Patrenn''s Stash (300{{m3','My research is going well. My decision to hire independent pilots has paid of really well. But i fear it also has backfired somewhat by putting too much heat on me. The Sisters have become aware of my whereabouts and what I''m trying to achieve. While I doubt it, one of my rivals could decide to dent my efforts by sending some thugs here to rough me up and destroy my work. The physical risk does not concern me all that much, but if I loose my work I have nothing. I always like to be on the safe side, so I''ve made backup copies of my research. I need to get them to a safe place. First, I considered placing them in a depository box in a bank, but me hiring such a box is too easy to track down. Maybe I''m being paranoid, but you never know. So instead I''ve opted to hire a low-key storage room in a remote system to stash my backup copies in. Obviously, I can''t go there myself, I might be followed. but they would never bother with someone such as you, so you''re an ideal candidate for the job. Take my stash to the Ragnarg system and by the time you return I''m sure i will have something more interesting , less paranoid, for you to do.'),
(93505,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter.',0,0,0,'Kill all the pirates in the area and loot there remains for two pieces of Broken Science Equipment (2{{m3','I''m ready to take my research to the next level. but to do so I must get my hands on some decent science instruments. Without a big corp behind me, the manufacturers of these items won''t even speak to me. I''ve been scouring the second hand market, but not found anything of value. My work will soon stall of I don''t get this stuff. I received an interesting tidbit from a former colleague of mine, one of the few still talking to me. it seems one of the secret research labs the Sisters are running in Lanngisi just had a serious accident and was abandoned. I don''t know the extent of the accident, but do know that some lethal substances leaked out. I''m sure the place is already crawling with scavengers, but if we move quickly we might get something good. It''s funny, only a few weeks ago I would be shattered by these news, but now I hardly feel anything. All I care about is how I can exploit this disaster to my own advantage. I guess I just have learnt that to succeed in this harsh world, one must be extra tough. My sheltered life has never exposed me to this world until now, but I feel I''m coping well. Enough about that. If you''re willing to go over to the contaminated research lab and see if you can find any science instruments, I''m sure I can find something suitable to reward you with upon your return. It doesn''t mater if the items are broken, just get me a few and I''m sure I can make something out of them. If the facility itself doesn''t yield anything you might have to take out some of the scavengers there and see if they cough something interesting up. Just make sure to blow up everything you see there to make sure you get all the salvageable items.'),
(93506,0,3,22159,3,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',0,0,0,'Acquire 3x Mysterious Portal Parts (3{{m3','Thanks to you my research is back on track. I feel like I''m getting close to something big. You remember those tablets you got me awhile ago? I''ve managed to get some sense out of them and the information I''ve gleaned points to one place in particular that might hold the key to this whole thing. Unfortunately that place is not exactly accessible. It lies deeper in the same complex that you found the tablets in, in the Traun system. This place I''m talking about is an ancient portal of some sorts. Sadly, it has long since ceased to function. I''m also beginning to suspect that it wasn''t build by the Nefantars themself, but some other, more elusive, civilization. I''m not sure exactly where it lies, but it is an immense structure, so it can;t be all that hard to locate. I need pieces of the damaged portal. If you can get them for me I would be eternally grateful. just to show you how serious I am, I''m offering you a very rare BPC as a reward when you return with a few pieces of the damaged portal. Needless to say you can expect trouble there, so be prepared.'),
(93507,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500020,11076,5,'Fight you way to the Ice Field then return to Sinogur Nitrut in the dream Port','Your first assignment is to conduct a reconnaissance mission near an ice field in Inder. We have reason to believe a Serpentis drug baron has set up shop there, hoarding drugs and other contraband goods in the deadspace surrounding the ice field, safe from our surveillance monitors. We have also been led to believe that this particular Serpentis pirate has been smuggling arms to the Angel Cartel criminal organization, which is a serious enough crime in itself. I want you to examine the area and report your findings back to me. If our information is correct, then I will have no choice but to launch a full scale assault into the ice field and the surrounding asteroid belt to exterminate this Serpentis pest for good. I will await your findings here in the Dream Port. Farewell.'),
(93508,0,1,3810,130,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Courier',500002,0,0,'Transport 130x Marines (260{{m3','Now that you''ve proven yourself I''ll fill you in on my secret assignment here in Ani. I was sent here by the Republic Fleet to prepare for a major assault that they''ve planned against the Angel Cartel strongholds in the constellation. The elimination of the Serpentis in the ice field was solely made to weaken the Cartel''s position, as the Serpentis there were directly supplying them with arms and other equipment. Your second task is to transport a regiment of our finest ground troops to the Sisters of EVE Bureau in Inder from the Brutor stronghold in Ivar. They will play a major role in our assault against the Cartel positions, so I need them here ASAP. I''ll fill you in on your last and most important mission after you''ve completed this simple task.'),
(93509,0,3,22288,1,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500002,17138,5,'Acquire 1x Angel Cartel Scanner Data (0.1{{m3','Now we''re entering the final stages of our preparations for the military offensive. But there is one last mission I''d like to offer you that is critical to our objective. The Military Depot in Inder is currently under Angel Cartel control. Allthough the meager fleet guarding their positions there are no match for a full scale assault by the Republic armada, they have a huge advantage due to the terrain. The acceleration gate leading in to the complex is not fit for large vessels and if we take the longer route of manually flying through the deadspace area we will undoubtedly run into countless of their booby traps, potentially causing us heavy casualties. But there is something that could turn the table in our favor, <Pilot>. Our agents have already infiltrated the pirate forces inside the Military Depot, and have reported a glaring weakness. They use a large scanner tower to detect any incoming ships from light years away, giving them extra time to prepare their defenses for any incoming assault. Ifthis scanner tower is destroyed, they will loose one of their biggest advantages. The scanner tower is located inside the Military Depot complex. Once you have destroyed it, bring me something from the wreckage as proof. I won''t doubt your sincerity, <Pilot>, but I''m afraid my superiors are a little more skeptical and would require some sort of evidence before they launch the strike.'),
(93510,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Courier',500001,0,0,'Deliver Clone SOE Officer (1{{m3',''),
(93511,0,3,22211,2,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500011,17138,5,'Retrieve 2x Angel Cartel Computer Hardware',''),
(93512,0,3,3806,4,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500011,17138,5,'Retrieve 4x Refugees',''),
(93513,0,1,3814,3,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Courier',500001,0,0,'Deliver 3x Reports (0.3 m3)',''),
(93514,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500002,17138,5,'Find and destroy ST58 and bring his AI chip (ST58 Memory Chip 0.1{{m3','Well, it''s rather complicated. But to keep it simple, I''ll give you the short version. A few days ago, I completed my latest project, the ST 50 series. They were supposed to be ultra-intelligent fighter drones, specifically ordered by the Minmatar Fleet to serve in our armed forces. In all of the tests I performed on them, they seemed to be in fine condition, easily dispatching all the previous models in our combat simulation tests. However, shortly after they were released from our lab and sent into action, they went missing. The loss was an enormous blow to Boundless Creation, especially considering all the time, effort, and money we spent creating those things. The sortie that they were on when they went missing was to attack a massive rogue drone hive within Barkrik. They were accompanied by over a dozen human pilots, who also haven''t been seen since. I''m not sure exactly what happened there, but a rumor is spreading that they were overwhelmed and captured by the rogue drone mothership. I can''t imagine such a thing happening, but... Anyway, a few days later we heard of a terrible tragedy in Hjoramold. An entire settlement was destroyed by rampaging rogue drones. I didn''t think much of it at the time, considering rogue drone attacks are pretty frequent in these parts, but later that day I turned on the evening news I heard something that chilled me to the bone. The recent rogue drone attacks were led by none other than one of my own ST drones! I couldn''t believe my ears at first, but it was true. I don''t know how, but the rogue drones have somehow managed to reconfigure the ST''s AI chip and turn it into a rampaging monster! It must be stopped at all costs; its existence is a terrible blow to my career, and the more damage it causes, the more likely I am to lose my job. You must help me! Unfortunately, the rogues seem to have deactivated the tracking devices I had installed into the STs. However, I have managed to triangulate the location of two of them, and the third has already been destroyed by local independent capsuleers. You''ll find ST 58 at the bookmarked location that I''m about to upload into your NeoCom, floating around a deadspace pocket filled with asteroids. Please bring back its memory chip so that I can study it and find out what went wrong.'),
(93515,0,1,22102,1,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Courier',500002,0,0,'Transport 1x ST 59 Memory Chip (0.1{{m3','Model ST 59 has somehow ended up in Evati, many jumps from here. It was destroyed by militia forces in the system, and its remains transferred to the Republic Justice Department station there. I made a deal with them to allow me to access the memory chip to investigate the cause of the malfunction, but I couldn''t find a convoy heading to Hjoramold in time. Could you fetch it for me ASAP? I have to return it in a couple of weeks, so the faster you get it here, the better.'),
(93516,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Trade',500002,0,0,'Acquire ST 60 Memory Chip (0.1{{m3','The last drone memory chip I need you to fetch is ST 60''s. The ''60 is my finest drone of the ST series, a prototype, and certainly a force to be reckoned with. I think you might have to find some friends to help you take it on ― yes, it''s really that tough, if I do say so myself. It''s currently orbiting a rogue drone installation near Hjoramold XII Moon I, located deep within what we call "Glittermore," the xenon gas cloud of Hjoramold XII. It''s a very hostile part of space, but a magnificent sight nonetheless and one frequented by tourists. Good luck finding those drones, <Pilot>.'),
(93517,0,5,22087,1,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500003,0,0,'Acquire 1x Ancient Vherokior Medallion (0.1 m3)','The first artifact I''m looking for is the famous Vherokior Medallion. Since ancient times, the Vherokior tribe has awarded it''s greatest achievers and leaders with medallions, signifying their status within the community. These medallions are rare, and usually they are buried along with the wearer after his death. The medallion worn by the leader of the Vherokior is an exception, as it is given to whoever takes control of the tribe to signify a change of leadership. A long time ago, before the Great Rebellion, the Nefantar claimed the Vherokior Medallion as tribute when they took control of most Minmatar worlds. It was never returned to the Vherokior, and although it was eventually remade after the Minmatar rebellion, the original is worth more than you can imagine. After tracking down this artifact for many years, I finally found out where it is being kept. To my utter dismay I was told it had fallen into the hands of the Cartel, sold to one of their leaders for an obscene amount of ISK from a private dealer. This Gist overlord''s name is Arrak Nutan, and he currently resides in the Legendary Minmatar Stronghold within Hjoramold. Getting to him will be difficult, as the place is a virtual deathtrap. I''ll pay a very handsome amount for this medallion, as long as it''s still fully intact. Not that I expect you to get past the Gist fleet inside ...'),
(93518,0,5,22096,1,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500003,0,0,'Acquire 1x Hraldar''s Sculpture (5 m3)','The next artifact on the list is Hraldar''s sculpture. Hraldar was a Nefantar general which defected to the Minmatar cause during the rebellion. After his death a sculpure was made of him to honor his name. Originally it was placed within the Legendary Minmatar Stronghold, but after it was abandoned the sculpture was moved to the historical museum in Barkrik. A few years ago however, it was stolen by Maru raiders. I have reliable information that the current owner of the sculpture is Bazeri Palen, one of the leaders of the Maru Rebels. He''s an old-time criminal who pretends to be a ''freedom fighter'', like most of those Maru scum. He flies a formidable battleship, and usually has a few of his goons around for protection. Taking him out will be hard, but I''m confident in you, <Pilot>. I don''t know where you will find him, but the last I heard he was orbiting one of the moons of Hjoramold. The Maru are extremely protective of their territory, so he might attack you when you find him. But don''t worry about the legal implications of killing him, he''s a wanted man within the Republic and therefore I doubt they will look harshly upon his murder.'),
(93519,0,5,22099,1,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500003,0,0,'Acquire 1x Telligman''s Stone (180 m3)','Telligman''s stone is an old symbol of Minmatar independence. Crad was the famous Amarrian architect who designed the Nefantar palace in Hjoramold, shortly before the Rebellion took place. When the Minmatar forces tore down the palace during the rebellion, they left a single stone intact which they called ''Telligman''s stone''. It was later moved to the Bastion museum to be shown as one of the symbols of Minmatar victory in Ani over the occupation. Find the Bastion museum and steal the stone. I don''t care how you do it, just bring it to me intact and I will reward you well.'),
(93520,0,1,22100,3,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Courier',500003,0,0,'Transport 3x Namian''s Artifacts (30 m3) from agent to a station in Sasta.','The last task I have for you, <Pilot>, is to transfer my artifacts to Sasta, which is located within Ammatar space. The system is en route to my home world within the Empire, so I''ll pick up the goods there. I''m much more confident in your abilities to smuggle these items out of Minmatar space undetected than my own, and I certainly wouldn''t want to be caught by the Republic authorities with these items in my cargo hold. No telling what they''d do to me, especially considering I''m a citizen of the Amarr Empire.'),
(93521,0,3,22141,9,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500011,17138,5,'Acquire 9x Finger Bone','Come close, child. I am blind and my cerebro-audial sensors are weak. Still, even so I can sense your inner strength and passion. They match my own. That is good. Very good. The Ani constellation is a place in turmoil. I can see it as a frantic swirl in my mind''s eye. This place has become the playground of many great powers, some visible to eye and some not. Lives are being taken and lives are being thrown away. Right and wrong hold little sway here: anger and hate are the driving forces. This flood of emotions pouring into this melting pot make it hard for me to perceive the currents of the future. I need to under take my most potent divinations to pierce this veil of uncertainty and proclaim the great prophecy I feel building within me. I need your help <pilot>. That is your name, correct? <Pilot>, the asteroid belts here, as everywhere, are infested with pirates and murderers, curse all, worthless dogs who prey on fear and passivity. I need you to bring me a few finger bones collected from pirates around the constellation. Yes, finger bones: I need nine for my divination to hold true.'),
(93522,0,1,22142,1,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Courier',500002,0,0,'Deliver 1x Prophecy Virus (0.1 m3)','My incantation is complete and my prophecy freed. Now I need to get it out to the people. But I''m not a popular man in the Republic. The tribal elders see me as a threat to their precious stability. Yet all I do is tell the truth as I see it. As I see it. Lethargy has settled upon our government and the Armarrians are exploiting it to their own advantage. I have seen a dusty road filled with blood-covered slaves. Minmatar slaves. Yes, the Empire dreams of conquering us once again: already they have woven a web of deceit and treachery around our mighty Republic. The elders are being deceived and the public lulled. Only my prophecies can make them realize the peril we are all in. A peril that is all too real and all too close. The Empire is building its strength and its hunger is rising. My words and my works have been banned from Republic space. But my message must be heard or all is lost. So I have to ask another favor from you <Pilot>. I have a friend not far from here who has access to a public network. If I can get the prophecy to him, he can spread it throughout the Republic. Masking my prophecy as a virus is not something i relish, but it must be done. What I need you to do is smuggle the prophecy virus to my friend. I''m much to well known a figure to republic authorities to have a chance of doing this myself.'),
(93523,0,1,22143,10,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Courier',500002,0,0,'Deliver 10x Freed Pet Slaves (10 m3)','My head is still aching from my last divination. I don''t think I will be ready for one for some time now. These old bones of mine are getting tired. I must rest soon. But before I do you must swear to me you''ll take care of an ugly business that came to my attention just now. It seemed an Amarr Holder exiled from the Empire has taken up a residence here in Ani. This particular Holder is notorious for his disgusting depravities. He hold slaves like they were his pets, forcing them to participate in his cruel games. Fortunately, several of these poor slaves managed to escape the evil clutches of their master. They are now in my care, but are in need of more then I am capable of giving them. Please help these unfortunate souls by transporting them over to the Servant Sisters of EVE station in Lanngisi, where they can be properly cared for. Meanwhile, I will have my disciples locate this crazed Holder so he can be dealt with before he hurts anyone else.'),
(93524,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500011,17138,5,'Retrieve Sadry Damoklet''s Head','How good of you to visit me again, <Pilot>. I''ve been awaiting your return for some time now. I managed to track down the depraved Amarr Holder of whom I spoke at our last meeting. He''s in the Traun system, visiting a station controlled by some lackeys from the Angel Cartel. I do not know what his business is there, and really I don''t care. Whatever it is it will die with him. He has fitted out an old Bestower as a pleasure ship, so look for a Bestower docked at an Angel station. You should find it in the contested complex in the Trau system. By the way, I was contacted by the Sisters in Lanngisi just before you arrived and they informed me that one of the slaves you brought them is a distant relative of mine. Even though my concern extends to all Minmatars, this makes the matter personal. As such, I''m offering a rare blueprint copy to be given to you once you take care of this Amarrian quickly and efficiently. Bring me his head when you''re done. then I can go and rest with my mind at peace.'),
(93525,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'',''),
(93526,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500002,0,0,'',''),
(93527,0,1,22315,1,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Courier',500002,0,0,'Deliver 1x Encoded RSS Brief (0.1 m3)','As you may be aware, the Ani constellation is beset by smugglers as well as dealers in all sorts of illicit goods. Most of the merchandise that comes through here goes to the criminal organizations, who''ve had this place in their clutches for far too long. Our plan is to change that, but it''s going to take a while. Every day, literally tons of arms, drugs, and even slaves are smuggled through the Nakugard ingress, whence they are taken to various parts of the constellation to be sold. Space is a big place, and hard to police, but we do what we can as we always have ― and any help from capsuleers such as yourself is much appreciated. Yesterday, I received an encrypted message from one of my deep cover agents. It appears that one Atek Vandano, a notorious fixer loosely affiliated with the Angel Cartel''s Gist division, has been establishing contacts in Ani. We''re not sure what he''s up to, but Command believes this is something that needs to be nipped in the bud if we''re to be able to maintain any semblance of control over this place down the line. But first thing''s first. I need you to take a copy of the brief down to some associates of mine at the Sisters of EVE Bureau in Inder. We need to make sure all our operatives in the region are informed of what''s going on so we can begin formulating a counter-plan if necessary. Report back to me when you''re done and we''ll take it from there.'),
(93528,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500011,17138,5,'Aquire Nanom Basskel''s Ship Logs','Well, we''ve found out what Atek Vandano''s up to, and it''s not pretty. Hold on to your seat ― if you''re anything like me, this is gonna piss you off something awful. The good Mr. Vandano, it seems, is not working for the Gist on this particular occasion. Our agents have uncovered data that indicates he''s helping to bring in slave labor from Amarrian colonies to the Joint Harvesting stations in this system. We think they might be here as part of the Insorum scare; our information shows that the influx of slaves to Amarrian facilities within Republic space has increased manifold in the past weeks. The holders are protecting their "investments" by bringing them to our turf under the guise of contract laborers. Vandano thinks he can do this right under our noses. We''re not going to let him. Obviously, to avoid an incident with the Amarrian Ministry of Foreign Affairs, we''ll have to go about this in some fairly unconventional ways, and we''ll have to use operatives not officially affiliated with us. You know where I''m going with this, right? Vandano has an associate, a lady by the name of Nanom Basskel. We have reason to believe she''s one of the major architects behind this plan, and according to our intelligence she''s in possession of documents detailing where they''re keeping the slaves before final transport to the Joint Harvesting plants in system. She can usually be found at the contested military depot in Inder. Go out there, "remove" Miss Basskel, and bring me these documents.'),
(93529,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500011,17138,5,'Destroy the Slave Containment Facility and the return back to you agent','Thanks in no small part to the documents you brought, we now have the location of the temporary facilities in this system where Vandano and his cohorts intend to keep the slaves while their forged documents are being submitted to the Republic. According to our reports, they will then be brought to the Joint Harvesting Plantation in Barkrik. If you head out there now and destroy this outpost, our other team should be in a prime position to intercept the slave convoy when it comes in.'),
(93530,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500001,0,0,'',''),
(93531,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500002,0,0,'',''),
(93532,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500002,0,0,'',''),
(93533,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / ?',500002,0,0,'',''),
(93534,0,1,22764,5,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Distribution',500004,0,0,'Item Drop-off 5 x Minmatar Training Certification Results (5.0 m³) obtained from [[Minmatar Military Training Grounds]]',''),
(93535,0,3,22764,5,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Security',0,0,0,'Bring 5 x Minmatar Training Certification Results (5.0 m³)','This assignment has been created as a mandatory test to ensure all personnel are adequately equipped and ready for the tasks ahead. This is done for your safety, we have no intention of sending you needlessly to your death. The assignment is simple, and should be completed within 1 hour''s time. A few floating containers have been placed in our training grounds in Audesder, surrounded by sentry guns and spider drones. All you have to do is retrieve the certificates from the containers. Recover 5 of these sheets to your contact. That is all. - Ison Tiadala'),
(93536,0,5,22764,5,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Bring Item',500002,0,0,'Acquire these goods: 5 x Minmatar Training Certification Results (5.0 m³)<br> Drop-off location: Esordik Mitt''s Rifter in Audesder - The Alliance Barracks (0.3 Low Sec Warning!)','Ahem, I''m really sorry if I insulted you, <Pilot>, but there''s nothing I can do about this. I was given the order to test EVERYONE before we send them out into the fray, and if I would ignore that order I risk being demoted. I hope you understand, Ison is very strict about us following her orders. Now you''ll find the details of your test assignment in the briefing which I''m about to load into your NeoCom. Complete the assignment, which I''m sure you''ll do in no time, and I''ll send you off to Tiadala. And don''t forget to read the advice I''ve uploaded into your journal. Good luck. This assignment has been created as a mandatory test to ensure all personnel are adequately equipped and ready for the tasks ahead. This is done for your safety, we have no intention of sending you needlessly to your death. The assignment is simple, and should be completed within 1 hour''s time. A few floating containers have been placed in our training grounds in Audesder, surrounded by sentry guns and spider drones. All you have to do is retrieve the certificates from the containers. Recover 5 of these sheets to your contact. That is all. - Ison Tiadala This is an important mission, which will have significant impact on your faction standings. Esordik Mitt''s Advice: <br> Do not speak with Warlord Ison unless you have powerful friends at your disposal. Although Ison will begin by sending you into fairly easy encounters, once she''s satisfied with your performance you will be sent straight into fleet battles, which I doubt you will be able to face alone and survive. And as my final word of advice, take care not to enter Ammatar space when criminally flagged by their security forces. It will mean certain death.'),
(93537,0,3,22738,1,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Security',500002,17138,5,'Acquire 1x Ison''s Voucher (1.0 m³)','Bring me a voucher from one of the recruiters nearby and you''re in.'),
(93538,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Security',0,0,0,'Explore the deadspace area which contains the Caldari Broadcasting Unit, and destroy most of the guards. Then report back to Ison.','You''re going to start with something easy, <Pilot>. The Caldari Navy''s propaganda machine has been spreading lies and misinformation amongst our army for some time now. For weeks we''ve been trying to located the source of their broadcasting but it wasn''t until today that we narrowed down the signal to a small area of deadspace in the outer regions of Audesder. I would like you to investigate the area and report your findings to me.'),
(93539,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Security',0,0,0,'Destroy the Caldari Broadcasting Unit','Ok. I want you to fly straight to the broadcasting unit that you discovered in your last mission. Destroy it, and return to me. You will probably have to face a number of guards from the Amarrian alliance, but I''m sure you can handle it. They''ve probably brought in some reinforcements since you''re last attack, so be prepared. Good luck.'),
(93540,0,3,3810,1,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Security',500002,17138,5,'Transport 1x Marines (2.0 m³) from 0.3 Audesder (Low Sec Warning!) to 0.5 Arnola VII - Moon 1 - Trust Partners Trading Post','"It''s time to send you into more dangerous territory, <Pilot>. I really hope you are up to it. This time I want you to smuggle a platoon of our marines into Arnola VII - Moon 1 - Trust Partners Trading Post, which the Ammatar have overtaken to use as a military base close to Kenobanala. The marines we are sending are on a suicide mission to sabotage the production facilities there, which are being used by the Ammatar and Imperial Navies to assemble their ships of war. Return to me immediately once this has been done. I''m counting on you, <Pilos>."'),
(93541,0,3,22752,1,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Security',500008,0,0,'Acquire 1x Khanid Commander (1.0 m³)','Yes, and now is when it starts to get really dangerous. Again I want you to travel to Kenobanala, this time to a Khanid outpost near Fort Kumar. It was erected to accommodate a large force of Kameira soldiers, because they were not considered ‘good enough'' to share living quarters with those of true Amarrian ancestry, nor even the traitorous Ammatar! As you well know, the Kameiras are Minmatar slaves of the Amarr and Khanid who are forced to serve in their military, and who''s purpose is usually to be cannon fodder on the front lines in times of war. I want these Kameiras rescued. But doing that will be tricky. The Khanid complex consists of 3 areas, not including the forward point at the entrance of the deadspace pocket. We have managed to acquire the access codes of the first two acceleration gates, but the 3rd one is unknown to us. Unfortunately the last room of the complex is where the Kameiras living quarters are. I want you to fly to the Khanid outpost and search the rooms we have access to. Try to find something that will help us unlock the 3rd room, and bring it back here. Perhaps someone among the Khanid guards knows the code.'),
(93542,0,3,22754,1,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Security',500002,17138,5,'Acquire 1x Gallente Intelligence Data Recorder (0.1 m³)','While we wait for the interrogation of the Khanid commander to finish, I''d like you to conduct an extremely dangerous mission for me, <Pilot>. The Gallente managed to smuggle a data recorder into Fort Kumar, the base of operations of our enemies in Kenobanala. It''s currently located in one of the army quarters inside their base. All you have to do is infiltrate Fort Kumar and retrieve this data recorder. Return to me once you have it.'),
(93543,0,3,17767,1,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Security',500008,0,0,'Acquire 1 x Kameiras (1.0 m³)','We managed to locate a key that should work on the 3rd acceleration gate inside the Khanid outpost where the Kameiras are being held. The Khanid commander you captured revealed its location to us. It''s more reliable than an access code, since they probably already changed those after your last attack. You''ll find the key in a small container not far from the stargate. It is cloaked and locked but since we know it''s exact location now, your ship scanner should be able to detect it. You''ll have to destroy the container to acquire the key. Assuming that the key still works, you should be able to get into the 3rd area of the complex and save the Kameiras from captivity. I''m sure the Khanid and their allies have sent in reinforcements after your last attack, so be prepared for a difficult fight. You''ll have to bring some friends along if you wish to have any chance of success. Just a word of warning though, the Kameiras are normally extremely loyal to the Empire, being more efficiently brainwashed than normal slaves. They are raised with no education of their origins, and it usually takes some time to convince them that we speak the truth. So you''ll probably have to take them by force. I''ll supply you with some Eforte gas which will paralyze them instantly, allowing your crew to safely transfer them into your cargo hold. Good luck, <Pilot>.'),
(93544,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Security',500001,16796,5,'Destroy the assembly array at the dreadnought manufacturing facility, then return to Ison Tiadala.','It''s time to send you on your last assignment, <Pilot>. I''m sure this will be one of the most difficult encounter you have ever faced. I''m reluctant to send you on such a suicide mission, but you''re the only one qualified for the job that we have. If we sent in our fleet they would be instantly attacked by everyone in Fort Kumar. You on the other hand should be able to get by them unnoticed, if you are cautious enough. What you need to do is destroy the assembly array of the primary Amarr dreadnought manufacturing facility in Kenobanala. It''s pumping out dreadnoughts faster than we imagined, greatly boosting their military strength. If we don''t take it out soon, they will be ready for a full scale assault into Audesder, and that will spell disaster for our campaign. I just don''t think we''re ready yet to face such a large fleet. And I can''t stress this enough, get help! You won''t be able to do this alone. Good luck! This is an important mission, which will have significant impact on your faction standings.'),
(93545,0,3,19493,1,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500002,17138,5,'Retrieve 1x Arms Cache (2.0 m3)','There are millions of minmatars living in the Joas constellation which are not ethnically Nefantar, and many of them are still loyal to the Republic. Even some of the Nefantar living in the area are sympathetic to our cause. Hence there is a strong resistance movement there, which in fact started long before the Rebellion. The strength of the resistance has varied greatly through the years, but the Audesder incident has refueled unrest in the region. And this may be a key factor in our campaign to hold Audesder. What I''d like you to do is transfer a large arms cache to my contact in <System>. This contact of mine is an agent of the Joas resistance, he will see to it that the arms cache gets to the right hands. Try to avoid any contact with the Ammatar or their allies, if they find out what you''re up to then you''ll have one hell of a fight on your hands. Good luck.'),
(93546,0,5,22764,5,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Bring Item',500002,0,0,'Acquire these goods: 5 x Minmatar Training Certification Results (5.0 m³)<br>','Ahem, I''m really sorry if I insulted you, <Pilot>, but there''s nothing I can do about this. I was given the order to test EVERYONE before we send them out into the fray, and if I would ignore that order I risk being demoted. I hope you understand, Ison is very strict about us following her orders. Now you''ll find the details of your test assignment in the briefing which I''m about to load into your NeoCom. Complete the assignment, which I''m sure you''ll do in no time, and I''ll send you off to Tiadala. And don''t forget to read the advice I''ve uploaded into your journal. Good luck. This assignment has been created as a mandatory test to ensure all personnel are adequately equipped and ready for the tasks ahead. This is done for your safety, we have no intention of sending you needlessly to your death. The assignment is simple, and should be completed within 1 hour''s time. A few floating containers have been placed in our training grounds in Audesder, surrounded by sentry guns and spider drones. All you have to do is retrieve the certificates from the containers. Recover 5 of these sheets to your contact. That is all. - Ison Tiadala'),
(93547,0,3,26696,1,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500011,17138,5,'Retrieve 1 x Sidura Meisana (0.1 m³)','I''ve been contacted by one of the mining harvesters working in the vicinity. It''s a private matter, and the poor man is desperate for assistance. His niece, a good-looking but rather quiet woman, lives with him and takes care of their living quarters, but when he got home a few days back, she was gone. After much searching, he discovered that she had been kidnapped by the Angel Cartel, in an operation led by the pirate captain Rubin Sozar. We need you to go find the girl. Her uncle is beside himself with worry and is willing to give up all his savings for her safe retrieval, along with the destruction of the man who put him through all this grief. It is imperative that you get his niece back to us before going after Rubin Sozar, because if anything goes wrong with the rescue we will need him alive to barter for her return. Needless to say, her uncle''s savings will not go to you unless the young woman is back where she belongs, safe and sound.'),
(93548,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Security',500011,17138,5,'Kill Rubin Sozar','I''m very glad you returned the young woman to her proper place. Under normal circumstances that would be the end of it and we''d all live happily ever after, if perhaps a little poorer in her uncle''s case. As it turns out, these are anything but normal circumstances. His niece wasn''t kidnapped by a pirate captain; she eloped with him. Rubin Sozar had promised her that once he had finished some business nearby, they would start a new life together and that she would be treated like a princess. It''s all a lie, of course - these people are no more capable of civilized behavior or affection than some wild animal would be. You have to find that pirate and kill him, or he will simply trick the poor, deluded girl into eloping again. Her uncle assures me that she was treated horribly at the hands of these pirates, so badly, in fact, that he has been forced to lock her up in a section of his quarters and refuse to let anyone speak to her. He says she will remain there until she comes to her senses.'),
(93549,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500011,17138,5,'Take out the smuggler convoy heading to Minmatar space.','You''ve heard, I hope, of the Angel Cartel drug smuggling into Minmatar space. No one will ever know how many lives have been destroyed by this ugly scourge, but while we cannot help those poor souls who have already fallen prey to booster abuse, I''m not going to sit by and let the drugs continue spreading to new victims. I am aware that not everyone around here shares my sentiments. My superiors feel that it''s useless to strike at the dealers and the couriers, that the only way to uproot this problem is to stop it at its source. They say that to do otherwise is a waste of time and money. And they''re right, I''m sure. Of course they''re right. So what I am absolutely not going to do is send out a single rogue pilot and tell him to cut off a supply convoy carrying drugs to Minmatar children. Let''s be crystal clear on that. I am certainly not asking you to help me out on a secret task to rid us of one clandestine shipment, just one, even if nobody would notice its disappearance anyway. We understand one another, I trust.'),
(93550,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500011,17138,5,'Destroy the Angel Cartel booster manufacturing facility.','Welcome back, and congratulations on your task. Not that I had anything to do with it in any way whatsoever, but I''m very happy with your efforts. Which I know nothing about. But good job nonetheless. Whatever you did. While you were away, we received orders that I''ve been praying for. We''ve located the booster manufacturing facility itself, and it''s time to strike at the source. There are some that claim this recent attack by an unnamed pilot on a smuggling convoy was badly timed, and that we now have only a few days before the Cartel decides to move its operation to a new secret location. But then, I don''t recall those same people giving any good reason why we should allow even one parcel of drugs to pass into the hands of our citizens. Nevertheless, fingers have been pointed, and people are quite annoyed at having to rush in. While I don''t have the slightest doubts that I made the right decision in sending you to destroy that convoy - NOT sending you to destroy that convoy, I should say, because of course I had nothing to do with it - it may nonetheless be a wise decision on our part to get there first and destroy that manufacturing facility all by ourselves. It will give us a little added glory, just in case someone decides to get clever about that convoy business.'),
(93551,0,3,15669,10,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Security',500002,17138,5,'Bring 10x Imperial Navy General Insignia II (1 m³)','We have a policy here within the Thukker Tribe that our more prominent members use certain implants to boost their mental ability, since it''s important that our people in key positions perform at a level above what''s considered normal for a human being. It''s a competitive world we live in, and sometimes one has to take risks to achieve one''s goals, even if it means meddling with the brain. You may not be a full-fledged member of Thukker Mix, but you''ve created such a name for yourself that we feel obliged to treat you as one of our own. And considering your record, we feel that our policy pertains to you as well. So I''ve been authorized to give you this implant in exchange for one simple task. Bring me a few insignias and the reward is yours.'),
(93552,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Encounter',500002,17138,5,'Destroy the enemy bunker and return with the informant(2{{m3','Okelle Alash has not yet broken under questioning. However, now that his fleet failed to save him, we have reason to believe that his brother Martokar is going to try it. This is the big break we were hoping for. Martokar is the very man we''ve been after, a brutal criminal who arrived here on the run, having been implicated in kidnappings, slave trade and the murder of CONCORD officers. He hasn''t been here long and has already established himself a big player in the booster smuggling business. We need this man taken down. Martokar is amassing an attack fleet at the moment, and one of the people he tried to recruit has been spotted by our agents in a nearby establishment, ranting about the lousy offer he got. This man is the only chance we''ll get at discovering Martokar''s precise location, so we need you to retrieve him right away. If we screw this up, Martokar may strike at any time while we''re completely unprepared, and good people will die. Obviously, Martokar is going to want to silence this poor fellow before he can reveal anything, so we need to get there first. However, we mustn''t let Martokar think that we''ve got sensitive information on him, since that''ll only make him change his plans and will ruin any advantage we had. We therefore need you to lay waste to the entire location, making it look like our informant perished in the process. Once you''ve destroyed the place and anyone snooping around, bring the guy back to us.'),
(93553,0,3,26167,1,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Security',500011,17138,5,'Bring Item. 1x Okelle''s Encryption-Protected Hard Drive (0.1 m³)','I''m glad to see you. Things are heating up. You may be aware that we''ve been hunting the infamous Thukker warlord named Martokar Alash. He''s proved quite difficult to provoke out of hiding, but we''ve finally been given a good lead. Unfortunately it''s not to him, but to his brother, Okelle Alash. I don''t know if our capturing Okelle will drive Martokar out of hiding, but at the very least it will give him one more thing to worry about. Okelle is a bit of a wild one. He''s reportedly done just about every drug in existence, goes through a girlfriend a month and ends up leaving them at that harem of his, has built up a reputation for being near-suicidal in battle, and all in all lives the definite pirate lifestyle. You should be aware that once you start hunting him, though, he may be a little more cautious. He''s only foolhardy when he''s the one who chooses the battlefield, and this time we''re aiming to catch him with his pants down. He''ll probably manage to escape before you reach his harem, so if you don''t find him there, I want you to bring back something he left that''ll allow us to determine his whereabouts. It''s a fairly well hidden place, so you''ll have to search hard.'),
(93554,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Security',500011,17138,5,'Destroy these targets Location -0.5 DUO-51 (Low Sec Warning!)','We ran Okelle''s hard drive through disinfection and decryption, and we got lucky! Sometimes these things are set to self-destruct after unauthorized access, or they''ve been planted and are full of things that attempt to infect our reader programs the instant we start picking them apart. I''d have thought that our data extraction people would be professional enough not to hook the darn things right up to our systems, but sometimes they get a little overzealous. It took us a month to clear out the last infection we got. At any rate, we now know Okelle''s whereabouts. Remember that he''s undoubtedly aware that we''re after him, and that we intend to use him as a bartering chip to lure his brother out of hiding, so he''s not going to come quietly. Try not to hang around, either, or he''ll just escape. Go in there, kill any backup forces you see, and bring Okelle back to us alive.'),
(93555,0,5,25279,20,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Trade',500002,0,0,'Trade 20x Azure Cytoserocin (200 m3)',''),
(93556,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Security',500011,17138,5,'Eliminate the enemy scout party.','"We''ve run into a little trouble. Word has spread that Okelle Alash is being held captive, and his legion is going absolutely insane. Apparently it''s all right for them to terrorize innocent citizens, but not for us to start hitting back. They''re tearing through the constellation, firing at everything in sight and demanding that Okelle be returned to them in one piece. This, unfortunately, is no longer an option, not unless they have a surgeon on their team who specializes in reattaching fingers. We will have to fight them. Their fleet is disorganized as you''d expect pirates to be, but nonetheless they have a small scouting party that flies ahead and coordinates the primary fleet. You have to take out the scouting party first, so that the primary fleet will be left blinded and confused. Once you''re done with that, report to me and we''ll see if we can use you in taking care of the remnants of Okelle''s fleet."'),
(93557,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Security',500011,17138,5,'Eliminate Overlord Sgnard and his escort.','"Since the scouting party is dead and gone, we''ve got the primary fleet hanging around in space and practically begging for someone to blow them to pieces. Seeing as how you did such a thorough job with their scouts, you were naturally our first choice for taking on their big guns. Once you''re finished with them, Okelle won''t have anyone to help him except his brother. And once our interrogators are done with Okelle, he''ll have given us all the information we need to hunt down Martogar. It''s only a matter of time - that is, unless the primary fleet manages to deploy more scouts and continue their murderous rampage, so you better get on your way to stop them. This is an important mission, which will have significant impact on your faction standings."'),
(93558,0,5,25279,20,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Trade',500002,0,0,'Trade 20x Azure Cytoserocin (200 m3)',''),
(93559,0,5,25279,20,0,'COSMOS Minmatar COSMOS / Trade',500002,0,0,'Trade 20x Azure Cytoserocin (200 m3)',''),
(93560,0,3,12539,20,5,'COSMOS Serpentis COSMOS / Security',500004,11076,5,'Transport 20 x Serpentis Gold Tag (2{{m3','I''m so glad to have a friend of the Federation around here, <Pilot>. Now if you can only eliminate some of those pesky Serpentis fighters in the area, I''ll pay you a lot of ISK. Bring me some of their Gold tags as proof of the deed.'),
(93561,0,3,17216,20,5,'COSMOS Serpentis COSMOS / Security',500004,11076,5,'Transport 20 x Serpentis Diamond Tag (2{{m3','Since your valiant efforts to aid our cause still hasn''t provided us with the results we need, I''d like you to try something a little harder. Some of the Serpentis top-tier battleship captains carry a Diamond embedded tag to display their status within the Serpentis fleet. Bring me these tags as proof of their demise, and I''ll reward you well. That should put a serious dent in their forces.'),
(93562,0,3,17294,1,5,'COSMOS Serpentis COSMOS / Security',500004,11076,5,'Transport 1 x Brynn Jerdola''s Tag (0.1{{m3','Before we leave back to Federation space, I want a certain Serpentis officer killed. Her name is Brynn Jerdola, and she roams the asteroid belts of Fountain, searching for unwary prey to murder in cold blood. She, of all the Serpentis I''ve encountered, has caused my men the most grief. We''ve lost over a dozen miners to her battleship, and the last encounter I had with her I barely escaped with my life. Bring proof of her death and I will reward you greatly. Then at least I can return home with the satisfaction of having caused the death of my greatest enemy.'),
(93563,0,3,3808,1,5,'COSMOS Serpentis COSMOS / Encounter',500006,11076,5,'Head out and break up the DED blockade and retrieve the imprisoned Achove for us and bring him to me. Transport 1 x Prisoners (7.5 m³) to -0.2 A8-XBW. (Low Sec Warning!)','One of our labs a few systems out is under a DED blockade, and all our "material" there is being confiscated. Our guards are being hit with serious firepower even as we speak. Now, most of our mobile research facilities are expendable, but this one is a bit special. Get in there and retrieve the imprisoned chemist, Achove Oullen.'),
(93564,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Serpentis COSMOS / Encounter',500006,11076,5,'If you come across any shipyards or supply facilities, I want them blown to pieces so they can''t fuel and repair their ships, and if anyone stands in your way, burn them. Location: -0.2 A8-XBW (Low Sec Warning!)','While on a routine courier job, one of my pilots recently ran into CTF forces that nearly destroyed his ship. Fortunately, his systems were intact enough that he could track their heading. Our covert ops ships later scanned the area and eventually discovered what is likely a DED communications and supply station. I want you to scope out the location, and if you find any hint of a CTF depot there, I want you to conduct a surgical strike on them before they know what''s happening. If you come across any shipyards or supply facilities, I want them blown to pieces so they can''t fuel and repair their ships, and if anyone stands in your way, hull their ships. Show no mercy.'),
(93565,0,1,0,0,0,'COSMOS Serpentis COSMOS / COSMOS',500022,0,0,'take the chip and bring it to the target location -0.2 A8-XBW (Low Sec Warning!)','For quite some time now, we have been aware of a COSMOS leak within our organization. Federal operatives have always been willing to pay a lot of money for inside information, and it has become abundantly clear to us in recent days that one of our commanders has fallen prey to the temptation of working for both sides. We have no proof as to who the leak might be, but recently some of our people retrieved an encoded computer chip from the wreckage of a scout outpost. The chip contained documents which we think provide clues to the mole''s identity. The chip is slightly damaged, so some parts are unencrypted and other parts missing entirely. I want you to take the chip and bring it to our best code decryptor. He currently resides deep within the A8-XBW system, and you might have to go through some rogue drones to reach him there. Don''t annoy him too much: He values his privacy and doesn''t like being disturbed. There is a data terminal at his docking bay, so dock there and then bring me back the news.'),
(93566,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Serpentis COSMOS / COSMOS',500004,11076,5,'Head out to A8-XBW and Destroy the commander. Location -0.2 A8-XBW (Low Sec Warning!)','Our decryption expert just got back to us with the results. Fortunately, the chip was not too damaged. We have some very trustworthy indications that the snitch is a well known commander within the organization. It came as quite a surprise to me personally that he would start playing for the other team, though in retrospect it does make sense that only someone in his position would have been able to feed the enemy the information they''ve apparently been receiving. The commander is on vacation right now at his residence and doesn''t go on active duty for three days, so now is the time to strike. His residence is in the A8-XBW system. Gear up and fly there as fast as you can. Make the bastard suffer for betraying us ― let''s hope it will be sufficient warning for others not to do the same. Return to me when you have completed your task.'),
(93567,0,5,25275,20,0,'COSMOS Serpentis COSMOS / Trade',500020,0,0,'Trade 20x Celadon Cytoserocin (200 m3)','I came here to investigate the Pegasus constellation, which has been reported to contain massive gas clouds full of material used in booster manufacturing. There have been a lot of rumors about it within Serpentis Inquest, and I thought I''d take a look for myself. Unfortunately, the number of rogue drones and outlaws here has me quite worried, so I dare not go looking for the clouds myself. Hence, I might have a job for you... However, I suggest you refrain from accepting my task unless you have access to a gas cloud harvester module. Without that, you will just be wasting my time. ---- A Brief Guide to Booster Manufacturing Boosters are made by processing chemicals extracted from special gas clouds that can be found in certain deadspace areas in many regions. Some constellations, such as E-8CSQ, 09-4XW, 9HXQ-G, OK-FEM, Pegasus, Assilot, I-3ODK, and 760-9C, however, are rumored to have massive clouds of a scale not seen anywhere else. Finding these clouds requires the ability to conduct long-range scanning, for example via scan probes. Finding them is not always an easy task, though; it sometimes requires quite a bit of exploration. The downside of searching for these clouds is the fact that they are generally located in dangerous pirate-infested space. Few if any of these clouds exist in civilized space, having been depleted long ago by the mega-corporations. Hence, searching for them can be quite risky and is not recommended for any but the most experienced combat pilots. To extract the chemicals from the gas clouds, you need a gas cloud harvester module. You also need to find the correct type of gas cloud. Not all clouds have chemicals that the gas cloud harvester can extract, and therefore you might have to go through some trial and error at first before you get the hang of gas cloud harvesting. Today, most boosters are very much illegal in civilized space, due to the horrible side-effects experienced by users during the Great Booster Craze many decades ago. Manufacturing them must therefore be done in lawless space, outside the spheres of power of the major civilized factions. Similarly, anyone caught smuggling illegal boosters into civilized space can face very steep penalties. Manufacturing boosters can broken into a few phases. Phase 1 involves extracting the material from the gas cloud. Phase 2 requires a refinery structure with the appropriate service module to process the chemicals and create reactions. Phase 3 also requires a structure or station with the equipment for booster manufacturing to process the reaction and create the booster. This simple 3-step process will result in the creation of a fairly common booster. With additional work, the right blueprint, and a combination of several low-quality boosters, one can create higher-quality versions.'),
(93568,0,5,25275,20,0,'COSMOS Serpentis COSMOS / Trade',500020,0,0,'Trade 20x Celadon Cytoserocin (200 m3)','I came here to investigate the Pegasus constellation, which has been reported to contain massive gas clouds full of material used in booster manufacturing. There have been a lot of rumors about it within Serpentis Inquest, and I thought I''d take a look for myself. Unfortunately, the number of rogue drones and outlaws here has me quite worried, so I dare not go looking for the clouds myself. Hence, I might have a job for you... However, I suggest you refrain from accepting my task unless you have access to a gas cloud harvester module. Without that, you will just be wasting my time. ---- A Brief Guide to Booster Manufacturing Boosters are made by processing chemicals extracted from special gas clouds that can be found in certain deadspace areas in many regions. Some constellations, such as E-8CSQ, 09-4XW, 9HXQ-G, OK-FEM, Pegasus, Assilot, I-3ODK, and 760-9C, however, are rumored to have massive clouds of a scale not seen anywhere else. Finding these clouds requires the ability to conduct long-range scanning, for example via scan probes. Finding them is not always an easy task, though; it sometimes requires quite a bit of exploration. The downside of searching for these clouds is the fact that they are generally located in dangerous pirate-infested space. Few if any of these clouds exist in civilized space, having been depleted long ago by the mega-corporations. Hence, searching for them can be quite risky and is not recommended for any but the most experienced combat pilots. To extract the chemicals from the gas clouds, you need a gas cloud harvester module. You also need to find the correct type of gas cloud. Not all clouds have chemicals that the gas cloud harvester can extract, and therefore you might have to go through some trial and error at first before you get the hang of gas cloud harvesting. Today, most boosters are very much illegal in civilized space, due to the horrible side-effects experienced by users during the Great Booster Craze many decades ago. Manufacturing them must therefore be done in lawless space, outside the spheres of power of the major civilized factions. Similarly, anyone caught smuggling illegal boosters into civilized space can face very steep penalties. Manufacturing boosters can broken into a few phases. Phase 1 involves extracting the material from the gas cloud. Phase 2 requires a refinery structure with the appropriate service module to process the chemicals and create reactions. Phase 3 also requires a structure or station with the equipment for booster manufacturing to process the reaction and create the booster. This simple 3-step process will result in the creation of a fairly common booster. With additional work, the right blueprint, and a combination of several low-quality boosters, one can create higher-quality versions.'),
(93569,0,3,15650,1,5,'COSMOS Serpentis COSMOS / Security',500020,11076,5,'Bring 1x Federation Navy Fleet Commander Insignia (0.1 m³)','We have a policy here within the Serpentis that our more prominent members fly a suitable ship according to their status, both to give them an edge during combat and to uphold our image, especially within our borders. We have recently decided to extend this benefit to mercenaries or freelancers employed by us that have shown admirable bravery and skill in the field, or earned the right through countless hours of dedicated service to our corporations. As you undoubtedly already know I have been assigned the task of allocating these ships to their deserved owners. After looking at your record, we decided that you, <Pilot>, are worthy of such an honor. There is just one catch, since you aren''t an official member we need something in exchange for this gift. Cough up 1x Federation Navy Fleet Commander Insignia and the Vindicator Blueprint is yours.'),
(93570,0,3,15647,1,5,'COSMOS Serpentis COSMOS / Security',500020,11076,5,'Transport 1 x Federation Navy Squad Leader Insignia (0.1 m³) to -0.3 Jaquon Jalibar''s Daredevil in MN5N-X. (Low Sec Warning!)','We have a policy here within the Serpentis that our more prominent members fly a suitable ship according to their status, both to give them an edge during combat and to uphold our image, especially within our borders. We have recently decided to extend this benefit to mercenaries or freelancers employed by us that have shown admirable bravery and skill in the field, or earned the right through countless hours of dedicated service to our corporations. As you undoubtedly already know I have been assigned the task of allocating these ships to their deserved owners. After looking at your record, we decided that you, <Character>, are worthy of such an honor. There is just one catch, since you aren''t an official member we need something in exchange for this gift. Cough up 1 x Federation Navy Squad Leader Insignia and the Daredevil Blueprint is yours. Dismissed.'),
(93571,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Serpentis COSMOS / Encounter',500004,11076,5,'Eliminate all enemies.','"We have a big problem, and very little time to deal with it, <Pilot>. Four days ago, two of our squadrons conducted a strike on a small outpost not far from here, not realizing the place was a key tactical and scientific asset belonging to the Federation. In retaliation, Fed Navy HICOM has issued three platoons of combat ships to attack the Fountain region. According to our intel, they will be striking several vital targets of ours in the next twenty-four-hour period. Rumor has it the order came from President Roden himself, so we can expect them to bring big guns and larger numbers. Losing these outposts is something we cannot afford, so we have to move swiftly and meet them head-on before they do their damage. Two teams have already been sent to intercept the first two squads. I want you to handle the third. We believe that they are currently residing at 4-EP12. Get over there and send them back to Yulai."'),
(93572,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Serpentis COSMOS / Encounter',500004,11076,5,'Put an end to this siege. Save our scientist, Kill all enemies.','"Something even bigger has come up, and I''m putting my best pilot, you, on the job. We''ve just learned that the group of Fed ships you took out wasn''t just there for retaliation. It appears that through an informant within our ranks, the Federation have caught wind of our next-gen booster project. The platoons in question were reportedly dispatched for one purpose: to locate and terminate our star scientist, the one who masterminded the project and who currently holds the prototype formulas. The Federate officers you took care of were getting awfully close to him and managed to relay their information back to Fed Central before you took them out, so now we have an even larger Fed group attacking our primary research facilities in 4-EP12. The facility itself is not as important as the scientist himself, and the plans he holds. Should these designs fall into the wrong hands, years of research will be lost and those responsible, myself included, would probably find ourselves swiftly exiled from existence. Load up your guns and put an end to this siege. Save our scientist, and return to me when your task is complete. This is an important mission, which will have significant impact on your faction standings."'),
(93573,0,5,25275,20,0,'COSMOS Serpentis COSMOS / Trade',500020,0,0,'Trade 20x Celadon Cytoserocin (200 m3)','I came here to investigate the Pegasus constellation, which has been reported to contain massive gas clouds full of material used in booster manufacturing. There have been a lot of rumors about it within Serpentis Inquest, and I thought I''d take a look for myself. Unfortunately, the number of rogue drones and outlaws here has me quite worried, so I dare not go looking for the clouds myself. Hence, I might have a job for you... However, I suggest you refrain from accepting my task unless you have access to a gas cloud harvester module. Without that, you will just be wasting my time. ---- A Brief Guide to Booster Manufacturing Boosters are made by processing chemicals extracted from special gas clouds that can be found in certain deadspace areas in many regions. Some constellations, such as E-8CSQ, 09-4XW, 9HXQ-G, OK-FEM, Pegasus, Assilot, I-3ODK, and 760-9C, however, are rumored to have massive clouds of a scale not seen anywhere else. Finding these clouds requires the ability to conduct long-range scanning, for example via scan probes. Finding them is not always an easy task, though; it sometimes requires quite a bit of exploration. The downside of searching for these clouds is the fact that they are generally located in dangerous pirate-infested space. Few if any of these clouds exist in civilized space, having been depleted long ago by the mega-corporations. Hence, searching for them can be quite risky and is not recommended for any but the most experienced combat pilots. To extract the chemicals from the gas clouds, you need a gas cloud harvester module. You also need to find the correct type of gas cloud. Not all clouds have chemicals that the gas cloud harvester can extract, and therefore you might have to go through some trial and error at first before you get the hang of gas cloud harvesting. Today, most boosters are very much illegal in civilized space, due to the horrible side-effects experienced by users during the Great Booster Craze many decades ago. Manufacturing them must therefore be done in lawless space, outside the spheres of power of the major civilized factions. Similarly, anyone caught smuggling illegal boosters into civilized space can face very steep penalties. Manufacturing boosters can broken into a few phases. Phase 1 involves extracting the material from the gas cloud. Phase 2 requires a refinery structure with the appropriate service module to process the chemicals and create reactions. Phase 3 also requires a structure or station with the equipment for booster manufacturing to process the reaction and create the booster. This simple 3-step process will result in the creation of a fairly common booster. With additional work, the right blueprint, and a combination of several low-quality boosters, one can create higher-quality versions.'),
(93574,0,3,1230,300,5,'COSMOS Serpentis COSMOS / Security',500020,11076,5,'Acquire 300 x Veldspar (30{{m3','Welcome to Yakura Harvesting Depot, <Pilot>. I have use for someone like you. You see, I''m not the typical Serpentis member, in fact I never took up the stereotypical practice of piracy. Instead I''ve devoted my life to creating a business which specializes in harvesting gas and rock from the Pegasus constellation. I still work for the Serpentis of course, but I''ve more interest in finding lucrative roid and gas fields than bullying the passersby. Anyway, I have a small job for you. Our scanners have indicated that there is a large quantity of gas clouds in a certain area in YZS5-4. We think the source is pretty close to a certain asteroid belt, which has been claimed by an Astral Mining Inc. expedition. I want you to warp over to this asteroid belt and take a sample from one of the asteroids there, bring it back to me for inspection. We''re hoping to find gas residue on the rock which would indicate the presence of gas clouds nearby.'),
(93575,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Serpentis COSMOS / Encounter',500004,11076,5,'Head out to the survey site and remove the Astral Mining Inc. expedition from the site.','The results of our tests indicate that vast swaths of gas clouds should be located not far from where you retrieved the sample. Since we expect the profits of harvesting these clouds to be extremely profitable, we''re willing to risk a possible confrontation with Astral Mining Inc. But first I want you to take care of their current expedition in the area. I want you to go back to where you found the sample and wait for the expedition to arrive. Destroy as many of their ships as you can, but it''s imperative that you at least take out their commanding officers. That should cripple them long enough for us to move in and set up our defense perimeter before any reinforcements arrive. This is an important mission, which will have significant impact on your faction standings.'),
(93576,0,3,15648,1,5,'COSMOS Serpentis COSMOS / Security',500020,11076,5,'Deliver 1 x Federation Navy Raid Leader Insignia (0.1 m³)','We have a policy here within the Serpentis that our more prominent members fly a suitable ship according to their status, both to give them an edge during combat and to uphold our image, especially within our borders. We have recently decided to extend this benefit to mercenaries or freelancers employed by us that have shown admirable bravery and skill in the field, or earned the right through countless hours of dedicated service to our corporations. As you undoubtedly already know I have been assigned the task of allocating these ships to their deserved owners. After looking at your record, we decided that you, <Character Name>, are worthy of such an honor. There is just one catch, since you aren''t an official member we need something in exchange for this gift. Cough up 1 x Federation Navy Raid Leader Insignia and the Vigilant Blueprint is yours.'),
(93577,0,5,25275,20,0,'COSMOS Serpentis COSMOS / Trade',500020,0,0,'Trade 20x Celadon Cytoserocin (200 m3)','I came here to investigate the Pegasus constellation, which has been reported to contain massive gas clouds full of material used in booster manufacturing. There have been a lot of rumors about it within Serpentis Inquest, and I thought I''d take a look for myself. Unfortunately, the number of rogue drones and outlaws here has me quite worried, so I dare not go looking for the clouds myself. Hence, I might have a job for you... However, I suggest you refrain from accepting my task unless you have access to a gas cloud harvester module. Without that, you will just be wasting my time. ---- A Brief Guide to Booster Manufacturing Boosters are made by processing chemicals extracted from special gas clouds that can be found in certain deadspace areas in many regions. Some constellations, such as E-8CSQ, 09-4XW, 9HXQ-G, OK-FEM, Pegasus, Assilot, I-3ODK, and 760-9C, however, are rumored to have massive clouds of a scale not seen anywhere else. Finding these clouds requires the ability to conduct long-range scanning, for example via scan probes. Finding them is not always an easy task, though; it sometimes requires quite a bit of exploration. The downside of searching for these clouds is the fact that they are generally located in dangerous pirate-infested space. Few if any of these clouds exist in civilized space, having been depleted long ago by the mega-corporations. Hence, searching for them can be quite risky and is not recommended for any but the most experienced combat pilots. To extract the chemicals from the gas clouds, you need a gas cloud harvester module. You also need to find the correct type of gas cloud. Not all clouds have chemicals that the gas cloud harvester can extract, and therefore you might have to go through some trial and error at first before you get the hang of gas cloud harvesting. Today, most boosters are very much illegal in civilized space, due to the horrible side-effects experienced by users during the Great Booster Craze many decades ago. Manufacturing them must therefore be done in lawless space, outside the spheres of power of the major civilized factions. Similarly, anyone caught smuggling illegal boosters into civilized space can face very steep penalties. Manufacturing boosters can broken into a few phases. Phase 1 involves extracting the material from the gas cloud. Phase 2 requires a refinery structure with the appropriate service module to process the chemicals and create reactions. Phase 3 also requires a structure or station with the equipment for booster manufacturing to process the reaction and create the booster. This simple 3-step process will result in the creation of a fairly common booster. With additional work, the right blueprint, and a combination of several low-quality boosters, one can create higher-quality versions.'),
(93578,0,5,25275,20,0,'COSMOS Serpentis COSMOS / Trade',500020,0,0,'Trade 20x Celadon Cytoserocin (200 m3)','I came here to investigate the Pegasus constellation, which has been reported to contain massive gas clouds full of material used in booster manufacturing. There have been a lot of rumors about it within Serpentis Inquest, and I thought I''d take a look for myself. Unfortunately, the number of rogue drones and outlaws here has me quite worried, so I dare not go looking for the clouds myself. Hence, I might have a job for you... However, I suggest you refrain from accepting my task unless you have access to a gas cloud harvester module. Without that, you will just be wasting my time. ---- A Brief Guide to Booster Manufacturing Boosters are made by processing chemicals extracted from special gas clouds that can be found in certain deadspace areas in many regions. Some constellations, such as E-8CSQ, 09-4XW, 9HXQ-G, OK-FEM, Pegasus, Assilot, I-3ODK, and 760-9C, however, are rumored to have massive clouds of a scale not seen anywhere else. Finding these clouds requires the ability to conduct long-range scanning, for example via scan probes. Finding them is not always an easy task, though; it sometimes requires quite a bit of exploration. The downside of searching for these clouds is the fact that they are generally located in dangerous pirate-infested space. Few if any of these clouds exist in civilized space, having been depleted long ago by the mega-corporations. Hence, searching for them can be quite risky and is not recommended for any but the most experienced combat pilots. To extract the chemicals from the gas clouds, you need a gas cloud harvester module. You also need to find the correct type of gas cloud. Not all clouds have chemicals that the gas cloud harvester can extract, and therefore you might have to go through some trial and error at first before you get the hang of gas cloud harvesting. Today, most boosters are very much illegal in civilized space, due to the horrible side-effects experienced by users during the Great Booster Craze many decades ago. Manufacturing them must therefore be done in lawless space, outside the spheres of power of the major civilized factions. Similarly, anyone caught smuggling illegal boosters into civilized space can face very steep penalties. Manufacturing boosters can broken into a few phases. Phase 1 involves extracting the material from the gas cloud. Phase 2 requires a refinery structure with the appropriate service module to process the chemicals and create reactions. Phase 3 also requires a structure or station with the equipment for booster manufacturing to process the reaction and create the booster. This simple 3-step process will result in the creation of a fairly common booster. With additional work, the right blueprint, and a combination of several low-quality boosters, one can create higher-quality versions.'),
(93579,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Serpentis COSMOS / Encounter',500004,11076,5,'Kill rats in A8-XBW (Low sec!)','Precisely one week from today, the Gallente Gaming Commission will have another Legends Trial tournament. The famed contestant, Kuroki Tselmi, will be going up against his long-time rival, Hadni Riiuto. Now, everybody loves to see two fighters face each other when they also have a personal dislike for each other. It makes the entire fight that much more intense. Of course, given the nature of mankind, everybody and their pet has placed some money on the outcome of this fight. Acquaintances of mine also placed money on this fight and we are all hoping that Kuroki Tselmi will win. He usually does, but it probably won''t hurt if we try to give fate a little nudge, here. This is where you come in. I need you to go to Riiuto''s agent. When you meet him, have a word with him about this whole business. He''ll know what to do next, and we''ll all be able to sleep a little easier at night knowing important people won''t lose a lot of money on the match. Now, I have spoken to Riiuto''s agent and he sounds fine with it, but keep your wits about you; don''t go thinking this is going to be a walk in the bio-dome. This needs to go precisely as planned with no screw-ups, otherwise the Betting Commission will be on top of this like a Gallente escort, and they''ll ride this thing for all it''s worth if they find out.. I suggest you bring some friends to make sure the agent doesn''t feel like telling anyone about this. What do you say, do we have a deal?'),
(93580,0,3,0,0,5,'COSMOS Serpentis COSMOS / Encounter',500004,11076,5,'Destroy targets in -0.5 M-PGT0. (Low Sec Warning!)','As it turns out, you did your job a little too well. We seem to have scared Riiuto into seeking protection from the Gaming Commission. Perhaps we should have stuck to bribery. Oh well, we''ll remember that for next time. We still need Tselmi to win this match against Riiuto and one way of accomplishing that is having Riiuto pull out of the match prematurely due to “unforeseen circumstances,” or whatever the Commission will choose to call it when you blow him out of the sky. Because of our previous attempt of nudging fate into the right and profitable direction for my friends, our boy Riiuto is a little more concerned about his safety. He is flying with a heavy escort, but luckily for you I have a plan that cannot fail if you follow the instructions to the letter. It''s not that complicated; just go to the location and hide behind an asteroid. After some time you''ll see Riiuto and his escort meet up with a fuel tanker to refuel their ships. This will be the time to come out of hiding and attack them. If you attack before this moment, Riiuto and his escort will know something is up. I trust you will perform as well as you did before. Don''t let me down now, because I took the liberty of placing a little more money on this, using another friend of mine. If you''re good to me, I might add you to the payroll during the next Legends Trial, or get you better seats if you want to play it safe. You do want to Tselmi to win, right? I mean, you''re a sports fan, right?');

